  ('Seven Gates of Hell — Trout Run Road', 'seven-gates-of-hell-trout-run-road', 'folklore', 40.03967, -76.66169, 'Hellam Township', 'PA', 'York County''s Seven Gates of Hell legend claims that a chain of gates hidden around Hellam Township leads eventually to an entrance to hell, with versions involving either a burned asylum or an eccentric doctor. The alleged asylum never existed and the land connected to the story is private property; this is strictly a **public-road folklore stop, not an invitation to search the woods**.', 'private', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seven\_Gates\_of\_Hell', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Shelburne Road Gravity Hill', 'shelburne-road-gravity-hill-greenfield-ma', 'folklore', 42.589306, -72.63028, 'Greenfield', 'MA', 'Stop on Shelburne Road, facing east just past the Route 2 overpass, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Smith''s Bull Ride Marker', 'smiths-bull-ride-marker', 'folklore', 40.8585, -73.2124, 'Smithtown', 'NY', 'Smithtown folklore claims founder Richard Smith received as much land as he could circle in a single day while riding a bull after helping return a kidnapped daughter to a Montauk leader. Historical deeds make the tale doubtful, but it remains central to the town''s identity and is commemorated by both a marker and the famous Whisper the Bull statue nearby.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/smiths-bull-ride/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Spook Hill', 'spook-hill', 'folklore', 41.58642, -73.89194, 'Wappingers Falls', 'NY', 'Spook Hill Road supposedly earned its name when moonlight reflecting from a rocky hillside created a strange glow that terrified horses traveling the old dirt road. The original landscape has changed considerably, but a 2023 Legends & Lore marker in Spook Hill Park preserves the story.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/spook-hill/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Spook Hill', 'spook-hill-fort-gaines-ga', 'folklore', 31.729083, -85.01056, 'Fort Gaines', 'GA', 'Stop on Spook Hill, north of town, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
