  ('Spook Rock Road', 'spook-rock-road-rockland-county-ny', 'folklore', 41.1626389, -74.0950278, 'Rockland County', 'NY', 'Stop on Spook Rock Road at US 202, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Stepp Cemetery', 'stepp-cemetery', 'folklore', 39.31428, -86.43024, 'Martinsville', 'IN', 'This small cemetery inside Morgan-Monroe State Forest has become the center of a long-running "Lady in Black" legend involving a grieving woman said to linger near an old tree and grave. The haunting is folklore, not established fact, and visitors should treat the active cemetery respectfully and use normal daylight forest access.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hauntedplaces.org/item/stepp-cemetery/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Sterling Gravity Hill', 'sterling-gravity-hill-sterling-ct', 'folklore', 41.7353889, -71.82833, 'Sterling', 'CT', 'Stop on Main Street, just before Snake Meadow Hill Road, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Stiffy Green Mausoleum', 'stiffy-green-mausoleum', 'folklore', 39.476, -87.3489, 'Terre Haute', 'IN', 'Terre Haute legend says a bulldog nicknamed Stiffy Green remained devoted to his owner, florist John Heinl, and later became associated with Heinl''s mausoleum in Highland Lawn Cemetery. Stories claim the dog''s green eyes could be seen glowing near the tomb; the original dog figure is now preserved at the Vigo County History Center, while the mausoleum remains the physical location tied to the legend.', 'open', null, 'https://www.terrehaute.com/things-to-do/experiences/legend-of-stiffy-green/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Sulphur Springs Gravity Hill', 'sulphur-springs-gravity-hill-helena-ar', 'folklore', 34.53583, -90.60583, 'Helena', 'AR', 'Stop on Sulphur Springs Road, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('The Legend of John Maynard Memorial', 'the-legend-of-john-maynard-memorial', 'folklore', 42.880979, -78.888742, 'Buffalo', 'NY', 'A four-foot plaque at the Erie Basin Marina commemorating Theodor Fontane''s poem about a helmsman who steers a burning Lake Erie steamer to shore. Maynard is a fictionalised name over a real rescue. Buffalo and its German sister city Dortmund dedicated it in 1997, with the finished plaque rededicated in 1998.', 'open', null, 'http://www.johnmaynard.net/mem.html', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Legend of the Iron Hoop', 'the-legend-of-the-iron-hoop', 'folklore', 41.145601, -81.339982, 'Kent', 'OH', 'A five-piece outdoor sculpture by Brinsley Tyrrell, professor emeritus at Kent State, made in 1980-81 and inspired by twisted dry wood near his home. After stints elsewhere in Ohio it was installed permanently near Henderson Hall in July 2011.', 'open', null, 'https://www.kent.edu/universityarchitect/sculptures-loan-ohio-arts-council', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Lewis Giant Marker', 'the-lewis-giant-marker', 'folklore', 44.2772, -73.56462, 'Lewis', 'NY', 'Joseph Call was a real nineteenth-century wrestler, logger and millwright whose unusual size and strength inspired stories of superhuman feats. Known as the Lewis Giant or the Paul Bunyan of the East, he is commemorated by a Legends & Lore marker along U.S. Route 9.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/the-lewis-giant/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Weeping Woman of Riverview Cemetery', 'the-weeping-woman-of-riverview-cemetery', 'folklore', 39.27477, -81.55457, 'Parkersburg', 'WV', 'A melancholy female statue in Riverview Cemetery has collected local legends claiming she weeps, changes position or grants wishes to visitors who approach her correctly. The monument is in an operating cemetery open during daytime hours, so this is a folklore stop that needs respectful cemetery behavior rather than nighttime ghost hunting.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-weeping-woman', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thompson Park Vortex', 'thompson-park-vortex', 'folklore', 43.96209, -75.89192, 'Watertown', 'NY', 'Local lore claims there is a strange area within Thompson Park where people become disoriented, lose several minutes of time, or briefly experience another time period. There is no proven supernatural vortex, but the story has become one of Watertown''s best-known modern legends and the public park can be visited normally.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore?category=creepy-locations\&utm_source=chatgpt.com', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thunderbird Drive Gravity Hill', 'thunderbird-drive-gravity-hill-el-paso-tx', 'folklore', 31.84361, -106.5175, 'El Paso', 'TX', 'Stop on Thunderbird Drive, facing south, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Upper Huffman Gravity Hill', 'upper-huffman-gravity-hill-anchorage-ak', 'folklore', 61.10861, -149.73333, 'Anchorage', 'AK', 'Stop on Upper Huffman Road, on the Hillside, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Anchorage'),
  ('Villamain Road Gravity Hill', 'villamain-road-gravity-hill-san-antonio-tx', 'folklore', 29.31722, -98.44333, 'San Antonio', 'TX', 'Stop on the railway crossing at Villamain and Shane Roads, put the car in neutral, and it appears to roll uphill. The slope is an illusion — the surrounding land hides the true horizon, so a gentle descent reads as a climb — which has never once stopped anyone trying it with a bottle of water. A public road, so pull over sensibly and watch for traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_gravity_hills', '2026-09-06T01:38:36.249959+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('W. W. Pool Mausoleum — Richmond Vampire Tomb', 'w-w-pool-mausoleum-richmond-vampire-tomb', 'folklore', 37.53755, -77.45412, 'Richmond', 'VA', 'The ornate mausoleum of bookkeeper W. W. Pool in Hollywood Cemetery became attached to Richmond''s vampire legend after the 1925 Church Hill Tunnel disaster. There is no evidence Pool was a vampire, but the tomb remains the physical focus of the story; visit only during cemetery hours and do not damage or enter the structure.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/hollywood-cemetery', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Witch of Pungo Statue', 'witch-of-pungo-statue', 'folklore', 36.86612, -76.13182, 'Virginia Beach', 'VA', 'This bronze statue honors Grace Sherwood, the Virginia woman convicted of witchcraft after a 1706 ducking trial in what was then Princess Anne County. The monument depicts Sherwood with a raccoon and stands on publicly accessible grounds near Sentara Bayside Hospital, giving the famous Witch of Pungo story a specific modern stop.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/34645', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fear Columbus Haunted House', '13th-floor-haunted-house', 'haunted', 40.08219, -82.948515, 'Columbus', 'OH', 'The former 13th Floor Haunted House in Columbus now operates under local ownership as Fear Columbus Haunted House. It remains a large seasonal horror attraction with elaborate walk-through sets, live actors and additional special-event nights, but the OddWay record should be renamed and pointed to the current brand.', 'limited', null, 'https://fearcolumbus.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.13thfloorcolumbus.com', null, 'way', 637555091, 'America/New_York'),
  ('13th Hour Haunted House', '13th-hour-haunted-house', 'haunted', 40.905432, -74.586599, 'Wharton', 'NJ', '13th Hour Haunted House is a New Jersey horror complex offering multiple themed haunted houses at one location along with escape rooms and other experiences. The major walk-through haunts are seasonal, while some of the site''s non-haunt attractions operate more broadly.', 'limited', null, 'https://13thhour.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://13thhour.com/', null, 'node', 9201376625, 'America/New_York'),
  ('217 Terror Haunted House', '217-terror-haunted-house', 'haunted', 39.485916, -90.372725, 'Roodhouse', 'IL', '217 Terror is a seasonal Illinois haunted attraction that bundles several themed walk-through haunts into one ticket. Live actors, dark sets and different horror environments make it a dedicated October scare stop operating only on select dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://217terror.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://217terror.com/', '+12173704650', 'node', 13947549128, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Abandoned Haunted House Complex', 'abandoned-haunted-house-complex', 'haunted', 42.700534, -87.952816, 'Mount Pleasant', 'WI', 'Abandoned Haunted House Complex is a large seasonal Wisconsin scare destination combining multiple haunted houses, outdoor zones and additional Halloween activities at one property. It operates on select dates from late September into the fall, so access is seasonal and ticketed.', 'limited', null, 'https://abandonedhauntedhouse.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 330459556, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Admiral Fell Inn', 'admiral-fell-inn', 'haunted', 39.2818, -76.5933, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'The Admiral Fell Inn occupies a collection of historic Fell''s Point buildings associated with the neighborhood''s long maritime history. Guests and tour guides have attached numerous ghost stories to its rooms and corridors, while the property continues to operate as a hotel.', 'open', null, 'https://www.visitmaryland.org/listing/hotels-motels/admiral-fell-inn', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Amityville Horror House', 'amityville-horror-house', 'haunted', 40.66661, -73.41481, 'Amityville', 'NY', 'The house associated with the 1974 DeFeo murders later became internationally famous through claims made by the Lutz family and The Amityville Horror books and films. It remains a private residence, so OddWay visitors should view only from public streets, should not enter the property, and should avoid disturbing the occupants.', 'private', null, 'https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3597031', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Apollo Civic Theatre', 'apollo-civic-theatre', 'haunted', 39.45798, -77.96218, 'Martinsburg', 'WV', 'This historic downtown theatre is one of the stops on West Virginia''s Paranormal Trail, with stories of unexplained activity tied to the old performance space. Visitors can see the building during scheduled performances and special haunted events, while paranormal investigations are offered only at selected times or by arrangement.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/west-virginia-paranormal-trail/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Astoria Ghost Tour', 'astoria-ghost-tour', 'haunted', 46.188873, -123.82965, 'Astoria', 'OR', 'Astoria Ghost Tour leads visitors into the city''s darker history and paranormal stories, including underground spaces and locations associated with reported hauntings. Access is through scheduled guided tours, so it is best treated as a book-ahead experience rather than a walk-in attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://astoriaghosttour.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 8895654901, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Asylum 49', 'asylum-49', 'haunted', 40.526335, -112.295012, 'Tooele', 'UT', 'Asylum 49 is a seasonal haunted attraction inside Tooele''s former hospital complex, using medical-horror themes, actors and elaborate sets throughout the building. The property also operates a Museum of Horrors with unusual medical and macabre objects, but the main haunt is available only on scheduled dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://asylum49.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 9631849882, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Auntie Mortem''s Abattoir at Hersheypark Dark Nights', 'auntie-mortem-s-abattoir', 'haunted', 40.293825, -76.654432, 'Derry Township', 'PA', 'Auntie Mortem''s Abattoir is one of the walk-through haunted houses inside Hersheypark''s Dark Nights Halloween event, built around a grotesque butcher-shop and slaughterhouse theme. It is not a standalone Derry Township business and can only be visited when the park''s seasonal Dark Nights event is operating.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hersheypark.com/darknights/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 12995090391, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Black Bass Hotel', 'black-bass-hotel', 'haunted', 40.40677, -75.03756, 'Lumberville', 'PA', 'The Black Bass Hotel has served travelers along the Delaware River for centuries and incorporates stories of unexplained visitors into its documented history and folklore. It remains a functioning hotel and restaurant, so travelers can visit normally without entering private guest spaces.', 'open', null, 'https://www.blackbasshotel.com/history/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Brandy Gap Tunnel No. 2', 'brandy-gap-tunnel-no-2', 'haunted', 39.29296, -80.50363, 'Salem', 'WV', 'Also called the Flinderation Tunnel, this roughly Civil War-era railroad tunnel is now reached from the North Bend Rail Trail and has accumulated stories of ghostly voices and unexplained figures. The tunnel is dark enough that a flashlight is necessary, and reaching it requires trail travel rather than simply pulling off the highway.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/brandy-gap-tunnel-2', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Brighton Asylum', 'brighton-asylum', 'haunted', 40.858032, -74.143347, 'Passaic', 'NJ', 'Brighton Asylum is a large horror-entertainment complex themed around an abandoned institution, with elaborate haunted walkthroughs, escape rooms and special events. Its main haunted-house season is limited to selected dates, although the property hosts other horror experiences at different times of year.', 'limited', null, 'https://brightonasylum.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, '+1-201-716-2827', 'node', 4830873565, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Brownella Cottage', 'brownella-cottage', 'haunted', 40.73298, -82.79176, 'Galion', 'OH', 'Brownella Cottage was built in 1887 and later became the home of Bishop William Montgomery Brown and his wife Ella, with much of the house''s original character and furnishings preserved. The Galion History Center now offers scheduled paranormal investigations and ghost tours in the cottage, including recurring public investigation dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://galion.squarespace.com/paranormal', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Burial Chamber Haunted House', 'burial-chamber-haunted-house', 'haunted', 44.198521, -88.477679, 'Neenah', 'WI', 'Burial Chamber Haunted Complex is a seasonal Neenah-area destination with several different haunted attractions, including high-intensity walkthroughs and darker maze-style experiences. The complex operates on select fall nights and bundles multiple scares into a single visit.', 'limited', null, 'https://burialchamber.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 655102278, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Carnegie Hall', 'carnegie-hall', 'haunted', 37.80212, -80.44822, 'Lewisburg', 'WV', 'Built in 1902, Lewisburg''s Carnegie Hall has accumulated reports of footsteps, whispers, lights and other unexplained activity inside the historic arts venue. It remains an operating performance hall, so visitors should attend a scheduled event or view the exterior rather than treating it as an unrestricted investigation site.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/west-virginia-paranormal-trail/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Casey''s Cottage at Mexico Point', 'caseys-cottage-at-mexico-point', 'haunted', 43.51968, -76.25514, 'Mexico', 'NY', 'Dr. William Casey transformed this former carriage house into an elaborate medieval-style cottage before his death in 1978. Later visitors reported organ music, cries for help, moving furniture and the apparition of a young girl; tours, ghost hunts and investigations are arranged by reservation at Mexico Point State Park.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/caseys-cottage-at-mexico-point-state-park', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ceely Rose House at Malabar Farm', 'ceely-rose-house-at-malabar-farm', 'haunted', 40.65021, -82.39502, 'Monroe Township', 'OH', 'In 1896, Celia "Ceely" Rose poisoned her parents and brother at the family home in Pleasant Valley after becoming fixated on a local man, creating one of Richland County''s most infamous stories. The house survives within Malabar Farm State Park and can be viewed from the park road or walking route, but the interior is not open to the public; local tradition also associates the house and nearby cemetery with Ceely''s ghost.', 'limited', null, 'https://malabarfarm.org/local-history/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Chaos Haunted House', 'chaos-haunted-house', 'haunted', 33.624571, -85.10171, 'Carrollton', 'GA', 'Chaos Haunted House was a seasonal Carrollton-area haunt featuring actors, dark walk-through spaces and outdoor scares. I could not verify a current 2026 operating season, so it should not be presented to travelers as an active attraction without new confirmation.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/981710792', null, null, null, null, 'way', 981710792, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cincinnati Music Hall', 'cincinnati-music-hall', 'haunted', 39.10939, -84.51922, 'Cincinnati', 'OH', 'Cincinnati Music Hall opened in 1878 and remains one of the city''s major performance venues, but its long history has also produced persistent stories of apparitions and unexplained activity. The building can be entered for performances and official tours, including occasional behind-the-scenes experiences that discuss its unusual history.', 'open', null, 'https://www.cincinnatiarts.org/plan-your-visit/visit-music-hall/tours-1', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Collingwood Arts Center', 'collingwood-arts-center', 'haunted', 41.66874, -83.55621, 'Toledo', 'OH', 'The massive building now known as the Collingwood Arts Center began as a convent and school complex associated with the Ursuline order and later became an arts facility. Its old dormitories, theater and corridors have generated enough paranormal reports that the center offers scheduled public and private ghost hunts; tours and investigations require arranging access rather than wandering the building.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.collingwoodartscenter.org/services', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cresson Sanatorium and Prison', 'cresson-sanatorium-and-prison', 'haunted', 40.4563, -78.5642, 'Lilly', 'PA', 'This sprawling mountaintop complex began as a tuberculosis sanatorium, later became a state hospital and then a prison before closing in 2013. Its empty cellblocks, medical buildings and tunnels are now used for scheduled historical tours, photography and paranormal investigations; the property is controlled and should never be entered outside an authorized event.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/cresson-sanatorium-and-prison', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Culbertson Mansion', 'culbertson-mansion', 'haunted', 38.2864, -85.8128, 'New Albany', 'IN', 'Industrialist William Culbertson began building this elaborate Second Empire mansion in 1867, filling it with ornate woodwork, painted ceilings and other high Victorian details. The state historic site is also widely associated with local haunting stories and seasonal paranormal programming, giving visitors a legitimate way to experience the building rather than approaching a private haunted house.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.in.gov/history/state-historical-markers/find-a-marker/culbertson-mansion/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.indianamuseum.org/historic-sites/culbertson-mansion/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Dark Chambers Haunted Attraction', 'dark-chambers-haunted-attraction', 'haunted', 42.555348, -90.61058, 'Hazel Green', 'WI', 'Dark Chambers is a seasonal haunted attraction in Hazel Green offering multiple themed walkthroughs at one location. The current official address is in Hazel Green, not Jamestown, so the city in the existing OddWay record should be corrected.', 'limited', null, 'https://darkchambers.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.darkchambers.com/', '+1-563-239-0367', 'node', 13891305702, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Dave Push Ghost at Haviland-Davison Mill', 'dave-push-ghost-at-haviland-davison-mill', 'haunted', 40.63976, -73.65954, 'East Rockaway', 'NY', 'Local boatman David "Dave Push" Terrell was found dead in the water in 1910, and folklore says his spirit later haunted the Haviland-Davison Mill. The historic mill was moved to Memorial Park in 1963 and is now a museum, with a Legends & Lore marker preserving the ghost story.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/dave-push/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Doctor Morbid''s Haunted House', 'doctor-morbid-s-haunted-house', 'haunted', 43.422529, -73.714346, 'Village of Lake George', 'NY', 'Doctor Morbid''s Haunted House was a long-running Lake George walk-through horror attraction with animated figures and mad-scientist-themed scenes. The attraction has closed, so it should be removed from current OddWay routing rather than treated as an active stop.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/4403648514', null, null, null, null, 'node', 4403648514, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dunkirk Lighthouse', 'dunkirk-lighthouse', 'haunted', 42.4936, -79.3537, 'Dunkirk', 'NY', 'The Dunkirk light station dates to 1827, with the present Victorian keeper''s house and tower preserving maritime and military history along Lake Erie. Reports include footsteps, voices, humming and unexplained touches inside the keeper''s house and tower; the site operates as a museum and also schedules paranormal investigations.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/dunkirk-historical-lighthouse-veterans-park-museum', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Eastern State Penitentiary', 'eastern-state-penitentiary', 'haunted', 39.968336, -75.172675, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Eastern State Penitentiary is a preserved 19th-century prison where visitors can explore cell blocks, prison yards and exhibits about incarceration, including Al Capone''s restored cell. The historic site operates as a museum, while separate Halloween programming adds large-scale haunted attractions during the fall.', 'open', null, 'https://www.easternstate.org/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', 'Su-Sa 10:00-17:00; Jan 01, Dec 23, Dec 24 off', 'https://www.easternstate.org', null, 'way', 320052082, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Erie Canal Museum', 'erie-canal-museum', 'haunted', 43.05065, -76.14872, 'Syracuse', 'NY', 'The museum occupies Syracuse''s 1850 Weighlock Building, the only surviving canal weighlock structure of its kind. Stories associated with the building include apparitions, footsteps and voices, while visitors can normally explore the canal exhibits during regular museum hours.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/erie-canal-museum', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Estate of Evil at Hersheypark Dark Nights', 'estate-of-evil', 'haunted', 40.291262, -76.655507, 'Derry Township', 'PA', 'Estate of Evil is a haunted-house experience inside Hersheypark Dark Nights, taking visitors through a sinister mansion filled with themed rooms and live scares. It is part of the amusement park''s fall event rather than a separate attraction, so access requires the appropriate Hersheypark/Dark Nights admission.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hersheypark.com/darknights/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 12995085649, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Exchange Hotel Civil War Medical Museum', 'exchange-hotel-civil-war-medical-museum', 'haunted', 38.13266, -78.18566, 'Gordonsville', 'VA', 'The Exchange Hotel became a receiving hospital during the Civil War and treated tens of thousands of sick and wounded soldiers before later serving other purposes. Today it operates as a museum with medical and wartime displays, while reported apparitions, voices and unexplained activity have made it a frequent paranormal destination.', 'open', null, 'https://www.theexchangehotelmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fairfield County Infirmary', 'fairfield-county-infirmary', 'haunted', 39.7394, -82.5881, 'Lancaster', 'OH', 'The former Fairfield County Infirmary is a large institutional building associated with generations of poor-farm and county-home residents. It now operates as a paranormal and historical venue offering scheduled tours, photography sessions, public ghost hunts and private investigations rather than everyday walk-in access.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitfairfieldcounty.org/listings/fairfield-county-infirmary/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fairport Harbor Ghost Cat Lighthouse', 'fairport-harbor-ghost-cat-lighthouse', 'haunted', 41.75709, -81.27734, 'Fairport Harbor', 'OH', 'The 1871 Fairport Harbor lighthouse and keeper''s house now operate as a seasonal marine museum, but their strangest resident is said to be a ghostly gray cat seen darting through the former living quarters. During renovation work, a mummified gray cat was found in a crawl space and is now part of the museum''s story; the museum and tower are seasonal.', 'limited', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairport_Harbor_Light', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ferry Plantation House', 'ferry-plantation-house', 'haunted', 36.86194, -76.11806, 'Virginia Beach', 'VA', 'The current Federal-style house dates to about 1830 on a property whose history reaches back to a 17th-century ferry and an earlier courthouse site near the famous Grace Sherwood witch trial. It operates as a historic house museum on limited weekly tour hours and has also become well known locally for reported paranormal activity.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitvirginiabeach.com/listing/ferry-plantation-house/531/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fiddler''s Ghost', 'fiddlers-ghost', 'haunted', 41.87079, -73.8365, 'Staatsburg', 'NY', 'A local fiddler was reportedly robbed and murdered on a bridge here in September 1808. The bridge is gone, but folklore says his music can still be heard on moonlit nights, and a roadside Legends & Lore marker identifies the site.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/fiddlers-ghost/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fort Mifflin', 'fort-mifflin', 'haunted', 39.87545, -75.21289, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Fort Mifflin is a surviving Revolutionary-era fort on the Delaware River and saw intense bombardment during the 1777 defense of Philadelphia. The historic site is open for tours and events and has also developed a major paranormal reputation involving voices, footsteps and apparitions reported in its old barracks and casemates.', 'open', null, 'https://www.fortmifflin.us/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fort Ontario''s Post Ghost', 'fort-ontarios-post-ghost', 'haunted', 43.46454, -76.50697, 'Oswego', 'NY', 'Fort Ontario''s best-known ghost is George Fikes, a British soldier who died there in 1782 and is said to continue guarding the fort with a red lantern. The state historic site preserves the fort and its underground passages, while a Legends & Lore marker specifically records the Post Ghost story.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/the-post-ghost/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fox Sisters Property / Hydesville Memorial Park', 'fox-sisters-property-hydesville-memorial-park', 'haunted', 43.0705, -77.10768, 'Newark', 'NY', 'Maggie and Kate Fox reported mysterious rapping sounds here in 1848 and became central figures in the rise of modern Spiritualism. The original cottage is gone but its foundation remains inside Hydesville Memorial Park; the park itself is open to visitors while access to the enclosure and guided interpretation may require the caretaker.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/the-fox-sisters-propertyhydesville-memorial-park', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Franklin Castle', 'franklin-castle', 'haunted', 41.48611, -81.71611, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'Built for German immigrant Hannes Tiedemann in the early 1880s, Franklin Castle became one of Cleveland''s most persistent haunted-house legends after a series of deaths and later stories of apparitions and hidden rooms. The restored private venue offers scheduled tours, storytelling events and overnight experiences, but it is not a casual walk-in attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://thefranklincastle.com/stay-the-night/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fright Factory Haunted House', 'fright-factory-haunted-house', 'haunted', 47.165644, -122.000647, 'Buckley', 'WA', 'Fright Factory is a seasonal Buckley haunted house set in a secluded property and built around dark indoor scenes, actors and traditional Halloween scares. It operates on select nights in the fall rather than as a year-round destination.', 'limited', null, 'https://frightfactory.net/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.frightfactory.net', null, 'way', 753445391, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Gadsby''s Tavern Museum', 'gadsbys-tavern-museum', 'haunted', 38.80561, -77.04364, 'Alexandria', 'VA', 'These historic tavern buildings hosted travelers, political figures and social events in early Alexandria and are now preserved as a city museum. The site is also bound to the Female Stranger mystery, whose unidentified young woman allegedly died here in 1816 and is said in local lore to still haunt the building.', 'open', null, 'https://www.alexandriava.gov/museums/location/visit-gadsbys-tavern-museum', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghost Tours of Harpers Ferry', 'ghost-tours-of-harpers-ferry', 'haunted', 39.32282, -77.73116, 'Harpers Ferry', 'WV', 'This guided walking tour uses the historic streets around Harpers Ferry to tell local ghost stories, Civil War tales and legends attached to the town''s old buildings. Tours meet near St. Peter''s Roman Catholic Church and run on a scheduled basis, so reservations are recommended.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/west-virginia-paranormal-trail/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghost Tours of Historic Frederick', 'ghost-tours-of-historic-frederick', 'haunted', 39.4162, -77.4104, 'Frederick', 'MD', 'This long-running walking tour uses downtown Frederick''s wars, executions and local tragedies as the background for documented paranormal stories. Tours depart on scheduled evenings from the Market Street area and require a ticket or reservation.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/ghost-tours-of-historic-frederick/24999/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghostly Friendship at Historic Richmond Town', 'ghostly-friendship-at-historic-richmond-town', 'haunted', 40.57138, -74.14743, 'Staten Island', 'NY', 'A Staten Island legend tells of a Hessian drummer named Ernest and a young Van Pelt girl called Pretty who became friends in 1776 and died the same year. Stories claim drumbeats, footsteps and the girl''s apparition can still be encountered around the historic house, and a Legends & Lore marker records the tale at Historic Richmond Town.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/ghostly-friendship/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghosts of Annapolis Tour', 'ghosts-of-annapolis-tour', 'haunted', 38.97756, -76.48768, 'Annapolis', 'MD', 'Annapolis ghost walks take visitors through the old waterfront and colonial core for stories involving historic taverns, pirates, former residents and reported hauntings. The current tour meets around Market Space on scheduled evenings, so this is a ticketed tour rather than an always-open attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitmaryland.org/events/ashes-and-apparitions-annapolis-ghost-tour', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Glenn Dale Hospital', 'glenn-dale-hospital', 'haunted', 38.96286, -76.80991, 'Glenn Dale', 'MD', 'Opened in 1934 as a tuberculosis sanatorium for Washington, D.C., Glenn Dale later served other patients before closing in 1982. Its abandoned hospital buildings have become a major source of local ghost stories, but entering the structures is prohibited; view them only from legal public roads and trails.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/glenn-dale-hospital', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Golden Lamb Ghosts', 'golden-lamb-ghosts', 'haunted', 39.4336, -84.20846, 'Lebanon', 'OH', 'The Golden Lamb has operated in Lebanon since 1803 and is Ohio''s longest continually operating business, with a restaurant, guestrooms and fourth-floor historical displays. Staff and guests have long reported apparitions associated with figures including Sarah Stubbs and politician Clement Vallandigham, who accidentally shot himself at the inn in 1871; the property itself publishes and preserves these ghost stories.', 'open', null, 'https://www.goldenlamb.com/news/does-the-golden-lamb-have-ghostly-uninvited-guests/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Goodleburg Cemetery', 'goodleburg-cemetery', 'haunted', 42.71406, -78.53754, 'Wales', 'NY', 'This inactive town-owned cemetery dates to 1811 and became notorious in the late twentieth century for stories of apparitions and other paranormal activity. Ghost hunters also caused serious vandalism here, so visit only during lawful cemetery access, remain within the grounds and treat the surviving graves with particular care.', 'open', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goodleburg_Cemetery', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Gretchen''s Lock', 'gretchens-lock', 'haunted', 40.7076, -80.59396, 'St. Clair Township', 'OH', 'Gretchen''s Lock is a surviving ruin of the nineteenth-century Sandy and Beaver Canal inside Beaver Creek State Park. Legend says canal engineer E.H. Gill temporarily entombed his young daughter Gretchen in the lock after her death before attempting to return her body to Europe, and visitors still tell stories of her spirit near the stones; reaching the lock requires a park trail hike.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.carnegie.lib.oh.us/gretchen', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Gudgeonville Bridge Ghost Site', 'gudgeonville-bridge-ghost-site', 'haunted', 41.9824, -80.26681, 'Girard Township', 'PA', 'The 1868 Gudgeonville Covered Bridge developed generations of folklore about phantom hoofbeats and ghostly figures around Elk Creek. Arson destroyed the historic covered portion in 2008 and the crossing was rebuilt, so travelers now visit the same folklore location rather than the original covered bridge.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.eriereader.com/article/the-erie-experience-spooky-urban-legends-folktales-and-lore', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Coal Mine at Hersheypark Dark Nights', 'haunted-coal-mine', 'haunted', 40.288598, -76.653548, 'Derry Township', 'PA', 'Haunted Coal Mine is a mine-themed walk-through haunt included in Hersheypark''s Dark Nights event. Visitors encounter underground-style sets, actors and horror scenes during select autumn event nights, not as a year-round standalone coal-mine attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hersheypark.com/darknights/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 12994423868, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Forest At Panic Point', 'haunted-forest-at-panic-point', 'haunted', 36.028109, -78.459502, 'Youngsville', 'NC', 'Panic Point is a large seasonal outdoor haunt built around a wooded property near Youngsville, with a haunted forest and a rotating lineup of trails, mazes and other scare experiences. It operates on select fall nights and tickets are tied to the Halloween season.', 'limited', null, 'https://raleighhauntedhouse.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://raleighhauntedhouse.com', null, 'node', 5390039038, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Halloween House at Land of Make Believe', 'haunted-halloween-house', 'haunted', 40.901362, -74.95719, 'Hope Township', 'NJ', 'The Haunted Halloween House is part of the Land of Make Believe amusement park rather than a standalone New Jersey haunted attraction. Visitors encounter Halloween-themed characters and spooky scenes as one attraction within the larger seasonal family park.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.lomb.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 260858515, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Hollow', 'haunted-hollow', 'haunted', 38.693255, -77.778469, 'Warrenton', 'VA', 'Haunted Hollow at Maple Tree Farm is a seasonal Virginia haunted trail that leads visitors through wooded paths, barns and farm settings populated by live scare actors. It operates on selected fall nights and requires visitors to follow the event''s ticketing and safety rules.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhollowva.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://hauntedhollowva.com', '+1 703-596-5113', 'node', 9597842952, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Hootchie', 'haunted-hootchie', 'haunted', 39.990871, -82.74832, 'Pataskala', 'OH', 'Haunted Hootchie at Dead Acres is an intense, adult-oriented Ohio haunted attraction known for large sets, live performers and deliberately extreme horror imagery. It is a seasonal fall destination and should be treated as limited access outside its posted operating nights.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hauntedhootchie.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 3118461459, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted House at Little Amerricka', 'haunted-house', 'haunted', 43.163323, -89.059251, 'Marshall', 'WI', 'This Haunted House is a dark ride inside Little Amerricka Amusement Park in Marshall, not a standalone Halloween haunt. Visitors board a ride vehicle and pass through old-school spooky scenes and effects during the amusement park''s operating season.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.littleamerricka.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 514606719, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Haunted House of Wax', 'haunted-house-of-wax', 'haunted', 43.08584, -79.063278, 'City of Niagara Falls', 'NY', 'Haunted House of Wax was a Niagara Falls walk-through attraction mixing wax figures with horror scenes and jump scares. It is reported closed, so the record should be removed from active routing rather than presented as a current attraction.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 3964938709, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Knoebels Haunted Mansion', 'haunted-mansion', 'haunted', 40.879976, -76.505058, 'Ralpho Township', 'PA', 'The Haunted Mansion in Ralpho Township is the classic dark ride at Knoebels Amusement Resort, not a standalone haunted house. Riders travel through old-school spooky sets, practical effects and monsters whenever the ride is operating during the park''s season.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.knoebels.com/rides/haunted-mansion/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 3700461518, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bloody Mary''s Haunted Museum & Voodoo Shop', 'haunted-museum-voodoo-pharmacy', 'haunted', 29.961754, -90.067069, 'New Orleans', 'LA', 'Bloody Mary''s Haunted Museum & Voodoo Shop combines New Orleans paranormal history, occult objects, haunted artifacts, dolls and Voodoo-related displays in a small museum and shop. Daytime museum visits are supplemented by scheduled ghost hunts and paranormal investigations after hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.bloodymarystours.com/hauntedmuseum.html', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', 'Mo-Fr 12:00-17:00; Sa-Su 12:00-18:00', null, null, 'node', 6559071386, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Haunted Picnic Table 29', 'haunted-picnic-table-29', 'haunted', 34.137186, -118.306787, 'Los Angeles', 'CA', 'Picnic Table 29 in Griffith Park is the subject of a Los Angeles urban legend involving a couple reportedly killed by a falling tree, with the damaged table and tree becoming an eerie hiking destination. Visitors reach the area on foot through Griffith Park, so this is a strange outdoor legend stop rather than a staffed attraction.', 'open', null, 'https://www.pinintheatlas.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://pinintheatlas.com/travel-blogs/haunted-picnic-table-29-griffith-park-california/', null, 'node', 11608850025, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Haunted Tales', 'haunted-tales', 'haunted', 39.356755, -74.427196, 'Atlantic City', 'NJ', 'Haunted Tales was an Atlantic City horror attraction built around spooky stories, theatrical effects and novelty scares. Current operation could not be reliably confirmed, and older haunt listings suggest the business is no longer a dependable active attraction, so it should remain unpublished until verified.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.hauntworld.com/haunted-house-in-atlantic-city-new-jersey-haunted-tales', null, null, null, null, 'way', 539916275, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Town Hall', 'haunted-town-hall', 'haunted', 40.759125, -83.948266, 'Lafayette', 'OH', 'Haunted Town Hall transforms Lafayette''s old town hall into a multi-level seasonal haunted attraction filled with actors, dark corridors and themed rooms. It operates on select September and October nights rather than year-round.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedtownhall.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://hauntedtownhall.com/', null, 'way', 703782669, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haunted Trails', 'haunted-trails', 'haunted', 41.55012, -88.088541, 'Joliet', 'IL', 'Haunted Trails Joliet is a year-round family entertainment center with a Halloween theme, offering attractions such as go-karts, miniature golf, laser tag, rides and an arcade. It is not a seasonal scare haunt, so travelers should expect an amusement center rather than a paranormal or horror experience.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedtrailsfun.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 495983548, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Haunted Trails', 'haunted-trails-2', 'haunted', 41.749571, -87.799311, 'Burbank', 'IL', 'Haunted Trails Burbank is a year-round Halloween-themed family entertainment center with miniature golf, go-karts, arcade games, rides and other activities. Despite the spooky branding, it is not a haunted house and is specifically designed as family entertainment.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedtrailsburbank.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://hauntedtrailsburbank.com/', null, 'way', 909609404, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Haunted Washoe Club Museum', 'haunted-washoe-club-museum', 'haunted', 39.309319, -119.650222, 'Virginia City', 'NV', 'The Washoe Club is one of Virginia City''s best-known historic saloons and paranormal stops, with a museum and tours exploring the building''s history and reported ghost activity. Visitors can see preserved rooms and displays during regular visits, with more intensive paranormal investigations offered separately.', 'open', null, 'https://thewashoeclubmuseum.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.thewashoeclubmuseum.com/', '+1-775-847-4467', 'node', 4243505100, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Hazel Drew Ghost Marker', 'hazel-drew-ghost-marker', 'haunted', 42.64404, -73.52709, 'Sand Lake', 'NY', 'Twenty-year-old Hazel Drew was found murdered near Teal''s Pond in 1908, and the case was never solved. Stories of her ghost walking the nearby woods survived for generations and later helped inspire the mystery behind Twin Peaks; a Legends & Lore marker now marks the local story without requiring visitors to enter the woods.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/hazel-drew/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Headless Horseman Hayrides and Haunted Houses', 'headless-horseman-hayrides-and-haunted-houses', 'haunted', 41.851567, -73.972109, 'Town of Esopus', 'NY', 'Headless Horseman Hayrides & Haunted Attractions is a large seasonal Halloween destination in the Hudson Valley combining theatrical hayrides with multiple walk-through haunted attractions. The experience runs on select fall nights and is designed as a full evening horror event.', 'limited', null, 'https://headlesshorseman.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.headlesshorseman.com/', '+1-845-339-2666', 'way', 419550850, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hempfield Tunnel', 'hempfield-tunnel', 'haunted', 40.07285, -80.71221, 'Wheeling', 'WV', 'This former railroad tunnel is now part of Wheeling''s trail system and has become associated with reports of voices, figures and other unexplained activity. It is publicly reachable on the trail, but the tunnel is dark and should be approached with a light and normal trail precautions.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/west-virginia-paranormal-trail/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hex House', 'hex-house', 'haunted', 36.081984, -96.047931, 'Tulsa', 'OK', 'Hex House is a Tulsa seasonal haunt with multiple walk-through attractions at one location, loosely drawing its name from the city''s infamous 1940s Hex House story. Visitors come for theatrical horror sets and live scares on select fall nights rather than for access to the original historical Hex House site.', 'limited', null, 'https://hexhouse.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', '"Tickets required. See website for ticketing information."', 'https://hexhouse.com/', null, 'node', 13719806084, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Hirschi''s Haunted Hollow', 'hirschi-s-haunted-hollow', 'haunted', 42.099848, -111.896225, 'Preston', 'ID', 'Hirschi''s Haunted Hollow was a seasonal haunted attraction in the Preston area with Halloween scares and themed outdoor experiences. Idaho High Country now lists the attraction as permanently closed, so it should be removed from active OddWay routing.', 'closed', null, 'https://idahohighcountry.org/item/hirschis-haunted-hollow/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://idahohighcountry.org/event/hirschis-haunted-hollow/', null, 'node', 11279806881, 'America/Boise'),
  ('Historic Avenel', 'historic-avenel', 'haunted', 37.33792, -79.52444, 'Bedford', 'VA', 'Built around 1838, Avenel remained in only two families for nearly 150 years and is now preserved by the Avenel Foundation. The house has long-standing stories of a spectral woman known as the White Lady and other unexplained activity, but visits to the interior must be arranged through scheduled tours or events.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.historicavenel.com/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Bundy House', 'historic-bundy-house', 'haunted', 42.10164, -75.92793, 'Binghamton', 'NY', 'Built in the 1890s for clock manufacturer Harlow Bundy, this Victorian house is now a museum and a recurring stop for paranormal investigators. Visitors have reported footsteps, voices and other unexplained activity, and the museum hosts scheduled ghost tours and investigations in addition to regular public hours.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/the-historic-bundy-house', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Buxton Inn', 'historic-buxton-inn', 'haunted', 40.0674, -82.51625, 'Granville', 'OH', 'The Buxton Inn traces its history to an 1812 tavern and stagecoach stop and has operated in Granville for more than two centuries. Stories of former owners, guests and even a ghostly cat have become part of the inn''s identity; it remains an active hospitality property, so public access is through its current lodging, dining and event operations.', 'open', null, 'https://www.buxtoninn.com/history', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Glen Ferris Inn', 'historic-glen-ferris-inn', 'haunted', 38.15025, -81.21472, 'Glen Ferris', 'WV', 'The riverside Glen Ferris Inn dates to the nineteenth century and has long been associated with stories of a resident spirit commonly called "The Colonel." It remains an operating inn and restaurant, so travelers can visit normally without needing a paranormal event.', 'open', null, 'https://www.glenferrisinn.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Hannah House', 'historic-hannah-house', 'haunted', 39.71167, -86.14305, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'Alexander Moore Hannah built this large brick house in the nineteenth century, and it later became one of Indianapolis''s best-known paranormal locations. The organization preserving the property offers historical access and scheduled paranormal investigations, allowing visitors to experience the site legally instead of relying on abandoned-building lore.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.historichannahhouse.net/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.historichannahhouse.net/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Historic Hotel Bethlehem', 'historic-hotel-bethlehem', 'haunted', 40.62009, -75.38244, 'Bethlehem', 'PA', 'Hotel Bethlehem stands on a historic Main Street site associated with hospitality going back to Bethlehem''s early years. Guests and staff have reported ghost stories throughout the building, including persistent lore surrounding Room 932, while the property remains a fully operating hotel.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hotelbethlehem.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Jail and Sheriff''s Residence', 'historic-jail-and-sheriffs-residence', 'haunted', 40.3018, -83.0689, 'Delaware', 'OH', 'Delaware County''s brick jail and attached sheriff''s residence were completed in 1878 and continued holding prisoners until 1988. The preserved complex now operates as a historic site with scheduled tours and seasonal lights-out ghost hunts, so visitors need to attend an official opening or event rather than entering on their own.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitdelohio.com/events/ghost-hunts-at-the-historic-jail-and-sheriffs-residence/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Prospect Place', 'historic-prospect-place', 'haunted', 40.13466, -82.01325, 'Trinway', 'OH', 'Prospect Place is an 1856 mansion built for abolitionist George W. Adams and is now preserved by a nonprofit historical organization. Its legends and reported paranormal activity are incorporated into scheduled flashlight tours and ghost hunts, while free daylight tours are offered seasonally from March through November.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.historicprospectplace.org/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Savage Mill Ghost Tour', 'historic-savage-mill-ghost-tour', 'haunted', 39.1354, -76.82521, 'Savage', 'MD', 'Historic Savage Mill dates to the 19th-century textile industry, and its organized ghost tour mixes mill history with reports of footsteps, apparitions and a mischievous child spirit. Tours require tickets and run on scheduled dates, so the haunting experience is limited even though the commercial mill complex is otherwise open.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.savagemill.com/ghost-tours/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Historic Zoar Village Ghost Tours', 'historic-zoar-village-ghost-tours', 'haunted', 40.61232, -81.42259, 'Zoar', 'OH', 'Zoar was founded in 1817 by German religious Separatists who created a communal village that survives today as a collection of historic museum buildings. Seasonal lantern ghost tours use stories of unexplained encounters reported by residents, staff and visitors, so the paranormal version of the stop requires a scheduled ticket.', 'limited', null, 'https://historiczoarvillage.com/events/ghost-tours/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hope Furnace Ghost', 'hope-furnace-ghost', 'haunted', 39.33194, -82.34028, 'Brown Township', 'OH', 'Hope Furnace was built in 1853-54 to smelt iron and operated until 1874, leaving a large stone furnace stack beside present-day Lake Hope State Park. Local legend says a night watchman who died at the furnace still appears carrying a lantern during storms, while the surviving furnace and historical marker remain publicly accessible.', 'open', null, 'https://visitvintonohio.com/what-to-do/paranormal-investigation/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hotel Morgan', 'hotel-morgan', 'haunted', 39.62849, -79.95761, 'Morgantown', 'WV', 'The restored Hotel Morgan is an operating downtown hotel with decades of guest stories about unexplained sounds and apparitions. It is included on West Virginia''s Paranormal Trail, but it remains a functioning hotel rather than a dedicated ghost attraction, so visit as a guest, diner or respectful sightseer.', 'open', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/west-virginia-paranormal-trail/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hundred Acres Manor Haunted House', 'hundred-acres-manor-haunted-house', 'haunted', 40.333511, -80.009363, 'Bethel Park', 'PA', 'Hundred Acres Manor is a large Pittsburgh-area seasonal haunt that combines several themed horror environments into one continuous attraction. Live actors, detailed sets, food and midway-style extras make it a destination haunt operating on selected fall nights.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hundredacresmanor.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 699118501, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hyde Hall', 'hyde-hall', 'haunted', 42.79231, -74.87513, 'Cooperstown', 'NY', 'This large early-nineteenth-century mansion overlooking Otsego Lake has more than a century of stories involving footsteps, whispers, phantom knocking and apparitions. Hyde Hall operates seasonal historic tours and scheduled haunted programming, including candlelit ghost tours in the fall.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/hyde-hall', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Imminent Doom Haunted House', 'imminent-doom-haunted-house', 'haunted', 32.433016, -94.844413, 'Kilgore', 'TX', 'Imminent Doom is a large Kilgore seasonal haunted attraction featuring live actors, animatronics and detailed horror sets across an indoor walkthrough. It operates on select dates around Halloween and is intended as a commercial scare experience rather than a historic haunted location.', 'limited', null, 'https://imminentdoomhaunt.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/people/Imminent-Doom-Haunted-House/61573117890491/?_rdr', '+1 9038086496', 'node', 12893715300, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Imogene Remus Ghost at Spring House Gazebo', 'imogene-remus-ghost-at-spring-house-gazebo', 'haunted', 39.11422, -84.49353, 'Cincinnati', 'OH', 'Bootlegger George Remus fatally shot his wife Imogene near Eden Park''s Spring House Gazebo in 1927 while she was on her way to divorce proceedings. Local legend says a woman dressed in black still appears around the gazebo and former reflecting pool, which remain freely accessible within the public park during park hours.', 'open', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_House_Gazebo', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Irene Byron Tuberculosis Sanatorium', 'irene-byron-tuberculosis-sanatorium', 'haunted', 41.196455, -85.170248, 'Huntertown', 'IN', 'The Irene Byron Tuberculosis Sanatorium complex once treated tuberculosis patients outside Fort Wayne, but the surviving historic structures were ultimately demolished. There is no public sanatorium attraction left to visit, so this entry should not be routed as an active destination.', 'closed', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irene_Byron_Tuberculosis_Sanatorium', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 948717037, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Iron Island Museum', 'iron-island-museum', 'haunted', 42.88992, -78.81142, 'Buffalo', 'NY', 'This former church and funeral home is now both a neighborhood history museum and one of Buffalo''s established paranormal destinations. Visitors can take scheduled guided museum tours, while longer overnight investigations are available separately by reservation.', 'open', null, 'https://ironislandmuseum.com/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jean Bonnet Tavern', 'jean-bonnet-tavern', 'haunted', 40.04243, -78.56058, 'Napier Township', 'PA', 'The stone Jean Bonnet Tavern dates to the eighteenth century and served travelers along the historic Forbes Road and Lincoln Highway corridor. The owners openly document generations of ghost stories involving apparitions and unexplained activity, while the building continues to operate as a tavern and inn.', 'open', null, 'https://www.jeanbonnettavern.com/ghosts/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jennie Wade House', 'jennie-wade-house', 'haunted', 39.82332, -77.23079, 'Gettysburg', 'PA', 'Twenty-year-old Jennie Wade was killed inside this house by a stray bullet during the Battle of Gettysburg, making her the battle''s only civilian fatality killed by direct fire. The preserved house operates as a museum and has also accumulated stories of apparitions, voices and other paranormal activity.', 'open', null, 'https://www.gettysburgmuseum.com/jennie-wade-house/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jericho Covered Bridge', 'jericho-covered-bridge', 'haunted', 39.45911, -76.39022, 'Kingsville', 'MD', 'This one-lane covered bridge dates to the 1860s and still carries traffic across Little Gunpowder Falls. Local legends attach hanging apparitions, stalled vehicles and stranger creature stories to the bridge, but it remains an active narrow roadway, so do not stop a vehicle inside it or block traffic.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/jericho-covered-bridge-maryland', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kilmer Mansion', 'kilmer-mansion', 'haunted', 42.09264, -75.92122, 'Binghamton', 'NY', 'Built in 1898 for the family behind the patent-medicine company that produced Swamp Root, Kilmer Mansion has accumulated reports of voices, footsteps, lights switching on and unexplained touches. The restored mansion opens for scheduled tours, events and paranormal programs rather than unrestricted daily access.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/kilmer-mansion', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lafayette Hotel', 'lafayette-hotel', 'haunted', 39.41076, -81.45234, 'Marietta', 'OH', 'The current Lafayette Hotel opened in 1918 after fire destroyed the earlier Bellevue Hotel at the riverfront site. Guests and staff have reported phantom footsteps, unexplained lights and apparitions including a former manager and a woman in dark clothing, while the building continues to operate as a normal hotel and public hospitality business.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ohiomagazine.com/travel/article/haunted-ohio-the-lafayette-hotel', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lake Shawnee Abandoned Amusement Park', 'lake-shawnee-abandoned-amusement-park', 'haunted', 37.40548, -81.14382, 'Rock', 'WV', 'The amusement park opened in 1926 and closed in the 1960s after multiple deaths, leaving behind a Ferris wheel, swings and other decaying structures that have since become the center of extensive paranormal lore. The property is private and visits are only permitted through scheduled tours, events or investigations—do not enter without an appointment.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.wvlakeshawnee.com/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Landmark Theatre', 'landmark-theatre', 'haunted', 43.04731, -76.15261, 'Syracuse', 'NY', 'The ornate theater opened in 1928 and has developed a long-running ghost story involving a woman named Clarissa, said to have fallen to her death and later appeared inside the building wearing white. It remains an active performance venue, with behind-the-scenes tours and paranormal investigations offered on selected dates or by arrangement.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/the-landmark-theatre', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Landoll''s Mohican Castle Ghost Walk', 'landolls-mohican-castle-ghost-walk', 'haunted', 40.57289, -82.23377, 'Loudonville', 'OH', 'Landoll''s Mohican Castle runs guided haunted-history walks that lead visitors through the property, nearby Heyd Cemetery and a replica nineteenth-century cabin. The experience combines documented local history with the area''s ghost stories and is offered only on scheduled dates, so advance booking is required.', 'limited', null, 'https://landollsmohicancastle.com/events/ghost-walk-haunted-history-tours/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lemp Mansion', 'lemp-mansion', 'haunted', 38.593173, -90.215771, 'Saint Louis', 'MO', 'The Lemp Mansion is the historic home of St. Louis''s Lemp brewing family and now operates as a restaurant, inn and event venue. Its tragic family history and long-running ghost stories are explored through special haunted-history events, tours and paranormal investigations.', 'open', null, 'https://www.lempmansion.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 526334314, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Licking County Historic Jail', 'licking-county-historic-jail', 'haunted', 40.0562, -82.40139, 'Newark', 'OH', 'The Licking County Historic Jail opened in 1889 and held prisoners until 1987, preserving its original cells and sheriff''s residence in downtown Newark. Deaths, a notorious 1910 lynching and decades of incarceration helped create its paranormal reputation, and the building now hosts scheduled historical tours, paranormal investigations and the seasonal Jail of Terror attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.newarkjail.com/about.html', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lincoln''s Ghost Train Marker', 'lincolns-ghost-train-marker', 'haunted', 41.78727, -73.94629, 'Hyde Park', 'NY', 'Abraham Lincoln''s funeral train passed through Hyde Park on April 25, 1865. Folklore later developed that a spectral version of the black-draped train returns along the Hudson River tracks on the anniversary of its passage, and a Legends & Lore marker now identifies the location associated with the story.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/ghost-train/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Logan Inn', 'logan-inn', 'haunted', 40.3635, -74.9517, 'New Hope', 'PA', 'The Logan Inn traces its history to 1727 and is one of New Hope''s oldest continuously used buildings. Its long-running ghost lore centers on rooms and hallways where guests have reported apparitions and unexplained activity, while the property remains an active hotel and restaurant.', 'open', null, 'https://www.loganinn.com/press-blogs', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lord Baltimore Hotel', 'lord-baltimore-hotel', 'haunted', 39.2897, -76.61612, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Opened in 1928, the Lord Baltimore is a surviving grand downtown hotel with decades of stories involving a girl in white, unexplained elevator stops and other reported activity. The hotel actively embraces the reputation today with ghost tours, paranormal events and haunted-stay packages.', 'open', null, 'https://www.lordbaltimorehotel.com/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Madison Seminary', 'madison-seminary', 'haunted', 41.79051, -81.04554, 'Madison', 'OH', 'Built in 1847 as a school, Madison Seminary later served as a home for Civil War veterans and their families before passing through several institutional uses. The restored building is now best known as a paranormal investigation venue, with tours and overnight ghost hunts offered by reservation rather than normal walk-in access.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.madisonseminary.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Majestic Theatre', 'majestic-theatre', 'haunted', 39.33489, -82.98105, 'Chillicothe', 'OH', 'Chillicothe''s Majestic Theatre traces its history to the nineteenth century and is tied in local lore to the devastating 1918 influenza epidemic at nearby Camp Sherman. Stories claim the theater was used to hold bodies during the crisis and now hosts apparitions and voices; it remains an active theater, with access through performances, scheduled tours and occasional ghost hunts.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.majesticchillicothe.net/wp-content/uploads/Haunted-Majestic-Ghost-Hunt.pdf', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Major Graham Mansion', 'major-graham-mansion', 'haunted', 36.91532, -80.87226, 'Max Meadows', 'VA', 'This 19th-century Wythe County mansion has accumulated stories of apparitions, voices and other reported paranormal activity tied to generations of the Graham family and the property''s history. Access is event-based and has included history tours, seasonal haunted attractions and paranormal investigations, so verify an authorized date before traveling.', 'limited', null, 'http://majorgrahammansion.com/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Martha Washington Inn', 'martha-washington-inn', 'haunted', 36.7096, -81.97539, 'Abingdon', 'VA', 'Built as a private home in 1832, the building later became a women''s college, served as a Civil War hospital and opened as a hotel in 1935. Stories of a ghostly violinist, wounded soldiers and a riderless horse remain part of the inn''s lore, while the property continues to operate as a hotel, restaurant and spa.', 'open', null, 'https://themartha.com/abingdon-hotel-history/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mary''s Ghost at the Friends Home', 'marys-ghost-at-the-friends-home', 'haunted', 39.53116, -84.08986, 'Waynesville', 'OH', 'Local legend says a young girl named Mary disappeared after her parents became ill in the early nineteenth century and that her laughing spirit still waits for her mother at what is now the Museum at the Friends Home. A Legends & Lore marker stands at the museum, where stories describe Mary rocking inside or appearing on the front porch; interior access follows the museum''s schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/marys-ghost/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Merchant''s House Museum', 'merchants-house-museum', 'haunted', 40.72766, -73.99234, 'New York', 'NY', 'The preserved 1832 Tredwell family home calls itself Manhattan''s most haunted house and has collected reports of footsteps, voices, odors and apparitions since becoming a museum. It remains open for normal daytime tours and also runs scheduled candlelight ghost tours and paranormal programming.', 'open', null, 'https://merchantshouse.org/ghosts/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Missouri State Penitentiary Tours', 'missouri-state-penitentiary-tours', 'haunted', 38.573749, -92.161798, 'Jefferson City', 'MO', 'Missouri State Penitentiary operated for more than a century before closing in 2004, and today visitors can enter former housing units, yards and the gas chamber on guided tours. The site offers both historical tours and scheduled ghost or paranormal experiences.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.missouripentours.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.missouripentours.com/', null, 'node', 9694349988, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Montgomery County Old Courthouse', 'montgomery-county-old-courthouse', 'haunted', 42.95294, -74.37553, 'Fonda', 'NY', 'Built in 1836, this courthouse witnessed generations of criminal trials and executions and now houses county historical records on its first floor. Paranormal reports include unexplained footsteps, voices, falling books and an apparition described as a woman in blue, while the public can visit during normal county history and archives hours.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/montgomery-county-old-courthouse', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Moonville Tunnel', 'moonville-tunnel', 'haunted', 39.30722, -82.32222, 'Brown Township', 'OH', 'Moonville was a remote mining and railroad settlement whose last residents left in the twentieth century, leaving behind its cemetery, foundations and brick-lined railroad tunnel. Numerous deaths along the old rail line produced stories of a spectral brakeman carrying a lantern and other apparitions; the tunnel is reached on the public Moonville Rail Trail, which is open from 6 a.m. to 11 p.m. and remains rugged in places.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitvintonohio.com/history/moonville-tunnel/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Morris-Jumel Mansion', 'morris-jumel-mansion', 'haunted', 40.83447, -73.93858, 'New York', 'NY', 'Manhattan''s oldest surviving house has accumulated stories of apparitions and unexplained activity connected with its long history, including former owner Eliza Jumel. The museum has offered dedicated paranormal investigations, although the mansion is temporarily undergoing roof work in 2026 and access should be checked before visiting.', 'limited', null, 'https://morrisjumel.org/programs/paranormal/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Nemacolin Castle', 'nemacolin-castle', 'haunted', 40.02258, -79.8837, 'Brownsville', 'PA', 'Nemacolin Castle grew from an eighteenth-century trading-post site into an elaborate nineteenth-century mansion overlooking the Monongahela River. The Brownsville Historical Society opens the castle for scheduled tours and events, including programs built around longstanding reports of unexplained activity.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nemacolincastle.net/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('New Orleans Nightmare Haunted House', 'new-orleans-nightmare-haunted-house', 'haunted', 29.951386, -90.175612, 'Elmwood', 'LA', 'New Orleans Nightmare is a large seasonal haunted attraction with multiple themed horror environments, live actors, elaborate sets and optional add-on experiences. It runs on select nights around Halloween rather than as a normal year-round museum or historical site.', 'limited', null, 'https://neworleansnightmare.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://neworleansnightmare.com/', null, 'node', 11145766959, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Nightmare Factory Haunted Attraction', 'nightmare-factory-haunted-attraction', 'haunted', 34.884935, -76.915938, 'Havelock', 'NC', 'Nightmare Factory was a long-running Havelock haunted attraction, but the Havelock location has closed while the business prepares a future move to New Bern. The old Havelock record should not be routed as open; the operator currently plans to return at the new location in 2027.', 'closed', null, 'https://nightmarefactorync.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://nightmarefactorync.com', '+1-252-444-3327', 'way', 616191563, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Nightmare Haunted House', 'nightmare-haunted-house', 'haunted', 33.693626, -78.878382, 'Myrtle Beach', 'SC', 'Nightmare Haunted House is a long-running Myrtle Beach walk-through attraction using dark corridors, horror scenes and live or theatrical scares near the oceanfront. Unlike many temporary October haunts, it operates across a much broader portion of the tourist season and may be open year-round on selected schedules.', 'open', null, 'https://nightmarehauntedhouse.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 2722767216, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ohio State Reformatory', 'ohio-state-reformatory', 'haunted', 40.78373, -82.50275, 'Mansfield', 'OH', 'The Ohio State Reformatory was built beginning in 1886 and operated as a prison until 1990 before becoming a museum and preservation site. Beyond its use as a filming location for The Shawshank Redemption, the enormous cellblocks have a major paranormal reputation and the reformatory offers both regular tours and structured ghost-hunting programs.', 'open', null, 'https://www.mrps.org/visit/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old Idaho Penitentiary', 'old-idaho-penitentiary', 'haunted', 43.602249, -116.162206, 'Boise', 'ID', 'Idaho''s former territorial and state prison operated from the 1870s until 1973 and is now a museum complex of historic cell blocks, yards, solitary-confinement spaces and the gallows. Visitors can tour the prison''s history during regular museum hours, with occasional programs exploring the site''s darker and paranormal reputation.', 'open', null, 'https://history.idaho.gov/oldpen/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://history.idaho.gov/old-penitentiary-hours-location', null, 'way', 421958184, 'America/Boise'),
  ('Old Jail Museum Handprint', 'old-jail-museum-handprint', 'haunted', 40.86384, -75.74649, 'Jim Thorpe', 'PA', 'The former Carbon County Jail opened in 1871 and is infamous for the executions of men accused of belonging to the Molly Maguires. Cell 17 contains a dark handprint that local lore says repeatedly returned after attempts to remove it, and visitors can see it on seasonal guided tours of the jail.', 'limited', null, 'https://theoldjailmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old Stone Fort Museum', 'old-stone-fort-museum', 'haunted', 42.67773, -74.30214, 'Schoharie', 'NY', 'Originally built as a church in 1772, the stone structure was fortified during the Revolutionary War and attacked in 1780. Visitors and investigators have reported apparitions, footsteps, screams and other unexplained activity; the museum is seasonal, with special paranormal programs and ghost hunts offered on selected dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/old-stone-fort-museum', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pennhurst Asylum', 'pennhurst-asylum', 'haunted', 40.19463, -75.56188, 'Spring City', 'PA', 'Pennhurst State School became nationally important after its abusive conditions were exposed and legal challenges helped push the disability-rights movement forward. Parts of the surviving campus now offer scheduled daytime history tours and museum interpretation alongside photography, paranormal and seasonal haunted-attraction experiences, so travelers need tickets for a specific event rather than wandering the property.', 'limited', null, 'https://pennhurstasylum.com/visit/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Peyton Randolph House', 'peyton-randolph-house', 'haunted', 37.27242, -76.70001, 'Williamsburg', 'VA', 'This restored Colonial Williamsburg house was home to prominent revolutionary-era statesman Peyton Randolph and generations of enslaved and free residents. Its long and sometimes violent history has produced some of Colonial Williamsburg''s most persistent ghost stories, and interior access is through the living-history site''s ticketed schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.colonialwilliamsburg.org/locations/peyton-randolph-house/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Phelps Mansion Museum', 'phelps-mansion-museum', 'haunted', 42.10068, -75.90556, 'Binghamton', 'NY', 'Built beginning in 1870 for businessman and former Binghamton mayor Sherman D. Phelps, the mansion is associated with reports of period-dressed apparitions, unexplained footsteps, moving objects and a clock chiming without being wound. It is now a public museum with regular tours, while dedicated haunted tours and paranormal investigations are offered on scheduled dates or by reservation.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/phelps-mansion-museum', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pink Hill Ghost Marker', 'pink-hill-ghost-marker', 'haunted', 42.58108, -75.86414, 'Pitcher', 'NY', 'Local legend says Zella Droff was murdered after secretly attending dances at the former Pitcher Hotel, then returned years later as a ghost who accepted a ride from an unsuspecting salesman. A Legends & Lore marker on Pitcher Hill Road marks the area associated with the story.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/pink-hill-legend/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Poasttown Elementary School', 'poasttown-elementary-school', 'haunted', 39.54838, -84.38132, 'Middletown', 'OH', 'The former Poasttown Elementary School has been converted into a dedicated paranormal investigation destination rather than demolished or repurposed as a conventional museum. Visitors can enter during scheduled flashlight tours, public investigations and private bookings, but the building is not open for casual exploration.', 'limited', null, 'https://poasttownschool.com/flashlight-tours/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Point Lookout Civil War Prison Camp', 'point-lookout-civil-war-prison-camp', 'haunted', 38.05965, -76.33698, 'Scotland', 'MD', 'Point Lookout held tens of thousands of Confederate prisoners during the Civil War, with thousands dying from disease and harsh conditions before the camp closed in 1865. The state park preserves the landscape and interpretation today, while generations of visitors and staff have reported apparitions, voices and other ghost stories around the former prison grounds and lighthouse area.', 'open', null, 'https://dnr.maryland.gov/publiclands/Pages/southern/pointlookout.aspx', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pueblo Ghost Tour', 'pueblo-ghost-tour', 'haunted', 38.281267, -104.496886, 'Pueblo', 'CO', 'Pueblo Ghost Tour combines local history with paranormal stories during guided visits to reportedly active locations in the Pueblo area. Tours run on scheduled dates and may include access to sites not normally experienced as part of a regular museum visit.', 'limited', null, 'https://puebloghosttour.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 12068875894, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Punderson Manor', 'punderson-manor', 'haunted', 41.45108, -81.20787, 'Newbury Township', 'OH', 'The Tudor-style Punderson Manor operates as the lodge at Punderson State Park and has accumulated long-running stories of footsteps, children''s laughter, moving objects and other unexplained activity. It remains a working state-park lodge and restaurant, so visitors can experience the building normally without entering restricted guest areas.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ohiotraveler.com/punderson-manor/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rebel Yell Haunted House', 'rebel-yell-haunted-house', 'haunted', 37.25026, -121.900745, 'San Jose', 'CA', 'Rebel Yell is a long-running San Jose home haunt built around a residential property, with elaborate Halloween displays and walk-through scares created for the season. It is a neighborhood attraction rather than a commercial year-round haunt, so visitors should only go during posted operating nights.', 'limited', null, 'https://rebelyell.info/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'http://www.rebelyell.info/rebelyell.html', null, 'way', 863999850, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Ripley''s Haunted Adventure', 'ripley-s-haunted-adventure', 'haunted', 35.710543, -83.518941, 'Gatlinburg', 'TN', 'Ripley''s Haunted Adventure in Gatlinburg is a year-round walk-through horror attraction on the Parkway featuring live actors, dark sets and jump scares. It is part of Ripley''s cluster of tourist attractions and can be visited independently with a ticket.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ripleys.com/attractions/ripleys-haunted-adventure-gatlinburg', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', 'Su 12:00-21:00; Mo-Th 11:00-22:00; Fr 11:00-23:00; Sa 10:00-23:00', 'https://www.ripleys.com/attractions/ripleys-haunted-adventure-gatlinburg', null, 'way', 1435782642, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ripley''s Haunted Adventure', 'ripley-s-haunted-adventure-2', 'haunted', 33.693268, -78.87879, 'Myrtle Beach', 'SC', 'Ripley''s Haunted Adventure in Myrtle Beach is an interactive walk-through horror attraction on Ocean Boulevard featuring live scares, dark themed rooms and theatrical effects. It operates as a regular tourist attraction rather than only as an October pop-up.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ripleys.com/attractions/ripleys-haunted-adventure-myrtle-beach', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 2722767214, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roberson Mansion', 'roberson-mansion', 'haunted', 42.094, -75.91866, 'Binghamton', 'NY', 'This Italian Renaissance-style mansion was completed in 1907 for Alonzo and Margaret Roberson and is now part of the Roberson Museum and Science Center. Staff and visitors have reported unexplained footsteps, voices and the sensation of unseen people in the house, while the mansion remains accessible through the museum and occasional ghost programs.', 'open', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/roberson-mansion', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rolling Hills Asylum', 'rolling-hills-asylum', 'haunted', 42.881184, -78.132805, 'East Bethany', 'NY', 'Rolling Hills Asylum occupies a former Genesee County poorhouse complex and is now operated specifically for paranormal tourism. Visits are reservation-based and include flashlight tours, self-guided ghost hunts and longer investigations inside the old institution.', 'limited', null, 'https://rollinghillsasylum.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.rollinghillsasylum.com/', '+1 585 502 4066', 'node', 5390600736, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Sachs Covered Bridge', 'sachs-covered-bridge', 'haunted', 39.79742, -77.2762, 'Cumberland Township', 'PA', 'Built in the 1850s, Sachs Covered Bridge carried both Union and Confederate troops during the Gettysburg campaign and is now preserved as a pedestrian bridge. It later accumulated extensive ghost lore involving apparitions, phantom sounds and Civil War soldiers, making it one of Gettysburg''s better-known paranormal stops while still being a legitimate historic structure visitors can walk across.', 'open', null, 'https://www.gettysburgbattlefieldtours.com/the-ghosts-of-gettysburg/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Screaming Bridge of Maud Hughes Road', 'screaming-bridge-of-maud-hughes-road', 'haunted', 39.39449, -84.4104, 'Liberty Township', 'OH', 'The railroad overpass on Maud Hughes Road has accumulated decades of local stories involving screams, apparitions and a phantom train, alongside a documented history of serious accidents in the area. The old bridge was replaced and the roadway realigned in 2015, but the legend remains attached to the crossing; there is no pedestrian facility, so do not stop or park on the bridge or enter the railroad property.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.ohioexploration.com/information/media/journalnews1/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Shepherdstown Ghost Tours', 'shepherdstown-ghost-tours', 'haunted', 39.43067, -77.80492, 'Shepherdstown', 'WV', 'These guided evening walks explore reported hauntings and darker stories around one of West Virginia''s oldest towns. Tours operate on scheduled dates and require booking rather than offering unrestricted access to the buildings discussed along the route.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.smalltownghosttours.net/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Shepherdstown Mystery Walks', 'shepherdstown-mystery-walks', 'haunted', 39.43075, -77.80591, 'Shepherdstown', 'WV', 'Shepherdstown Mystery Walks leads visitors through the historic district while recounting local ghost stories, strange incidents and town legends. Walks meet near the town''s visitor area and operate on scheduled dates, so check the current calendar before routing here.', 'limited', null, 'https://shepherdstownmysterywalks.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Silver Run Tunnel', 'silver-run-tunnel', 'haunted', 39.20769, -81.19664, 'Cairo', 'WV', 'Tunnel No. 19 on the North Bend Rail Trail is associated with the “White Woman of Silver Run,” a ghost said to have appeared on the former B&O tracks in front of passing trains. The 1,376-foot tunnel is publicly reachable from the rail trail, but it is dark, damp and requires a walk or bike ride to reach, so visitors should bring a light.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/the-west-virginia-paranormal-trail-just-got-spookier-with-these-4-new-locations/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Sinister Sidney', 'sinister-sidney', 'haunted', 40.748182, -95.635706, 'Sidney', 'IA', 'Sinister Sidney is a seasonal southwest Iowa haunted attraction built around dark trails, sets and live actors. It generally operates on select fall nights, making it a Halloween-season stop rather than a year-round destination.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/SinisterSidney/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 6239206983, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('South Bass Island Lighthouse', 'south-bass-island-lighthouse', 'haunted', 41.6291, -82.8414, 'Put-in-Bay Township', 'OH', 'The South Bass Island Lighthouse was completed in 1897, and tragedy arrived almost immediately when assistant keeper Harry Anderson died during the island''s 1898 smallpox outbreak. The lighthouse later developed stories of unexplained activity connected to its keepers; the grounds can be viewed publicly, while interior and tower access is limited to scheduled open houses or tours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitputinbay.org/haunted-spirits-put-in-bay/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Split Rock Quarry and the Crusher', 'split-rock-quarry-and-the-crusher', 'haunted', 43.02454, -76.24219, 'Onondaga', 'NY', 'A massive explosion at the Split Rock munitions plant killed more than 50 workers in 1918, and the abandoned quarry later developed stories of phantom footsteps, voices and machinery. The surviving stone Crusher can still be reached on foot within the wooded former factory site, but it is an undeveloped hike and visitors should stay on the permitted public route.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/split-rock-quarry', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Squire''s Castle', 'squires-castle', 'haunted', 41.57994, -81.41926, 'Willoughby Hills', 'OH', 'Squire''s Castle is the stone gatehouse of an estate that Standard Oil executive Feargus B. Squire planned but never completed. Stories later developed about the ghost of Squire''s wife haunting the building, although the tale does not match the documented family history; the castle itself remains freely accessible in Cleveland Metroparks during park hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/squires-castle', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('St. Albans Sanatorium', 'st-albans-sanatorium', 'haunted', 37.13972, -80.57806, 'Fairlawn', 'VA', 'The property began as a boys'' school before becoming St. Albans psychiatric hospital in 1916, and its long institutional history has made it one of Virginia''s best-known paranormal investigation sites. The building is private and entry is allowed only through authorized tours, haunted events or scheduled investigations; never enter outside an official event.', 'limited', null, 'https://stalbans-sanatorium.com/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Story Inn Blue Lady', 'story-inn-blue-lady', 'haunted', 39.09898, -86.21411, 'Story', 'IN', 'Guests at the historic Story Inn have long reported a female apparition known as the Blue Lady, particularly around one of the inn''s rooms. Accounts collected by the property describe details such as the scent of peaches and sightings near a dressing table, while the active inn allows visitors to experience the location through normal lodging and dining access.', 'limited', null, 'https://storyinn.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://storyinn.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Sweet Dreams Haunted Attraction', 'sweet-dreams-haunted-attraction', 'haunted', 30.688622, -88.053745, 'Mobile', 'AL', 'Sweet Dreams is an immersive indoor haunted attraction in Mobile built around theatrical sets, live actors, scare zones and horror-themed side activities. It operates on select nights during the Halloween season rather than as a year-round attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://sweetdreamshaunt.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://sweetdreamshaunt.com', null, 'node', 13565360401, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('The 1890 House Museum', 'the-1890-house-museum', 'haunted', 42.59614, -76.18222, 'Cortland', 'NY', 'This elaborate stone mansion was built for industrialist Chester Wickwire and his family in 1890. Reports of footsteps, shadows, knocking and figures in the windows have made it a local paranormal destination; the museum operates seasonally and also offers scheduled ghost-hunting events and private investigations.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/the-1890-house-museum', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Anchorage Mansion', 'the-anchorage-mansion', 'haunted', 39.41441, -81.46333, 'Marietta', 'OH', 'The Anchorage, originally called Putnam Villa, was built in 1859 and survives as one of Marietta''s imposing nineteenth-century houses. Hidden Marietta uses the property for guided haunted-history tours, flashlight tours and paranormal investigations, with entry limited to scheduled programs and reservations.', 'limited', null, 'https://hiddenmarietta.com/the-anchorage-mansion', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Bates Motel & Haunted Hayride', 'the-bates-motel-haunted-hayride', 'haunted', 39.945144, -75.49665, 'Edgmont Township', 'PA', 'The Bates Motel & Haunted Hayride is a major Philadelphia-area Halloween attraction combining a haunted hayride with the Bates Motel walk-through and additional outdoor scare experiences. It operates on select dates during the fall season and is built as a theatrical haunt rather than a historic motel.', 'limited', null, 'https://thebatesmotel.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://thebatesmotel.com/', null, 'node', 12304730005, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Bellaire House', 'the-bellaire-house', 'haunted', 40.00279, -80.74478, 'Bellaire', 'OH', 'This Belmont Street house has become one of eastern Ohio''s best-known dedicated paranormal investigation properties, with stories involving apparitions, voices and other unexplained activity. It operates as a ticketed paranormal attraction with tours and overnight investigations, so visitors need to book access and should not treat the residential property as an open walk-in site.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.bellairehousetours.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Brewerie at Union Station — Haunted History', 'the-brewerie-at-union-station-haunted-history', 'haunted', 42.12082, -80.0822, 'Erie', 'PA', 'Erie''s Union Station opened in 1927, and the Brewerie''s own history preserves the local legend of "Clara," a child said to have died on its marble stairs and linger in the station afterward. The Brewerie has operated here since 2006 as a normal restaurant and brewpub, with ticketed Haunted History Tours offered on selected dates.', 'open', null, 'https://www.brewerie.com/history.html', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, 'https://www.brewerie.com/tours.html', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Castle Historic House Museum', 'the-castle-historic-house-museum', 'haunted', 39.42054, -81.45502, 'Marietta', 'OH', 'This Gothic Revival mansion was completed in 1855 and is now preserved as a historic house museum in Marietta. The property also hosts ghost tours built around reported sightings, unexplained sounds and local stories associated with the house, while normal historical tours provide daytime access.', 'open', null, 'https://mariettaohio.org/events/the-castle-ghost-tour/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Dark Manor Haunted House', 'the-dark-manor-haunted-house', 'haunted', 41.597772, -72.046822, 'Sprague', 'CT', 'Dark Manor is a seasonal Connecticut haunted attraction combining a large indoor haunted house with outdoor graveyard, village and trail-style scenes. It operates on select fall nights and is designed as a theatrical scare attraction rather than a genuinely historic haunted site.', 'limited', null, 'https://darkmanorproductions.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, '+1 860 822 8662', 'way', 926063400, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Fear Factory', 'the-fear-factory', 'haunted', 36.425363, -89.056996, 'Union City', 'TN', 'The Fear Factory was a multi-floor seasonal haunted attraction in downtown Union City built inside a large old commercial building. Reliable current operating information is scarce, so it should not be marked open until a current season or operator is confirmed.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.thepacer.net/haunted-house-review-fear-factory/', null, null, null, null, 'node', 12165400492, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('The Haunted Blennerhassett Hotel', 'the-haunted-blennerhassett-hotel', 'haunted', 39.26477, -81.56154, 'Parkersburg', 'WV', 'The Blennerhassett opened in 1889 and remains an operating historic hotel in downtown Parkersburg. Guests and paranormal tours have attached numerous apparition, voice and unexplained-activity stories to the building, making it one of the city''s best-known haunted landmarks.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hauntedparkersburgtours.com/13-haunted-places-near-parkersburg', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Haunted Haymond', 'the-haunted-haymond', 'haunted', 38.6625, -80.70917, 'Sutton', 'WV', 'This century-old Sutton house is promoted for paranormal tours and overnight investigations centered on stories of former residents William and Emma Haymond. It is not a normal walk-in museum; tours and overnight access are by appointment or scheduled event.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/west-virginia-paranormal-trail/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Haunted Hinsdale House', 'the-haunted-hinsdale-house', 'haunted', 42.16731, -78.34226, 'Hinsdale', 'NY', 'The Dandy family reported lights switching on by themselves, chanting from the woods and apparitions after moving into this McMahon Road house in the early 1970s, eventually seeking an exorcism. The property is now a paranormal research site offering scheduled day tours, ghost tours and overnight investigations rather than ordinary walk-in access.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/the-haunted-hinsdale-house', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Haunted Hotel', 'the-haunted-hotel', 'haunted', 30.083183, -94.099344, 'Beaumont', 'TX', 'The Haunted Hotel is a long-running Beaumont seasonal haunt that fills a large indoor space with themed rooms, live actors, animatronics and horror sets. It operates on select fall nights and should be treated as limited outside Halloween season.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhoteltx.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 542860725, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('The Haunted Jail', 'the-haunted-jail', 'haunted', 41.155809, -85.48714, 'Columbia City', 'IN', 'The Haunted Jail is a seasonal scare attraction in downtown Columbia City that transforms a jail-themed space into a live-actor Halloween walkthrough. It has operated for decades but is only available during its posted fall schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.facebook.com/TheHauntedJail/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 5931585811, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('The Haunted Mansion', 'the-haunted-mansion-3', 'haunted', 43.627582, -89.776242, 'Wisconsin Dells', 'WI', 'The Haunted Mansion in Wisconsin Dells is a classic downtown walk-through funhouse filled with monsters, spooky scenes, effects and old-school haunted-house gags. It operates during the Dells tourist season rather than only on Halloween, but its schedule is still seasonal.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.dellshauntedmansion.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 9189369882, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('The Horse You Came In On Saloon', 'the-horse-you-came-in-on-saloon', 'haunted', 39.28154, -76.5941, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'A tavern has operated at this Fell''s Point location since the 18th century, and the modern saloon has long embraced stories linking the building to Edgar Allan Poe and a resident ghost known as Edgar. It remains an operating bar and live-music venue rather than a formal paranormal attraction.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-horse-you-came-in-on-saloon-baltimore-maryland', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Huntting''s Pumpkin Patch and Haunted Forest', 'the-huntting-s-pumpkin-patch-and-haunted-forest', 'haunted', 46.571092, -122.5542, 'Cinebar', 'WA', 'Huntting''s is a family-run pumpkin patch near Cinebar that adds a haunted forest and nighttime attractions during the Halloween season. Daytime visitors can expect the farm and pumpkin-patch experience, while the haunted portion is limited to specific fall evenings.', 'limited', null, 'https://thehunttings.business.site/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', 'Sep Fr[-1]-Oct 31 Mo-Su 10:00-23:00', 'https://thehunttings.business.site', '+1-360-388-7920', 'node', 11214339511, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('The Old Hospital on College Hill', 'the-old-hospital-on-college-hill', 'haunted', 37.67495, -82.27287, 'Williamson', 'WV', 'Opened as a hospital in 1928, this large hilltop building served medical and later office uses before becoming a public historic and paranormal-tour destination in 2021. Current visits are through scheduled tours, investigations and special events; it is not a daily walk-in attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.collegehillhospital.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Ridges', 'the-ridges', 'haunted', 39.32026, -82.1094, 'Athens', 'OH', 'The Athens Lunatic Asylum opened in 1874 and eventually became the enormous complex now called The Ridges, which Ohio University acquired after the hospital era ended. The grounds and trails are public and parts of the complex now house university facilities and the Kennedy Museum, while abandoned or restricted buildings are off-limits; the site''s institutional history has made it one of Athens'' best-known paranormal locations.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.ohio.edu/ridges/visit', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The White Lady of Durand Eastman Park', 'the-white-lady-of-durand-eastman-park', 'haunted', 43.23597, -77.55674, 'Irondequoit', 'NY', 'For generations, people around Durand Eastman Park have told stories of a white-clad woman wandering near Lake Ontario with ghostly hounds while searching for her missing daughter. A Legends & Lore marker now stands on Lakeshore Boulevard near the park and the stone ruins popularly called the White Lady''s Castle.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/the-white-lady/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thirteen Curves', 'thirteen-curves', 'haunted', 42.98883, -76.25056, 'Onondaga', 'NY', 'Cedarvale Road''s twisting section known as Thirteen Curves is associated with the legend of a newlywed bride who died with her husband and still wanders the road looking for him. A Legends & Lore marker stands near Cedarvale Road and West Seneca Turnpike, so visitors do not need to stop on the narrow curves themselves.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/thirteen-curves/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thurber House', 'thurber-house', 'haunted', 39.96578, -82.98522, 'Columbus', 'OH', 'Humorist James Thurber lived in this house as a child, and unexplained noises experienced by his family helped inspire his story "The Night the Ghost Got In." The restored house is now a literary museum with regular weekend hours, and it also permits scheduled private ghost investigations.', 'open', null, 'https://www.thurberhouse.org/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Trans-Allegheny Lunatic Asylum', 'trans-allegheny-lunatic-asylum', 'haunted', 39.038246, -80.471814, 'Weston', 'WV', 'A quarter-mile of hand-cut sandstone, built for 250 patients and holding well over two thousand by the 1950s. Daytime tours cover the architecture and the medical history; the overnight ones cover the reason most people have heard of it.', 'limited', null, 'https://trans-alleghenylunaticasylum.com/', '2026-09-06T01:56:28.154232+00:00', null, 'https://trans-alleghenylunaticasylum.com/', '+1-304-259-5070', 'way', 374509925, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Trimper''s Haunted House', 'trimpers-haunted-house', 'haunted', 38.32653, -75.08808, 'Ocean City', 'MD', 'Built in 1964 and designed by legendary dark-ride creator Bill Tracy, Trimper''s Haunted House is one of the few surviving Tracy attractions still operating in its original location. The two-story boardwalk ride retains vintage stunts alongside newer effects and operates seasonally with Trimper Rides.', 'limited', null, 'https://trimpershauntedhouse.com/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Twin City Opera House', 'twin-city-opera-house', 'haunted', 39.649, -81.85349, 'McConnelsville', 'OH', 'Twin City Opera House opened in 1892 and still operates as a theater and movie house in downtown McConnelsville. Decades of reports involving footsteps, voices and apparitions have made it a major Ohio paranormal site, and the theater offers scheduled public ghost hunts and private investigations rather than unrestricted after-hours access.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedtwincityoperahouse.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Victoria Theatre', 'victoria-theatre', 'haunted', 39.76223, -84.19174, 'Dayton', 'OH', 'Victoria Theatre opened in 1866 and has accumulated several long-running ghost stories during more than a century and a half of performances. The best-known involves the legendary "Miss Vicki," whose presence is associated with rose perfume, footsteps and a face in a dressing-room mirror; the theater remains an active public performance venue.', 'open', null, 'https://www.destinationdayton.org/blog/post/uncovering-eerie-legends-5-haunted-places-in-dayton-with-tales-to-know-about/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('West Virginia State Penitentiary Tours', 'west-virginia-state-penitentiary-tours', 'haunted', 39.916014, -80.742304, 'Moundsville', 'WV', 'The former West Virginia Penitentiary is a massive Gothic prison that operated until 1995 and now offers guided history tours through cell blocks, yards and other restricted areas. Visitors can also book public ghost hunts, paranormal investigations and seasonal Halloween experiences, with the normal tour season running on scheduled dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvpentours.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.wvpentours.com/', '+1-304-845-6200', 'way', 829669282, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Whispers Estate', 'whispers-estate', 'haunted', 38.73332, -86.47452, 'Mitchell', 'IN', 'Built in the 1890s, this house has been operated specifically as a paranormal attraction rather than simply marketed through outside ghost stories. Whispers Estate offers scheduled investigations and events centered on reported voices, apparitions, movement and other unexplained activity inside the property.', 'limited', null, 'https://whispersestate.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://whispersestate.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('White Horse Inn;White Horse Inn & Bar', 'white-horse-inn-white-horse-inn-bar', 'haunted', 41.998436, -117.719895, 'McDermitt', 'NV', 'The old White Horse Inn near McDermitt is a historic roadside building, but current public records describe the structure as unsafe, with serious deterioration, asbestos and mold concerns. It is not a public haunted attraction and should not be routed for entry or exploration.', 'private', null, 'https://www.humboldtcountynv.gov/DocumentCenter/View/8501/HCC-031824', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'http://www.pbase.com/nevada_beeutiful/white_horse_inn_nevada', null, 'way', 1121464184, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Widow Susan Road', 'widow-susan-road', 'haunted', 42.92811, -74.16155, 'Amsterdam', 'NY', 'The road is named for Susan DeGraff, whose ghost is said to appear wearing white and crying while searching for her husband''s grave. A Legends & Lore marker at 179 Widow Susan Road gives travelers a safe physical point for the story rather than encouraging anyone to wander the road at night.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/widow-susan-road/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Wildwood Sanitarium', 'wildwood-sanitarium', 'haunted', 42.15829, -78.6924, 'Salamanca', 'NY', 'Wildwood opened in 1906 as a sanitarium and bath house and later served as a tuberculosis clinic and apartments. Visitors and investigators report shadow figures, voices and unexplained physical contact, and the restored property now offers history tours, ghost tours and investigations by reservation.', 'limited', null, 'https://hauntedhistorytrail.com/explore/wildwood-sanitarium', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Willard Library Grey Lady', 'willard-library-grey-lady', 'haunted', 37.97836, -87.57404, 'Evansville', 'IN', 'Willard Library''s best-known legend concerns the "Grey Lady," an apparition reportedly seen inside the Victorian Gothic library for decades. The library openly embraces the story with its long-running Ghost Cams and paranormal programming, making this an unusually accessible haunted-location stop rather than an abandoned site.', 'open', null, 'https://www.willardlib.org/ghost-cams', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.willardlib.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Witch Mansion Haunted House', 'witch-mansion-haunted-house', 'haunted', 42.521794, -70.89348, 'Salem', 'MA', 'Witch Mansion is a walk-through Salem attraction using witches, ghosts, monsters, lighting effects and animated scenes to create a traditional haunted-house experience. It operates on a seasonal schedule that expands heavily during Salem''s October crowds.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.witchmansion.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 13043301667, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Witch''s Tower', 'witchs-tower', 'haunted', 39.70992, -84.18012, 'Kettering', 'OH', 'The stone Lookout Tower at Hills & Dales MetroPark, commonly called the Witch''s Tower or Frankenstein''s Castle, was completed in 1941. A teenage girl was killed by lightning at the tower in 1967, after which stories of ghostly figures became attached to it; the tower''s entrance is sealed, but hikers can reach and view the exterior from the park trail.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.daytondailynews.com/what-to-do/the-ghostly-tales-behind-hills-dales-witchs-tower/M55XOSN3I5CTJKSAAITLOOPG4E/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Zak Bagan''s The Haunted Museum', 'zak-bagan-s-the-haunted-museum', 'haunted', 36.158381, -115.145638, 'Las Vegas', 'NV', 'Zak Bagans'' The Haunted Museum fills a historic Las Vegas mansion with rooms devoted to paranormal objects, notorious crimes, occult artifacts and items claimed to be cursed or haunted. Visitors follow a guided experience through the collection, with age restrictions and upgraded experiences available.', 'open', null, 'https://thehauntedmuseum.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', 'Mo, We-Sa 13:00-21:00; Su 12:00-20:00', 'https://thehauntedmuseum.com/', '+1-702-444-0744', 'way', 806953202, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Alien Rock Formation near Cliff Dwellers', 'alien', 'ufos', 36.782399, -111.766073, 'Marble Canyon', 'AZ', 'An OpenStreetMap node named only Alien, about two and a half miles north of Cliff Dwellers in Coconino County — in the Vermilion Cliffs and Marble Canyon country, not near LeChee. No independent source explains what the feature is, who named it, or whether it is an established stop at all, and we have not confirmed the land status. Treat it as an unverified lead rather than a destination.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/5596600521', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Alien Museum at Rockin'' Rollers', 'alien-museum', 'ufos', 35.662973, -105.998555, 'Santa Fe', 'NM', 'Mapped as the Alien Museum, this shares an address with Rockin'' Rollers Event Arena, a long-running roller rink known for its extensive alien-themed decor. There is no separate museum with its own hours — you see the extraterrestrial displays by turning up to a public skating session or an event.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.santafe.org/things-to-do/family-activities/', '2026-09-06T01:53:15.49385+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Alien Woman Hoodoo, Bisti Badlands', 'alien-woman', 'ufos', 36.270912, -108.226433, 'West Hammond', 'NM', 'Not a statue or a business but a naturally eroded rock formation in the Bisti Rock Garden, among named hoodoos including the Elegant Hoodoo and the Valley of Bones. This is BLM-managed federal wilderness rather than Navajo Nation land. Open to hikers, but there are no marked routes, effectively no phone signal or water, and access roads can become impassable after rain or snow.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/bisti-de-na-zin-wilderness', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Area 51 Alien Center', 'area-51-alien-center', 'ufos', 36.643767, -116.395984, 'Amargosa Valley', 'NV', 'A commercial alien-themed travel centre on US 95 — fuel, food, a gift shop and a great deal of Area 51 merchandise, rather than a museum or a crash site. Open daily from 5am to 11pm, and an easy walk-in stop rather than a destination.', 'open', null, 'https://area51aliencenter.net/', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Area 51 North Gate (Rachel Back Gate)', 'area-51-back-gate', 'ufos', 37.594035, -115.898805, 'Alamo', 'NV', 'Where a public desert road meets the heavily monitored northern boundary of the Nevada Test and Training Range. You may go as far as the warning signs, fence and gate and no further: beyond that line is restricted military property patrolled by armed security. Obey every posted trespass and photography warning.', 'roadside', null, 'https://travelnevada.com/extraterrestrial/area-51/', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Avrocar', 'avrocar', 'ufos', 39.78225, -84.10767, 'Dayton', 'OH', 'The Avrocar was a real Cold War attempt to build a disc-shaped vertical-takeoff aircraft that looked remarkably like the flying saucers dominating UFO culture at the time. One surviving example is displayed inside the National Museum of the United States Air Force, where admission is free during museum hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/avrocar', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Carbondale UFO Marker', 'carbondale-ufo-marker', 'ufos', 41.56985, -75.5034, 'Carbondale', 'PA', 'A city historical marker records the November 1974 incident in which teenagers reported a glowing object flying low over Carbondale and crashing into a silt pond near Russell Park. Crowds and investigators descended on the site before a lantern was eventually recovered from the water, but the case remains a major piece of local UFO folklore and now inspires the annual Carbondalien Festival.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=135019', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hook-Up Towing UFO', 'hook-up-towing-ufo', 'ufos', 39.856108, -95.5433, 'Hiawatha', 'KS', 'A flying saucer parked outside a towing company in northeast Kansas — roadside advertising that outgrew its purpose. Visible from the road, but the yard is a working business, so look rather than wander in.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/9077872686', '2026-09-06T01:37:28.209467+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('International UFO Museum & Research Center', 'international-ufo-museum-research-center', 'ufos', 33.393705, -104.52322, 'Roswell', 'NM', 'The centre of the Roswell industry, in a former cinema on Main Street. Founded in 1991 by people connected to the 1947 incident, it holds exhibits, witness affidavits and a research library, and takes the documentary record rather more seriously than the gift shops around it.', 'open', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/1806341993', '2026-09-06T01:37:28.209467+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Kecksburg UFO Monument', 'kecksburg-ufo-monument', 'ufos', 40.1834, -79.462, 'Kecksburg', 'PA', 'Something came down in the woods here on the evening of 9 December 1965, seen across several states. Astronomers called it a meteor; witnesses described an acorn-shaped object and a military convoy. The village settled the matter its own way: the large acorn outside the volunteer fire department is a prop built for an Unsolved Mysteries episode in 1990, and it has stood there ever since.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kecksburg_UFO_incident', '2026-09-06T01:56:28.154232+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Landing Zone by Peter Reiquam', 'landing-zone', 'ufos', 47.890874, -122.276852, 'Everett', 'WA', 'A public artwork at Paine Field Community Park: a sixteen-foot flying-saucer shelter surrounded by alien boulders and an X-shaped landing-zone bench, commissioned by Snohomish County in 2004 and recognised among the top public art projects of 2010. The park is public and open daily from 7am to dusk.', 'open', null, 'https://snohomishcountywa.gov/Facilities/Facility/Details/Paine-Field-Community-Park-83', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Pine Bush UFO Museum', 'pine-bush-ufo-museum', 'ufos', 41.609741, -74.301059, 'Pine Bush', 'NY', 'The Pine Bush UFO & Paranormal Museum explores the Hudson Valley area''s long history of UFO sightings through interactive exhibits, witness accounts, displays and alien-themed experiences. This is clearly a UFO-focused attraction and belongs in the `ufos` category rather than `haunted`.', 'open', null, 'https://pinebushmuseum.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://pinebushmuseum.com/', null, 'node', 8703565078, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Presque Isle Beach 6 UFO Encounter', 'presque-isle-beach-6-ufo-encounter', 'ufos', 42.14441, -80.13804, 'Erie', 'PA', 'On July 31, 1966, witnesses stranded at Beach 6 reported a luminous metallic object descending near the beach, an incident later investigated as Project Blue Book case 10798. Beach 6 is still an ordinary public beach at Presque Isle State Park—there is no UFO monument—so the physical stop is the location associated with the documented Erie UFO story.', 'open', null, 'https://www.eriereader.com/article/eerie-erie-', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/presque-isle-state-park/swimming', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roswell crash site (1947)', 'roswell-crash-site-1947', 'ufos', 33.950328, -105.313908, 'Capitan', 'NM', 'These coordinates match the BLM''s Alleged UFO Skip Site, where the agency has built a legal public route: park on Lincoln County Road B007 and walk roughly a mile across BLM land. The old approaches from north and south cross private property and may not be used. Remote, unshaded, and with no water.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/alleged-ufo-skip-site', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Rt 30 Alien', 'rt-30-alien', 'ufos', 43.633298, -74.39443, 'Lake Pleasant', 'NY', 'A roadside alien figure on Route 30 in the Adirondacks, the sort of thing that exists purely so people slow down. A quick photograph rather than a destination.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/9925313103', '2026-09-06T01:37:28.209467+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Black Mailbox', 'the-black-mailbox', 'ufos', 37.457061, -115.482604, 'Alamo', 'NV', 'The long-running meeting point for UFO watchers on the Extraterrestrial Highway, named for rancher Steve Medlin''s mailbox. The original was removed years ago and a succession of replacements has followed; the one standing in July 2025 was reported destroyed by November. Treat the spot as the attraction rather than expecting a particular box to be there.', 'roadside', null, 'https://travelnevada.com/extraterrestrial/black-mailbox/', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Travis Walton''s Abduction Site', 'travis-walton-s-abduction-site', 'ufos', 34.299978, -110.649058, 'Heber-Overgaard', 'AZ', 'The Turkey Springs area of the Apache-Sitgreaves National Forest, associated with the incident of 5 November 1975 in which logger Travis Walton''s crew reported a luminous object and Walton disappeared for five days. There is nothing built here: it is public National Forest backcountry on forest and logging roads. Check current road conditions and which routes are legally open before going in.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.navajocountyaz.gov/597/NCSO-History-PDF', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('UFO crash site ( Aztec NM )', 'ufo-crash-site-aztec-nm', 'ufos', 36.878494, -107.841069, 'Aztec', 'NM', 'The claimed site of the alleged crash of 25 March 1948, marked by a plaque placed in 2007, sitting on the BLM-managed Alien Run trail system in Hart Canyon. Both the City of Aztec and the BLM point hikers and mountain bikers here. No admission fee, but it is a remote dirt-road and trail destination with no drinking water.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/alien-run-mountain-bike-trail', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('UFO Experience', 'ufo-experience', 'ufos', 33.555006, -111.876563, 'Scottsdale', 'AZ', 'A ticketed indoor exhibition at Arizona Boardwalk covering famous UFO reports, alleged abductions, government and military material and science-fiction pop culture. Open daily 10am to 6pm. Worth knowing that Arizona Boardwalk sits within the Salt River Pima-Maricopa Indian Community: the Scottsdale label is geographically convenient but does not describe the jurisdiction.', 'limited', null, 'https://theufoexperience.com/', '2026-09-07T02:03:56.500228+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('UFO Landing Port', 'ufo-landing-port', 'ufos', 44.444383, -87.837378, 'Poland', 'WI', 'A marked landing pad built for visitors who have not arrived yet, standing by the roadside in rural Wisconsin. Free, always there, and entirely sincere about being a joke.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/node/4530157043', '2026-09-06T01:37:28.209467+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Abandoned Lock No. 19', 'abandoned-lock-no-19', 'weird-history', 39.25509, -81.69157, 'Washington', 'WV', 'Built in 1916, Lock and Dam No. 19 once helped move river traffic past a wicket dam on the Ohio River before the system was replaced in 1968. Ruins of the old powerhouse remain near a public boat ramp, but the structure is deteriorated and should be viewed without climbing; the former lock houses uphill are private property and should not be approached.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/abandoned-lock-no-19', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('abandoned mine marker', 'abandoned-mine-marker', 'weird-history', 35.464799, -106.12779, 'La Cienega', 'NM', 'A mapped abandoned-mine marker about seven miles south of La Cienega. No reliable source identifies which mine it commemorates or documents a visitor site, so expect a marker rather than anything explorable. Abandoned workings should never be entered.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/programs/aml-environmental-cleanup/aml', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Alan Freed''s Jukebox Grave', 'alan-freeds-jukebox-grave', 'weird-history', 41.51413, -81.59282, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'Disc jockey Alan Freed, who helped popularize the term rock and roll, was reinterred at Lake View Cemetery in 2016 after his ashes had previously been displayed at the Rock & Roll Hall of Fame. His grave is marked by a distinctive jukebox-shaped monument that can be visited during cemetery hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/grave-of-alan-freed', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Anamosa State Penitentiary Museum', 'anamosa-state-penitentiary-museum', 'weird-history', 42.112511, -91.29138, 'Anamosa', 'IA', 'The Anamosa State Penitentiary Museum sits outside the walls of the still-active prison and documents its history through uniforms, photographs, inmate-made objects, weapons and a replica cell. The museum operates on a limited seasonal schedule and is a prison-history stop rather than a conventional haunted house.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.asphistory.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 367089373, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Angel Mounds State Historic Site', 'angel-mounds-state-historic-site', 'weird-history', 37.93886, -87.46023, 'Evansville', 'IN', 'Between roughly A.D. 1000 and 1450, Mississippian people built a major town here containing large earthen platform mounds, plazas and houses. The preserved archaeological site and museum allow visitors to encounter the landscape without treating the Indigenous city as a mysterious or vanished-civilization legend.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.indianamuseum.org/historic-sites/angel-mounds/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Aquia Church', 'aquia-church', 'weird-history', 38.46463, -77.40303, 'Stafford', 'VA', 'The present Aquia Church was completed in 1757 after its nearly finished predecessor burned, and the building later survived use by Union soldiers as a stable, hospital and campsite during the Civil War. It remains an active Episcopal church with remarkably preserved colonial woodwork, and historical tours should be arranged with the church office rather than treated as unrestricted sightseeing.', 'limited', null, 'https://aquiachurch.org/about/history/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ashcroft Ghost Town', 'ashcroft-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 39.055591, -106.799564, 'Ashcroft', 'CO', 'Ashcroft is a preserved silver-mining ghost town outside Aspen where visitors can walk among surviving cabins, commercial buildings and other remnants of the short-lived 1880s boomtown. Seasonal interpretation and tours help explain the settlement''s mining history and rapid decline.', 'limited', null, 'https://aspenhistory.org/tours-sites/ashcroft/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 2965136490, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Aspin Hill Pet Cemetery', 'aspin-hill-pet-cemetery', 'weird-history', 39.0799, -77.07629, 'Aspen Hill', 'MD', 'Established in the early 20th century, Aspin Hill is one of the country''s oldest pet cemeteries and contains tens of thousands of animal burials alongside a smaller number of human graves. Elaborate markers memorialize dogs, cats, birds and other pets, and the cemetery is open for respectful daytime visits.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/aspin-hill-pet-cemetery', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Assassin''s End — John Wilkes Booth Marker', 'assassins-end-john-wilkes-booth-marker', 'weird-history', 38.14009, -77.2286, 'Port Royal', 'VA', 'John Wilkes Booth was cornered at Richard Garrett''s farm and fatally shot on April 26, 1865, twelve days after assassinating Abraham Lincoln. The farm buildings are gone and the actual site lies in a posted highway median with no public access, so OddWay should route travelers only to the roadside "Assassin''s End" historical marker and pull-off.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/assassins-end', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Austin Dam Ruins', 'austin-dam-ruins', 'weird-history', 41.65272, -78.08592, 'Keating Township', 'PA', 'The broken concrete walls in Austin Dam Memorial Park are the remains of the dam that failed catastrophically in 1911, sending water and debris through the valley and killing dozens of people. Visitors can walk among the enormous tilted sections of concrete and see interpretive material in the public park.', 'open', null, 'https://www.austindam.net/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bacon''s Castle', 'bacons-castle', 'weird-history', 37.10905, -76.72231, 'Surry', 'VA', 'Built in 1665, this extraordinary brick house acquired its misleading name after followers of Nathaniel Bacon seized and fortified it during Bacon''s Rebellion in 1676. The historic house is open for scheduled tours during its operating season, while the grounds generally have broader daytime access.', 'limited', null, 'https://preservationvirginia.org/historic-sites/bacons-castle/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ballarat', 'ballarat', 'weird-history', 36.047917, -117.225675, 'Searles Valley', 'CA', 'Founded in 1897 to serve gold mines in the Panamint Mountains, with around 400 residents by 1898. What is left is adobe ruins and scattered mining remains off Panamint Valley Road. Privately owned, genuinely remote, and with no dependable services.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/deva/learn/historyculture/death-valley-ghost-towns.htm', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Bannerman Castle', 'bannerman-castle', 'weird-history', 41.45531, -73.98887, 'Fishkill', 'NY', 'Military-surplus dealer Francis Bannerman built this eccentric castle-like arsenal on Pollepel Island between 1900 and 1918, later leaving a romantic ruin after explosions, fire and abandonment. The island is controlled by New York State Parks and can be visited only through authorized seasonal boat or kayak tours.', 'limited', null, 'https://bannermancastle.org/faq/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Barcelona Lighthouse', 'barcelona-lighthouse', 'weird-history', 42.3411, -79.59483, 'Westfield', 'NY', 'Completed in 1829, Barcelona Lighthouse is recognized as the world''s first lighthouse powered by natural gas. The grounds are open year-round and the restored tower can be climbed during staffed seasonal hours when weather and staffing permit.', 'open', null, 'https://staffportal.parks.ny.gov/parks/196/details.aspx', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Beckley Exhibition Coal Mine', 'beckley-exhibition-coal-mine', 'weird-history', 37.78434, -81.19614, 'Beckley', 'WV', 'Visitors ride a mine car roughly 1,500 feet into a historic drift mine while veteran miners explain the equipment and working conditions of West Virginia coal mining. The surrounding complex includes relocated coal-camp buildings, but the underground attraction operates seasonally.', 'limited', null, 'https://beckley.org/coal-mine/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Belcamp (Ghost Town)', 'belcamp-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 33.443616, -98.685788, 'Olney', 'TX', 'A mapped ghost-town locality in rural Archer County, roughly six miles northeast of Olney near Anarene. No dependable published history or visitor facility could be found, so treat it as a drive-by locality and stay on public roads rather than entering ranch property.', 'roadside', null, 'https://mapcarta.com/N1731158405', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Bethlehem Steel Blast Furnaces at SteelStacks', 'bethlehem-steel-blast-furnaces-at-steelstacks', 'weird-history', 40.61487, -75.36953, 'Bethlehem', 'PA', 'Five enormous blast furnaces from the former Bethlehem Steel plant loom over the SteelStacks arts campus, preserving the scale of a company that once employed tens of thousands of workers. Visitors can view the furnaces freely from the public campus and Hoover-Mason Trestle, with guided industrial-history tours available separately.', 'open', null, 'https://www.historicbethlehem.org/visit-us/experience/rise-and-fall-of-bethlehem-steel-walking-tour/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Biddison Family Cemetery', 'biddison-family-cemetery', 'weird-history', 39.34005, -76.5552, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'A tiny 19th-century family cemetery survives improbably in the middle of a modern Baltimore neighborhood, a remnant of the much larger property once owned by the Biddison family. Most graves date to the 1800s, and neighborhood volunteers have periodically cleared vegetation from the otherwise easily overlooked burial ground.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/biddison-family-cemetery', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bilby Tower', 'bilby-tower', 'weird-history', 39.11805, -85.29394, 'Osgood', 'IN', 'U.S. Coast and Geodetic Surveyor Jasper Bilby designed a distinctive steel surveying tower in the 1920s that could be erected quickly above trees and terrain. One surviving tower stands near Osgood as a rare monument to the pre-satellite era of precision mapping.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/bilby-tower', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.in.gov/history/markers/4326.htm', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Blackbeard''s Severed Head Marker', 'blackbeards-severed-head-marker', 'weird-history', 37.01663, -76.34278, 'Hampton', 'VA', 'After Blackbeard was killed off North Carolina in 1718, his severed head was brought back to Virginia and displayed at the mouth of the Hampton River as a warning to other pirates. A modern historical marker at Blackbeard''s Point identifies the tradition and gives travelers a physical stop tied to one of the grimmest episodes in Virginia''s pirate history.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/70036', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bladensburg Dueling Grounds', 'bladensburg-dueling-grounds', 'weird-history', 38.93356, -76.95199, 'Colmar Manor', 'MD', 'The fields near old Bladensburg became a notorious place for settling political and personal disputes with pistols during the 19th century, earning the nearby stream the nickname “Blood Run.” More than 50 duels are associated with the area, and a marker now interprets the history from the public grounds.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/bladensburg-dueling-grounds', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Blennerhassett Island Historical State Park', 'blennerhassett-island-historical-state-park', 'weird-history', 39.27194, -81.62472, 'Parkersburg', 'WV', 'Harman and Margaret Blennerhassett built an extravagant estate on this Ohio River island, which later became tangled in Aaron Burr''s mysterious western political schemes. A reconstructed mansion and historical grounds can be toured today, but normal visitor access depends on the seasonal sternwheel boat from Parkersburg.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvstateparks.com/parks/blennerhassett-island-historical-state-park/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Blue Ridge Tunnel', 'blue-ridge-tunnel', 'weird-history', 38.03009, -78.85297, 'Afton', 'VA', 'Engineer Claudius Crozet''s 4,273-foot railroad tunnel opened in 1858 after nearly nine years of difficult construction through the Blue Ridge Mountains. The abandoned bore reopened as a pedestrian and bicycle trail in 2020, but it is completely dark inside and the walk to and through it requires a flashlight and appropriate trail access.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nelsoncounty-va.gov/2020/11/20/claudius-crozet-blue-ridge-tunnel-open/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bollman Truss Bridge', 'bollman-truss-bridge', 'weird-history', 39.13486, -76.82538, 'Savage', 'MD', 'This bright iron bridge is the last surviving example of Wendel Bollman''s once-influential railroad truss design. Built in the 19th century and later moved to Savage, it now carries a pedestrian trail across the Little Patuxent River and can be walked through freely.', 'open', null, 'https://www.loc.gov/item/md0583/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Brunswick Stew Origin Marker', 'brunswick-stew-origin-marker', 'weird-history', 36.98743, -77.96328, 'Blackstone', 'VA', 'Virginia tradition says camp cook Jimmy Matthews created an early Brunswick stew during an 1828 hunting trip in Brunswick County, originally using squirrel, butter, onions, bread and seasoning. A Virginia historical marker erected in 1997 preserves the claim, though competing origin stories exist elsewhere, making this a suitably odd food-history roadside stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=107700', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Buffalo Central Terminal', 'buffalo-central-terminal', 'weird-history', 42.88965, -78.83024, 'Buffalo', 'NY', 'This enormous Art Deco railway terminal opened in 1929 and was abandoned by passenger trains in 1979, leaving its tower and concourse as one of Buffalo''s most imposing industrial-era landmarks. Interior historic tours are currently suspended during restoration work, but an official self-guided outdoor audio tour follows designated exterior paths.', 'limited', null, 'https://buffalocentralterminal.org/tours/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Buffalo Ridge Ghost Town', 'buffalo-ridge-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 43.607993, -96.885893, 'Hartford', 'SD', 'Buffalo Ridge Ghost Town is a quirky roadside Old West display near the Buffalo Ridge travel stop, with recreated frontier buildings and weathered western scenes. It is more roadside attraction than authentic abandoned settlement, making it a fun photo stop for travelers interested in kitschy ghost-town imagery.', 'open', null, 'https://maps.apple.com/?q=Buffalo%20Ridge%20Ghost%20Town', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 1063293375, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Buried in Her Cadillac', 'buried-in-her-cadillac', 'weird-history', 39.02583, -84.88778, 'Aurora', 'IN', 'Aurora Schuck was buried at River View Cemetery in 1989 inside her red 1976 Cadillac Eldorado, reportedly requiring a burial area spanning multiple normal grave plots. Nothing dramatic rises above the burial today, but the cemetery itself is public and the bizarre interment story gives the site an unusually literal connection between car culture and burial custom.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/76516', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://aurorariverviewcemetery.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Calamity Corners', 'calamity-corners', 'weird-history', 41.31803, -74.29696, 'Sugar Loaf', 'NY', 'The intersection of Hambletonian Road and Pine Hill Road became known locally as Calamity Corners because of a succession of deaths, accidents and violent events associated with the area. Its reputation begins with the 1818 murder of Richard Jennings, a case often cited as an early American murder-for-hire, and a Legends & Lore marker was added in 2026.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/calamity-corners/', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Calico Ghost Town', 'calico-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 34.948373, -116.864611, 'Yermo', 'CA', 'Calico grew around one of California''s richest silver districts from 1881, reaching roughly 1,200 residents before falling silver prices emptied it. Walter Knott restored the surviving town and gave it to San Bernardino County in 1966. Ticketed: historic buildings, shops, the Maggie Mine and a railroad.', 'limited', null, 'https://parks.sbcounty.gov/park/calico-ghost-town-regional-park/', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Camp Atterbury POW Chapel', 'camp-atterbury-pow-chapel', 'weird-history', 39.37572, -86.06832, 'Edinburgh', 'IN', 'Italian prisoners of war held at Camp Atterbury built this tiny Catholic chapel in 1943 using limited and salvaged materials. Restored after later vandalism and fire damage, the Chapel in the Meadow survives as a rare physical remnant of the camp''s World War II prisoner compound.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/camp-atterbury-prisoner-of-war-chapel', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.in.gov/indiana-national-guard/about/history-and-museums/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Cardiff Giant', 'cardiff-giant', 'weird-history', 42.70598, -74.92973, 'Cooperstown', 'NY', 'The Cardiff Giant was a ten-foot stone figure secretly manufactured and buried before being "discovered" in 1869 and promoted as a petrified prehistoric man. One of America''s most famous nineteenth-century hoaxes survives today inside The Farmers'' Museum in Cooperstown.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/cardiff-giant', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Carrie Blast Furnaces', 'carrie-blast-furnaces', 'weird-history', 40.40757, -79.8867, 'Rankin', 'PA', 'Carrie Furnaces 6 and 7 are surviving pieces of the enormous Homestead Works steel complex that once dominated the Monongahela Valley. Rivers of Steel preserves the furnaces and offers scheduled industrial-history tours, but visitors cannot freely enter the site outside authorized programs.', 'limited', null, 'https://riversofsteel.com/attractions/carrie-furnaces/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cass Scenic Railroad State Park', 'cass-scenic-railroad-state-park', 'weird-history', 38.39682, -79.91429, 'Cass', 'WV', 'Cass preserves a former lumber-company town and the steam railroad that once hauled timber out of the surrounding mountains. Visitors can explore the historic town area, while the famous Shay-locomotive train rides operate on scheduled, ticketed departures rather than as an always-available attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvstateparks.com/parks/cass-scenic-railroad-state-park/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Castle Dome Mine Museum', 'castle-dome-mine-museum', 'weird-history', 33.045874, -114.178023, 'Yuma', 'AZ', 'Castle Dome Mine Museum recreates and preserves the once-bustling Castle Dome mining district with dozens of historic buildings, mining artifacts and exhibits collected from the surrounding desert. It is primarily a mining and ghost-town history stop, with seasonal hours and additional mine/mineral experiences available.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.castledomemuseum.org/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 1137995652, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Cathedral Tower', 'cathedral-tower', 'weird-history', 41.14894, -81.50628, 'Cuyahoga Falls', 'OH', 'Televangelist Rex Humbard began building a 750-foot tower in 1971 that was supposed to contain a revolving restaurant and support television broadcasting from his Cathedral of Tomorrow complex. Construction abruptly stopped when the concrete shaft reached 494 feet, and the unfinished tower still dominates the skyline as a communications structure; view it from public roads and do not enter the fenced property.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.summitmemory.org/digital/collection/ABJarchives/id/2497/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Catoctin Furnace', 'catoctin-furnace', 'weird-history', 39.58116, -77.43445, 'Thurmont', 'MD', 'Iron production began at Catoctin Furnace in 1776 and relied in part on enslaved labor before the industrial village expanded through the 19th century. The surviving furnace stack, historic village, trails and Museum of the Ironworker now interpret both the industry''s technology and the lives of the people who worked there.', 'open', null, 'https://dnr.maryland.gov/publiclands/Pages/western/CunninghamFalls/Catoctin-Furnace.aspx', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cedar Hill Cemetery Faux-Bois Sculptures', 'cedar-hill-cemetery-faux-bois-sculptures', 'weird-history', 38.86023, -76.94105, 'Suitland-Silver Hill', 'MD', 'Cedar Hill Cemetery contains a surprising group of 1930s faux-bois concrete sculptures by Dionicio Rodriguez, made to resemble gnarled trees, logs and rustic wooden structures. The cemetery also contains a mass grave connected to the deadly 1906 Terra Cotta railroad wreck, giving the grounds an unusually layered history.', 'open', null, 'https://spacesarchives.org/explore/search-the-online-collection/cedar-hill-cemetery/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Center of the World', 'center-of-the-world', 'weird-history', 41.228, -80.91, 'Leavittsburg', 'OH', 'The tiny crossroads community called Center of the World was named in the 1840s by businessman Randall D. Wilmot, who hoped the stagecoach stop would become an important settlement. The dream never materialized, but an official green highway sign still marks the oddly named place near the junction of OH-82 and OH-5/OH-534; view it safely from a legal roadside position.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/66691', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Centralia', 'centralia', 'weird-history', 40.804, -76.3405, 'Centralia', 'PA', 'A coal seam under the borough caught fire in 1962 and is still burning. Almost everyone was bought out and moved; the street grid remains, the buildings mostly do not, and steam still works its way up through the ground on cold mornings.', 'roadside', null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Century of Progress Homes', 'century-of-progress-homes', 'weird-history', 41.68476, -86.99881, 'Beverly Shores', 'IN', 'Five experimental houses from Chicago''s 1933–34 Century of Progress World''s Fair were moved across Lake Michigan to Indiana after the exposition. Their futuristic materials and designs survive along the lakeshore in Indiana Dunes National Park; exteriors can be viewed year-round, while interior tours are normally limited to special events.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/century-of-progress-architectural-district', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Cerro Gordo Ghost Town', 'cerro-gordo-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 36.537743, -117.79506, 'Lone Pine', 'CA', 'A silver, lead and zinc town high in the Inyo Mountains from the 1860s, holding an unusually complete set of mining structures. The whole townsite is privately owned and reached up a steep eight-mile dirt road — follow the owner''s current visiting rules rather than treating it as open ground.', 'limited', null, 'https://lonepinechamber.org/sightseeing-in-the-lone-pine-area/ghost-towns/', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Chef Boyardee''s Grave', 'chef-boyardees-grave', 'weird-history', 41.59212, -81.26771, 'Chardon', 'OH', 'Hector Boiardi, the Italian-born chef whose name became the Chef Boyardee brand, is entombed in the Crucifixion Mausoleum at All Souls Cemetery. Visitors can find his crypt in the Sacred Heart aisle during cemetery and mausoleum access hours, but this remains an active burial place and should be visited respectfully.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/grave-of-chef-boyardee', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Chief Menominee Monument and Trail of Death Site', 'chief-menominee-monument-and-trail-of-death-site', 'weird-history', 41.29565, -86.36177, 'Plymouth', 'IN', 'A 17-foot granite memorial marks the homeland of Potawatomi leader Menominee and the starting area associated with the forced 1838 removal remembered as the Potawatomi Trail of Death. The monument was dedicated in 1909 and is significant as an early government-funded memorial to a Native American leader.', 'open', null, 'https://www.visitmarshallcounty.in/history-culture', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Church Hill Tunnel Eastern Portal', 'church-hill-tunnel-eastern-portal', 'weird-history', 37.52719, -77.41489, 'Richmond', 'VA', 'The Church Hill railroad tunnel catastrophically collapsed on October 2, 1925 while crews were attempting to reopen it, entombing a locomotive and an uncertain number of workers underground. The tunnel was sealed and remains unsafe and inaccessible; only view the surviving portal area from legal public ground and never attempt to enter.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.rva.gov/press-releases-and-announcements/news/city-commemorates-church-hill-tunnel-collapse', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cincinnati Subway', 'cincinnati-subway', 'weird-history', 39.13663, -84.53281, 'Cincinnati', 'OH', 'Cincinnati began building an underground rapid-transit system in the 1920s using the former Miami and Erie Canal route, but the project was abandoned before any trains ever ran. Sections of tunnel and four unfinished stations still survive beneath the city, but official tours ended years ago and the sealed tunnels are illegal and unsafe to enter; record this as a closed historical stop only.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-cincinnati-subway-cincinnati-ohio', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('City West Ghost Town', 'city-west-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 41.6632, -87.06315, 'Chesterton', 'IN', 'City West was platted on the Lake Michigan shore in the 1830s with ambitions of becoming a major city and port. The Panic of 1837 helped kill the development, and shifting dunes eventually swallowed nearly every trace; the former townsite is now within Indiana Dunes State Park.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/city-west-ghost-town', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Clopper Mill Ruins', 'clopper-mill-ruins', 'weird-history', 39.15313, -77.25369, 'Germantown', 'MD', 'A mill operated at this Seneca Creek location from the 18th century until the surviving structure burned in 1947, leaving picturesque stone walls beside the water. The area also has a Lincoln-assassination connection through conspirator George Atzerodt, who was familiar with and sought refuge around the region; reaching the ruins involves park trails and uneven ground.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ruins-of-clopper-mill', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Concrete City', 'concrete-city', 'weird-history', 41.18852, -75.97528, 'Hanover Township', 'PA', 'Twenty reinforced-concrete houses were built here in 1911 as experimental company housing for coal workers, then abandoned little more than a decade later. The roofless shells still stand in the woods near Nanticoke, but reaching them requires walking from the public access area and the structures are deteriorated, so do not climb unstable walls or enter restricted land.', 'limited', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concrete_City', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Constitution Elm', 'constitution-elm', 'weird-history', 38.21348, -86.12734, 'Corydon', 'IN', 'Delegates drafting Indiana''s first state constitution met beneath a huge elm in Corydon in 1816 because the territorial capitol building was too hot. The tree died in 1925, but its enormous preserved trunk remains under a protective sandstone shelter at the historic site.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/constitution-elm', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Daniels Ghost Town', 'daniels-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 39.31677, -76.81741, 'Ellicott City', 'MD', 'Daniels grew around a textile mill on the Patapsco River before the mill closed in the 1960s and Tropical Storm Agnes devastated the remaining community in 1972. Today hikers can find foundations, cemetery remnants and other traces of the vanished mill town inside the Patapsco Valley area.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/daniels', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Deep Throat Parking Garage Marker', 'deep-throat-parking-garage-marker', 'weird-history', 38.89601, -77.07308, 'Arlington', 'VA', 'During the Watergate investigation in 1972 and 1973, reporter Bob Woodward secretly met FBI official Mark Felt, later confirmed as "Deep Throat," in an underground garage in Rosslyn. A historical marker installed outside the complex in 2008 identifies the site; the garage remains an active parking facility, so OddWay visitors should use the exterior marker rather than wander through private parking levels.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/deep-throat-parking-garage', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Devil''s Hole Ruins', 'devils-hole-ruins', 'weird-history', 41.1403, -75.336, 'Paradise Township', 'PA', 'Deep in State Game Lands 221 are stone fireplaces, foundations and mechanical remnants from a large building whose exact purpose remains disputed, with stories ranging from a ski lodge to a Prohibition-era speakeasy. Reaching the ruins requires a secluded hike with multiple stream crossings, and hunters use the surrounding state game lands seasonally.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/devils-hole-ruins', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dingess Tunnel', 'dingess-tunnel', 'weird-history', 37.86902, -82.17847, 'Dingess', 'WV', 'The 3,327-foot Dingess Tunnel opened in 1892 as part of the Norfolk & Western Railway and later became a one-lane county-road tunnel after the rail route was abandoned. It was substantially rehabilitated in 2019 with lighting, drainage and paving, and travelers can still drive through this unusually long former railroad bore today.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wvencyclopedia.org/entries/1867', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dinosaur Park Fossil Site', 'dinosaur-park-fossil-site', 'weird-history', 39.0708, -76.86861, 'Laurel', 'MD', 'This protected Early Cretaceous fossil site preserves one of the most important dinosaur deposits in the eastern United States, including material from Maryland''s state dinosaur, Astrodon. The fenced fossil area is only opened during scheduled public programs and dig experiences, although the surrounding playground and garden have broader access.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.pgparks.com/parks_trails/dinosaur-park', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Doodletown Ghost Town', 'doodletown-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 41.29596, -73.9916, 'Stony Point', 'NY', 'Doodletown was a small Hudson Highlands settlement whose remaining residents left in the 1960s after the Palisades Interstate Park Commission acquired the property. House foundations, roads, cemeteries and interpretive signs remain in the woods, reached only by hiking trails inside Bear Mountain State Park.', 'limited', null, 'https://parks.ny.gov/sites/default/files/BearMountainSuggestedHikes.pdf', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Double Parking Meter Tombstone', 'double-parking-meter-tombstone', 'weird-history', 41.24949, -84.83918, 'Harlan', 'IN', 'Archillous "Archie" Arnold''s grave in Scipio Cemetery is flanked by two old parking meters, both permanently reading "Expired." The intentionally comic memorial turns an ordinary rural cemetery visit into one of Indiana''s stranger examples of personalized grave art.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/75086', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Doumar''s Original Waffle Cone Machine', 'doumars-original-waffle-cone-machine', 'weird-history', 36.86616, -76.28485, 'Norfolk', 'VA', 'Doumar''s still uses the original-style four-iron waffle machine associated with founder Abe Doumar, who helped popularize the rolled waffle ice-cream cone at the 1904 St. Louis World''s Fair. The century-old drive-in remains in business, and visitors can often watch cones being made on the historic machine while ordering from the restaurant.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/doumar-s-barbecue', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dr. Samuel A. Mudd House Museum', 'dr-samuel-a-mudd-house-museum', 'weird-history', 38.60958, -76.8262, 'Waldorf', 'MD', 'Dr. Samuel Mudd treated John Wilkes Booth''s broken leg here after Lincoln''s assassination, helping make the farmhouse one of the most notorious stops on Booth''s escape route. The privately owned historic property operates as a seasonal museum on selected days rather than daily.', 'limited', null, 'https://drmudd.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Drake Well Museum and Park', 'drake-well-museum-and-park', 'weird-history', 41.61128, -79.65827, 'Titusville', 'PA', 'Edwin Drake''s successful 1859 oil well at this site helped launch the modern petroleum industry. The museum preserves a replica well house, operating historic oil-field equipment and exhibits explaining the chaotic oil boom that transformed northwestern Pennsylvania.', 'open', null, 'https://www.drakewell.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Eckley Miners'' Village', 'eckley-miners-village', 'weird-history', 40.99525, -75.85606, 'Foster Township', 'PA', 'Eckley is a remarkably intact nineteenth-century anthracite company town with miners'' houses, churches, a company store and other surviving structures. The village itself can be walked or driven through from dawn to dusk, while the museum and building interiors follow posted hours.', 'open', null, 'https://eckleyminersvillage.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Edgar Allan Poe Grave', 'edgar-allan-poe-grave', 'weird-history', 39.29027, -76.62333, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Edgar Allan Poe was buried at Westminster Burying Ground after his mysterious death in Baltimore in 1849, then moved to the prominent monument near the cemetery entrance in 1875. Visitors can see both the monument and his original burial place inside the historic graveyard.', 'open', null, 'https://www.westminsterhall.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Edgar Cayce A.R.E. Headquarters', 'edgar-cayce-are-headquarters', 'weird-history', 36.8928, -75.98994, 'Virginia Beach', 'VA', 'Psychic Edgar Cayce and his supporters founded the Association for Research and Enlightenment in 1931 to preserve and study material from his thousands of claimed psychic readings. The Virginia Beach headquarters now includes a large metaphysical library, bookstore, meditation garden, historic hospital building and public programs on Cayce''s work.', 'open', null, 'https://edgarcayce.org/about-us/our-organization/', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://edgarcayce.org/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Evans City Cemetery — Night of the Living Dead', 'evans-city-cemetery-night-of-the-living-dead', 'weird-history', 40.76239, -80.064, 'Evans City', 'PA', 'The opening cemetery sequence in George A. Romero''s 1968 Night of the Living Dead was filmed here, including the first zombie attack on Johnny and Barbra. The cemetery is still active and open to respectful visitors, so stay on cemetery roads and paths and avoid disturbing graves while looking for recognizable filming locations.', 'open', null, 'https://filmoblivion.com/2021/10/20/night-of-the-living-dead-1968/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('F. Scott and Zelda Fitzgerald Graves', 'f-scott-and-zelda-fitzgerald-graves', 'weird-history', 39.082, -77.14536, 'Rockville', 'MD', 'F. Scott Fitzgerald and Zelda Fitzgerald are buried together in the small cemetery at St. Mary''s Catholic Church, beneath a stone engraved with the final line of The Great Gatsby. The graves are easy to visit from the church property but should be treated as an active cemetery rather than a roadside photo prop.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/location/md/all', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fernald Preserve Visitors Center', 'fernald-preserve-visitors-center', 'weird-history', 39.28805, -84.68354, 'Hamilton', 'OH', 'The Fernald site produced uranium metal for the U.S. nuclear weapons program during the Cold War before shutting down production in 1989 and undergoing a massive environmental cleanup. It is now a Department of Energy nature preserve, and the free visitor center contains exhibits on uranium production, contamination, remediation and the site''s transformation into public trails and habitat.', 'open', null, 'https://www.energy.gov/lm/fernald-preserve-ohio-site', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('First Washington Monument', 'first-washington-monument', 'weird-history', 39.50047, -77.62315, 'Middletown', 'MD', 'Boonsboro residents climbed South Mountain on July 4, 1827 and built a rough stone tower honoring George Washington, making it the first completed monument to Washington in the country. The rebuilt tower stands inside Washington Monument State Park and requires a short uphill walk from the parking area.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/first-washington-monument', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fort Armistead', 'fort-armistead', 'weird-history', 39.20929, -76.53368, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Built around the turn of the 20th century as part of Baltimore''s coastal-defense system, Fort Armistead later became an abandoned military battery inside a public park. The concrete emplacements are heavily weathered and graffitied; stay in legitimate public areas and do not enter unsafe tunnels, sealed spaces or restricted sections.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/fort-armistead', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fort Lincoln Cemetery', 'fort-lincoln-cemetery', 'weird-history', 38.93048, -76.95672, 'Brentwood', 'MD', 'This large active cemetery occupies land with layers of history that include Civil War-era Fort Lincoln earthworks, an old spring house, monuments and a sprawling mausoleum complex. Visitors can see the historic features during cemetery hours but should stay on cemetery roads and treat active burial areas respectfully.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/fort-lincoln-cemetery', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fort Roberdeau', 'fort-roberdeau', 'weird-history', 40.58272, -78.27379, 'Tyrone Township', 'PA', 'Fort Roberdeau reconstructs a Revolutionary War-era lead-mining fort built in 1778 to protect local mining operations. The palisade, cabins and grounds can be explored during its seasonal tour season, while the exterior grounds remain visible outside normal interior-tour hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://fortroberdeau.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Forts Ferry', 'forts-ferry', 'weird-history', 42.787988, -73.793012, 'Clifton Park', 'NY', 'One of the earliest European settlement sites in what is now Clifton Park, where Nicholas Fort ran a rope ferry across the Mohawk from 1728. It sits inside the public Vischer Ferry Nature and Historic Preserve, with a mile-and-a-half historic trail to the ferry site, the Fort homestead foundation and interpretive panels.', 'open', null, 'https://cliftonparkny.gov/document-center/open-space/3063-vischer-ferry-nature-and-historic-preserve-booklet-2002/file', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Franklin Ghost Town', 'franklin-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 47.297998, -121.95874, 'Black Diamond', 'WA', 'A coal settlement from the 1880s, and the scene of an 1894 mine fire that killed thirty-seven men before operations largely ended in 1919. A 2.5-mile round trip now passes a coal cart, a sealed shaft, the powerhouse foundation and the cemetery. Trail parking is on a private field and costs five dollars a person.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.wta.org/go-hiking/hikes/franklin-ghost-town', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Garnet Ghost Town', 'garnet-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 46.825141, -113.339388, 'Clinton', 'MT', 'A gold camp that reached around a thousand residents in the 1890s and dwindled as the gold ran out. The BLM keeps it as one of Montana''s best-preserved ghost towns, with historic buildings and a seasonal visitor centre. Ten dollars for visitors sixteen and over; the last roads are unpaved and winter access is over snow only.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/garnet-ghost-town', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Ghost Church at Polegreen', 'ghost-church-at-polegreen', 'weird-history', 37.6452, -77.32927, 'Mechanicsville', 'VA', 'Polegreen Church was destroyed by Confederate artillery in 1864 during the Civil War. In 2012, a stark white framework was erected on the footprint of the vanished meetinghouse, creating a skeletal "Ghost Church" that visitors can walk around during daylight hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/59428', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://historicpolegreen.org/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghost Town', 'ghost-town', 'weird-history', 36.011137, -114.945574, 'Henderson', 'NV', 'This Henderson entry appears to be tied to an old or temporary western ghost-town-style attraction rather than a currently documented permanent destination. I could not verify a public attraction operating here now, so the record should be removed or held unpublished until the exact coordinates and current operator are confirmed.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/way/1377065863', null, null, null, null, 'way', 1377065863, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Ghost Town', 'ghost-town-2', 'weird-history', 40.958415, -83.671578, 'Eagle Township', 'OH', 'An OpenStreetMap-derived tourist-attraction record called Ghost Town exists in Eagle Township, but there is almost no current public information explaining what visitors would actually find there. It should not be routed as an active attraction until its ownership, access and purpose are independently verified.', 'closed', null, 'https://mapcarta.com/W421738252', null, null, null, null, 'way', 421738252, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghost Town of Clara', 'ghost-town-of-clara', 'weird-history', 34.09176, -98.69693, 'Burkburnett', 'TX', 'This is a Texas historical marker telling the story of Clara, a former German settlement near Burkburnett, rather than a preserved ghost town with buildings to explore. The marker is a roadside stop, although the Texas Historical Commission currently indicates that the physical marker is being replaced, so travelers may temporarily find no plaque on site.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://atlas.thc.texas.gov/Details/5485002180', null, 'node', 12453787783, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Ghost Town of Cotton Gin', 'ghost-town-of-cotton-gin', 'weird-history', 31.68067, -96.35993, 'Teague', 'TX', 'Settled before 1848 around Dr J. S. Wills'' mule-powered cotton gin, growing to support churches, a school, a newspaper, stores and saloons. The businesses went when the railroad bypassed it in the 1870s. What stands now is a Texas historical marker explaining a settlement that is no longer there.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/Details/5161009870', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Ghost Town of White Hills', 'ghost-town-of-white-hills', 'weird-history', 35.700322, -114.474416, 'Dolan Springs', 'AZ', 'A short-lived silver boomtown of the 1890s that vanished when mining declined. Essentially nothing of the town remains, but historical markers at US 93 and White Hills Road explain the settlement and point toward the old district. Active and private mine areas should not be entered.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=31880', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Ghost Town Pahreah Old Cellar', 'ghost-town-pahreah-old-cellar', 'weird-history', 37.24808, -111.952794, 'Kanab', 'UT', 'A cellar remnant within the abandoned Pahreah townsite, settled by Mormon pioneers in 1865 and given up after repeated flooding along the Paria River. A five-mile dirt road reaches the wider site, where there are foundations, artefacts and a cemetery. One feature of a larger place rather than a separate stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/glca/planyourvisit/day-hikes.htm', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Ghost Town Pahreah Old Chimney', 'ghost-town-pahreah-old-chimney', 'weird-history', 37.247594, -111.952313, 'Kanab', 'UT', 'Another surviving feature of the same Pahreah townsite, where settlement began in 1865 and recurring floods eventually drove everyone out. Same dirt-road approach as the rest of the site, and road and river conditions change quickly after rain.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/paria-movie-set-day-use-site', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Ghost Town Tours', 'ghost-town-tours', 'weird-history', 34.750699, -112.116606, 'Clarkdale', 'AZ', 'Ghost Town Tours offers guided walks through Jerome focused on the former mining town''s colorful history, old buildings, local legends and paranormal stories. Visitors should expect a scheduled tour rather than a self-guided attraction, so advance booking is the safest way to visit.', 'limited', null, 'https://ghosttowntours.org/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://ghosttowntours.org/', null, 'node', 9953774076, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Ghost Town Village', 'ghost-town-village', 'weird-history', 35.526815, -83.103619, 'Maggie Valley', 'NC', 'Ghost Town Village, better known as Ghost Town in the Sky, was a mountaintop Wild West amusement park overlooking Maggie Valley. The park has been closed for years and the property is not a normal public sightseeing stop, so it should be removed from active routing unless the site officially reopens.', 'closed', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghost_Town_Village', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'way', 1092172492, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ghost Town Wild West Museum', 'ghost-town-wild-west-museum', 'weird-history', 38.840433, -104.860859, 'Colorado Springs', 'CO', 'Ghost Town Museum is an indoor Colorado Springs museum built around preserved Old West storefronts, rooms, wagons and artifacts rescued from the Pikes Peak region. Despite the name, it is a western-history museum rather than a paranormal attraction, with hands-on exhibits and seasonal gold panning.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ghosttownmuseum.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.ghosttownmuseum.com', null, 'way', 130923480, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Gilbert Ghost Town', 'gilbert-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 48.457381, -120.562214, 'Okanogan County', 'WA', 'A small mining camp in the North Creek drainage of Okanogan County during the late-nineteenth-century boom, reportedly about a dozen buildings at its peak. A cabin, partial ruins, foundations and mining traces remain deep in the Cascade backcountry near the Gilbert Trailhead. No staffed attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://washingtonstate.fandom.com/wiki/Gilbert', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Gold King Mine Ghost Town', 'gold-king-mine-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 34.75655, -112.130827, 'Jerome', 'AZ', 'The camp began around 1890 north of Jerome, when miners looking for copper struck gold in a 1,270-foot shaft. The present attraction dates from 1982 and holds historic shafts, over a hundred vintage vehicles, mining equipment and a working sawmill. Admission charged, closed Tuesdays.', 'limited', null, 'https://goldkingmineghosttown.com/', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Goldfield Ghost Town', 'goldfield-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 33.45733, -111.491847, 'Apache Junction', 'AZ', 'The original Goldfield boomed beside the Mammoth Mine in the 1890s and faded when the ore body disappointed. Bob and Lou Ann Schoose rebuilt the site from the 1980s as a commercial Old West attraction: shops, museum, mine tour, narrow-gauge train, gold panning and staged gunfights.', 'open', null, 'https://goldfieldghosttown.com/', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Goodwin', 'goodwin', 'weird-history', 34.355719, -112.380399, 'Mayer', 'AZ', 'Established in 1882 after the Nonsuch Mining Company bought the Goodwin Mine and built a mill and smelter, later serving as hotel, stage stop, store and supply centre. Almost nothing survives beyond sparse foundations and a sign on Senator Highway.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.arizonahighways.com/archive/issues/chapter/Doc.705.Chapter.6', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Goodyear Airdock', 'goodyear-airdock', 'weird-history', 41.03194, -81.47083, 'Akron', 'OH', 'Completed in 1929, the Goodyear Airdock was built to construct and house enormous lighter-than-air craft and was once one of the world''s largest buildings without interior supports. The industrial facility is not a public attraction, but the immense black hangar can be viewed from surrounding public roads without entering the secured property.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/goodyear-airdock', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Belgum (Grande Vista) Sanitarium Ruins', 'grande-vista-sanitarium', 'weird-history', 37.949607, -122.308551, 'Richmond', 'CA', 'The Grande Vista, later known as Belgum Sanitarium, closed in the 1960s and its main buildings were destroyed by fire. Today hikers in Wildcat Canyon Regional Park can find remnants such as foundations, stonework and old landscaping along the former sanitarium grounds.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ebparks.org/parks/wildcat-canyon', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 2640323068, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Grave Creek Mound Archaeological Complex', 'grave-creek-mound-archaeological-complex', 'weird-history', 39.91686, -80.74472, 'Moundsville', 'WV', 'Built by Adena people around 250–150 B.C., Grave Creek Mound is one of the largest surviving conical burial mounds of its culture and required the movement of tens of thousands of tons of earth. A free state museum beside the mound interprets West Virginia archaeology and the people who built it.', 'open', null, 'https://wvculture.org/explore/grave-creek-mound/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Grave of Doctor Pepper', 'grave-of-doctor-pepper', 'weird-history', 36.89056, -81.28028, 'Rural Retreat', 'VA', 'Dr. Charles T. Pepper is buried in Mountain View Cemetery, and a long-running local story connects him to the naming of the Dr Pepper soft drink through pharmacist Wade Morrison. The exact origin of the beverage''s name remains disputed, but the grave gives travelers a physical stop for one of Virginia''s most persistent soda-history stories.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/9262', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Greenbrier Congressional Bunker', 'greenbrier-congressional-bunker', 'weird-history', 37.78456, -80.30886, 'White Sulphur Springs', 'WV', 'Hidden beneath the Greenbrier resort during the Cold War, Project Greek Island was a massive fallout shelter designed to house the entire United States Congress after a nuclear attack. Its existence was exposed publicly in 1992, and the declassified bunker can now be visited only on scheduled guided tours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.greenbrier.com/activities/bunker-tours/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Greenbrier County Courthouse', 'greenbrier-county-courthouse', 'weird-history', 37.80323, -80.44514, 'Lewisburg', 'WV', 'This is the courthouse where Erasmus Shue was tried for the 1897 murder of his wife Zona, the crime at the center of the Greenbrier Ghost legend. The building remains a functioning courthouse, so it is a legitimate historical stop rather than a paranormal attraction and visitors should behave accordingly during business hours.', 'open', null, 'https://greenbrierwv.com/places/greenbrier-county-courthouse', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Griffith & Feil Soda Fountain', 'griffith-feil-soda-fountain', 'weird-history', 38.39953, -82.57819, 'Kenova', 'WV', 'Griffith & Feil traces its pharmacy roots to 1892 and still operates an old-fashioned soda fountain inside the working business. Visitors can sit at the counter for ice cream and diner food while surrounded by a surviving piece of small-town pharmacy history.', 'open', null, 'https://gfsodafountain.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hank Williams Death Monument', 'hank-williams-death-monument', 'weird-history', 37.97603, -81.14121, 'Oak Hill', 'WV', 'A small monument in Oak Hill marks the city where driver Charles Carr discovered that country singer Hank Williams had died in the back seat of his Cadillac on New Year''s Day 1953. The marker gives travelers a physical stop tied to one of American music''s most famous and grim road-trip stories.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wvencyclopedia.org/entries/2277', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Harry Houdini''s Grave', 'harry-houdinis-grave', 'weird-history', 40.69344, -73.8848, 'Queens', 'NY', 'Escape artist Harry Houdini is buried beneath a distinctive monument in Machpelah Cemetery, where magicians and fans have gathered for decades around the anniversary of his Halloween 1926 death. The grave can be visited during cemetery hours, but this is an active burial ground and should be treated respectfully.', 'open', null, 'https://houdinimuseum.wordpress.com/2013/02/05/houdini-grave-aerial-map/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hart Island', 'hart-island', 'weird-history', 40.85326, -73.77044, 'Bronx', 'NY', 'New York City has used Hart Island as its public cemetery for more than a century, burying more than a million people there in mass and individual graves. The island is not freely accessible, but NYC Parks now offers limited public ranger visits and scheduled gravesite visits using the city ferry.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nyc.gov/site/hartisland/hart-island/visitation.page', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hawks Nest Tunnel Disaster Overlook', 'hawks-nest-tunnel-disaster-overlook', 'weird-history', 38.12267, -81.12752, 'Ansted', 'WV', 'From the Hawks Nest State Park overlook area, visitors can follow interpretation connected with the three-mile tunnel whose construction exposed thousands of workers to dangerous silica dust beginning in 1930. The National Park Service directs visitors here as a formal stop for understanding the disaster.', 'open', null, 'https://home.nps.gov/places/hawks-nest-tunnel-disaster.htm', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hawks Nest Workers Memorial and Grave Site', 'hawks-nest-workers-memorial-and-grave-site', 'weird-history', 38.23447, -80.85269, 'Lookout', 'WV', 'This memorial marks the burial area associated with African American workers who died after being exposed to enormous concentrations of silica dust during construction of the Hawks Nest Tunnel in the early 1930s. The National Park Service describes the project as one of America''s worst industrial tragedies.', 'open', null, 'https://home.nps.gov/places/hawks-nest-workers-memorial-and-grave-site.htm', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hillandale Bridge', 'hillandale-bridge', 'weird-history', 41.59097, -81.49117, 'Euclid', 'OH', 'This abandoned concrete bridge was built for a 1920s residential development that never materialized, leaving a substantial bridge standing alone in the woods. It can be reached from trails in the Hillandale Park area, but the structure is weathered and damaged, so visitors should stay on established legal access routes and avoid climbing unsafe sections.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/hillandale-bridge', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hindostan Falls Ghost Town', 'hindostan-falls-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 38.6245, -86.85083, 'Shoals', 'IN', 'Hindostan was once a promising early Indiana settlement on the White River before disease and economic decline emptied the community in the 1820s. Little of the town survives today, but the public recreation area at Hindostan Falls preserves the landscape and remnants associated with one of the state''s earliest ghost towns.', 'open', null, 'https://www.in.gov/dnr/fish-and-wildlife/properties/hindostan-falls-public-fishing-area/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Vincennes'),
  ('Historic Pithole City', 'historic-pithole-city', 'weird-history', 41.52089, -79.58699, 'Cornplanter Township', 'PA', 'Pithole exploded into a booming oil town after nearby wells struck petroleum in 1865 and collapsed almost as quickly when the boom moved elsewhere. Little of the original city remains above ground, but paths, foundations, interpretation and a seasonal visitor center preserve one of Pennsylvania''s most dramatic ghost towns.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.drakewell.org/plan-your-visit/what-to-see-and-do', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hollensbury Spite House', 'hollensbury-spite-house', 'weird-history', 38.80731, -77.04506, 'Alexandria', 'VA', 'John Hollensbury built this exceptionally narrow house in 1830 to fill an alley beside his home, reportedly after growing tired of people and wagons using the passage. The roughly seven-foot-wide residence still stands at 523 Queen Street, but it is a private home and should be viewed only from the public sidewalk.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/hollensbury-spite-house', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hollow Earth Monument', 'hollow-earth-monument', 'weird-history', 39.39477, -84.56241, 'Hamilton', 'OH', 'This unusual monument marks the grave of John Cleves Symmes Jr., the nineteenth-century Army officer who argued that the Earth was hollow and accessible through enormous openings near the poles. His son erected the stone topped with a hollow globe, and it remains publicly accessible in Hamilton''s Ludlow Park.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/hollow-earth-monument', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hooper', 'hooper', 'weird-history', 34.26614, -112.382945, 'Mayer', 'AZ', 'A camp in the same Yavapai County district as the earlier settlement of Meesville, whose buildings were reportedly moved here when mining revived around 1900. No developed attraction and no well-documented surviving structures — a remote locality on the Senator Highway corridor.', 'limited', null, 'https://azgw.org/yavapai/ghosttowns.html', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Hotel Victory Ruins', 'hotel-victory-ruins', 'weird-history', 41.64556, -82.83816, 'Put-in-Bay', 'OH', 'The enormous Hotel Victory opened on South Bass Island in the 1890s and burned in 1919, leaving behind foundations, portions of its pool and scattered structural remains. The ruins lie around South Bass Island State Park''s campground area, and some are within camper-only sections, so visitors should follow park access rules rather than wandering through occupied campsites.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/hotel-victory-ruins', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Howard Tunnel', 'howard-tunnel', 'weird-history', 39.89148, -76.7496, 'North Codorus Township', 'PA', 'Built in the 1830s, Howard Tunnel is one of the oldest surviving railroad tunnels in the United States and remains part of an active rail corridor. The York County Heritage Rail Trail passes beside and through the historic corridor, so visitors should use the designated trail and never walk on the active tracks.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/howard-tunnel', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Humpback Covered Bridge', 'humpback-covered-bridge', 'weird-history', 37.80054, -80.04711, 'Covington', 'VA', 'Built in 1857, this wooden bridge arches noticeably higher at its center than at either end, giving it the humpback profile that makes it unique. It is Virginia''s oldest surviving covered bridge and now stands in a public wayside park where travelers can walk through it rather than drive across it.', 'open', null, 'https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/va0239/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Indianapolis Moon Tree', 'indianapolis-moon-tree', 'weird-history', 39.7683, -86.162, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'This sycamore grew from a seed carried around the Moon aboard Apollo 14 in 1971 as part of astronaut Stuart Roosa''s famous seed experiment. Planted in Indianapolis during the U.S. Bicentennial era, it is one of the surviving "Moon Trees" scattered across the country.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/indianapolis-moon-tree', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('International Mother''s Day Shrine', 'international-mothers-day-shrine', 'weird-history', 39.34073, -80.01854, 'Grafton', 'WV', 'The former Andrews Methodist Episcopal Church hosted the first official Mother''s Day observance on May 10, 1908 after Anna Jarvis began campaigning for a holiday honoring mothers. The 1873 church became the International Mother''s Day Shrine in 1962 and now operates as a seasonal historic attraction and museum.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.internationalmothersdayshrine.org/about-us', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('J Lorraine, Texas Ghost Town', 'j-lorraine-texas-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 30.332325, -97.509487, 'Manor', 'TX', 'J. Lorraine Ghost Town is a recreated Old West roadside attraction outside Austin, built with western storefronts, props and rustic structures meant to evoke a fictional frontier settlement. It is a playful man-made ghost town rather than an authentically abandoned community, with access depending on the property''s posted hours and events.', 'limited', null, 'https://ghosttownaustin.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'http://www.ghosttownaustin.com', '+1-512-922-2683', 'way', 962329436, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('James Dean''s Grave', 'james-deans-grave', 'weird-history', 40.43309, -85.64503, 'Fairmount', 'IN', 'James Dean was returned to his hometown after his fatal 1955 automobile crash and buried in Park Cemetery north of Fairmount. Fans still visit the simple headstone, often leaving small memorial items or lipstick marks, making the cemetery one of the most enduring pilgrimage sites connected to the actor.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/460', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://showmegrantcounty.com/park-cemetery/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('James Rumsey Monument', 'james-rumsey-monument', 'weird-history', 39.43288, -77.79913, 'Shepherdstown', 'WV', 'This 75-foot monument honors inventor James Rumsey, who demonstrated an early steam-powered boat on the Potomac River at Shepherdstown in 1787. The monument stands in a public park overlooking the river and marks one of America''s lesser-known early experiments with steam navigation.', 'open', null, 'https://www.canaltrust.org/pyv/james-rumsey-monument-and-park/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jean Baptiste Charbonneau Grave', 'jean-baptiste-charbonneau-grave', 'weird-history', 42.951943, -117.339185, 'Danner', 'OR', 'The infant who travelled with Sacagawea and the Lewis and Clark expedition died near Inskip Station in 1866, taken ill crossing the Owyhee country. His grave was rediscovered in the twentieth century, dedicated in 1971 and listed on the National Register in 1973. The signed site is reached by gravel road southwest of Jordan Valley — in Oregon, not Idaho.', 'limited', null, 'https://traveloregon.com/things-to-do/culture-history/historic-sites-oregon-trail/jean-baptiste-charbonneau-grave-site/', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('John Dillinger''s Grave', 'john-dillingers-grave', 'weird-history', 39.82212, -86.16484, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'Bank robber John Dillinger was killed by federal agents in Chicago in 1934 and returned to Indianapolis for burial in Crown Hill Cemetery. His granite grave has long attracted visitors interested in Depression-era outlaw history and has reportedly been replaced or repaired after decades of souvenir damage.', 'open', null, 'https://thetombstonetourist.com/graves/john-dillinger/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('John Paul Jones Crypt', 'john-paul-jones-crypt', 'weird-history', 38.98069, -76.48184, 'Annapolis', 'MD', 'Revolutionary War naval hero John Paul Jones died in Paris in 1792, disappeared beneath a later development, and was rediscovered more than a century afterward before being returned to the United States. His ornate black-and-white marble sarcophagus now sits beneath the U.S. Naval Academy Chapel; visitors must follow Naval Academy identification and security rules.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/john-paul-jones-crypt', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('John Wilkes Booth Grave', 'john-wilkes-booth-grave', 'weird-history', 39.30711, -76.606, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Lincoln assassin John Wilkes Booth is buried in the Booth family plot at Green Mount Cemetery beneath a small, deliberately unremarkable marker. Visitors often leave pennies on the stone, but the cemetery is an active burial ground and should only be visited during its posted daytime hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/grave-of-john-wilkes-booth', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Julius Sturgis Pretzel Bakery', 'julius-sturgis-pretzel-bakery', 'weird-history', 40.15655, -76.3013, 'Lititz', 'PA', 'Julius Sturgis opened his commercial pretzel bakery here in 1861, and the historic stone building still operates as a visitor attraction. Guided bakery tours explain early pretzel making and let visitors try forming the traditional pretzel shape by hand.', 'open', null, 'https://juliussturgis.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Katherine Johnson Statue', 'katherine-johnson-statue', 'weird-history', 38.38023, -81.76765, 'Institute', 'WV', 'West Virginia State University unveiled this seven-foot bronze statue of NASA mathematician and alumna Katherine Johnson in 2018. It stands on the university campus as a public monument to the woman whose calculations helped make early American spaceflight possible.', 'open', null, 'https://wvstateu.edu/news/west-virginia-state-university-alumnus-creates-las/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kaymoor Mine Site', 'kaymoor-mine-site', 'weird-history', 38.04529, -81.06775, 'Fayetteville', 'WV', 'Kaymoor was one of the New River Gorge''s major coal operations, and its abandoned mine complex, coke ovens and town remains survive on the gorge wall. These coordinates route to the Kaymoor Top trailhead; reaching the mine requires a steep hike, and access conditions can change during trail rehabilitation.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/neri/learn/historyculture/visiting-kaymoor.htm', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kelleys Island Glacial Grooves', 'kelleys-island-glacial-grooves', 'weird-history', 41.61363, -82.70539, 'Kelleys Island', 'OH', 'A retreating Ice Age glacier carved enormous parallel grooves into the limestone of Kelleys Island, leaving some of the largest and most accessible glacial striations in the world. A walkway surrounds the protected geological feature, but reaching it requires travel to the Lake Erie island, with ferry service varying by season and weather.', 'limited', null, 'https://kelleysisland.com/listing/glacial-grooves/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kelleys Island Winery Ruins', 'kelleys-island-winery-ruins', 'weird-history', 41.60142, -82.72943, 'Kelleys Island', 'OH', 'Stone ruins from Kelleys Island''s nineteenth-century wine industry survive near Maple Drive, remnants of an era when Lake Erie islands were major American grape-growing centers. The ruins are on private property, so they should be viewed only from the public road without entering the site.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/kelleys-island-winery-ruins', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kerr Lock Ruins', 'kerr-lock-ruins', 'weird-history', 40.83718, -85.72538, 'Lagro', 'IN', 'Stone remains beside the Wabash River preserve part of a lock from the Wabash and Erie Canal, once one of the longest canal systems in North America. A public trail now passes the nineteenth-century masonry, allowing travelers to inspect infrastructure from a transportation network that almost completely disappeared.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/kerr-lock', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Killiansburg Cave', 'killiansburg-cave', 'weird-history', 39.45879, -77.79609, 'Sharpsburg', 'MD', 'During the Battle of Antietam, local civilians reportedly sheltered beneath this large rock overhang along the Potomac while fighting raged nearby. The site is reached from the C&O Canal towpath near mile 75.7 and requires walking plus a short climb away from the canal, so it is not a drive-up stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/killiansburg-cave', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kings Park Psychiatric Center at Nissequogue River State Park', 'kings-park-psychiatric-center-at-nissequogue-river-state-park', 'weird-history', 40.89593, -73.23956, 'Kings Park', 'NY', 'The former Kings Park Psychiatric Center grew into a sprawling institutional campus that held more than 9,000 patients at its peak before closing in 1996. Much of the property is now Nissequogue River State Park, where public roads and trails pass surviving hospital buildings; the abandoned structures themselves are unsafe and off-limits, so do not enter them.', 'open', null, 'https://apps.cio.ny.gov/apps/mediacontact/public/view.cfm?backButton=&parm=DBCB9EAF-BB2B-D983-D05568DCB12EB50B', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kiptopeke Concrete Fleet', 'kiptopeke-concrete-fleet', 'weird-history', 37.16463, -75.97825, 'Kiptopeke', 'VA', 'Nine concrete cargo ships built during World War II were deliberately sunk off Kiptopeke in 1948 to form a protective breakwater for the former ferry terminal. Their decaying hulls still rise from Chesapeake Bay and can be viewed from Kiptopeke State Park, with kayaks offering a closer look when conditions permit.', 'open', null, 'https://www.dcr.virginia.gov/state-parks/kiptopeke', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Knights of the Golden Horseshoe Pyramid', 'knights-of-the-golden-horseshoe-pyramid', 'weird-history', 38.35781, -78.54741, 'Elkton', 'VA', 'A stone pyramid placed at Swift Run Gap in 1921 commemorates Governor Alexander Spotswood''s 1716 expedition across the Blue Ridge, later romanticized as the Knights of the Golden Horseshoe. The roadside monument preserves that colonial legend, although claims that the party "discovered" the region ignore Indigenous occupation and earlier European travel through the area.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/knights-of-the-golden-horseshoe-markers', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Laurel Hill Cemetery', 'laurel-hill-cemetery', 'weird-history', 40.00483, -75.19018, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Laurel Hill opened in 1836 as one of America''s early rural cemeteries and became a landscape of elaborate mausoleums, sculptures and graves of prominent Philadelphians. The cemetery welcomes self-guided visitors every day and also hosts historical, architectural and macabre-themed tours and events.', 'open', null, 'https://thelaurelhillcemetery.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lawrence Park Dinor', 'lawrence-park-dinor', 'weird-history', 42.15071, -80.01431, 'Lawrence Park Township', 'PA', 'This prefabricated Silk City "dinor" arrived in Lawrence Park in 1948 and retains much of its original mid-century diner architecture. It is listed on the National Register, still serves breakfast and lunch, and preserves the peculiar **dinor-with-an-o** spelling that became a Northwestern Pennsylvania tradition.', 'open', null, 'https://www.eriereader.com/article/prefab-but-uniquely-erie', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, 'https://www.thelpdinor.com/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Leadfield', 'leadfield', 'weird-history', 36.848316, -117.060807, 'Beatty', 'NV', 'The boom lasted under a year in 1926-27, after aggressive promotion pulled miners and investors into Titus Canyon and poor ore collapsed the whole thing. A few shacks, workings and ruins remain along the one-way Titus Canyon Road — which is scheduled to close from October 2026 to September 2027 for repairs.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/deva/planyourvisit/titus-canyon.htm', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Leefe', 'leefe', 'weird-history', 41.811762, -111.024733, 'Kemmerer', 'WY', 'A phosphate mining and processing locality in western Wyoming — not Utah, despite the nearest town being over the line. The Leefe Mine ran from 1947 until Wyoming phosphate production ended in 1977. The mine and plant area lies about thirty miles west of Kemmerer and is not maintained for visitors; do not enter old workings or industrial property.', 'limited', null, 'https://main.wsgs.wyo.gov/mineral-resources/industrial-minerals/phosphate', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Leo Petroglyph', 'leo-petroglyph', 'weird-history', 39.15091, -82.67472, 'Ray', 'OH', 'The Leo Petroglyph contains dozens of prehistoric figures carved into a sandstone outcrop, including humans, animals and abstract forms associated with Indigenous people of the region. A protective shelter covers the carvings and the state historic site is accessible to visitors from the adjoining public area.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/leo-petroglyph', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Logan City', 'logan-city', 'weird-history', 37.609462, -115.393523, 'Hiko', 'NV', 'Founded after silver was found at Mount Irish in 1865, with a post office by 1867 and largely abandoned by 1869 once the shallow high-grade ore ran out. Only stone foundations remain in the Pahranagat district, on rough desert roads.', 'limited', null, 'https://eplanning.blm.gov/public_projects/lup/87546/128764/156632/Appendix_Q.pdf', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Lost Arch Historic Mining Camp', 'lost-arch-historic-mining-camp', 'weird-history', 34.436412, -114.824378, 'Needles', 'CA', 'A BLM-managed historic mining area in the remote Turtle Mountains, reached over roughly thirteen miles of backroads from US 95. You find an information kiosk, a mining landscape and primitive campsites rather than a reconstructed ghost town.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/lost-arch-historic-mining-camp', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Luther Elkins Petroglyphs', 'luther-elkins-petroglyphs', 'weird-history', 37.68156, -81.66492, 'Clear Fork', 'WV', 'These rock carvings are genuine Indigenous petroglyphs generally attributed to Native peoples of the region, although they became famous in the 1980s after fringe claims tried to reinterpret them as ancient Irish writing. The site is undeveloped and reached through rough terrain near private property; stay on the legitimate access route and never touch, chalk or trace the carvings.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/luther-elkins-petroglyphs', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Maconaquah''s Grave — Slocum Cemetery', 'maconaquahs-grave-slocum-cemetery', 'weird-history', 40.69852, -85.90759, 'Wabash', 'IN', 'This family cemetery contains the grave of Maconaquah, the Miami woman long known in American histories as Frances Slocum after she was taken from her Pennsylvania family as a child and raised among the Miami. She later chose to remain with her Miami family rather than return east, making the cemetery an important physical site for a complicated story often flattened into frontier folklore.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-slocum-cemetery', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Mad Anthony Wayne Blockhouse', 'mad-anthony-wayne-blockhouse', 'weird-history', 42.14003, -80.07432, 'Erie', 'PA', 'This reconstructed blockhouse marks the Fort Presque Isle site where Revolutionary War general Anthony Wayne died in 1796 and was first buried. When his son later came to move the body east, Wayne''s partially decomposed remains were boiled so the bones could be transported, leaving Erie associated with one of the strangest posthumous journeys in American military history; interior access is limited, but the grounds can be visited.', 'limited', null, 'https://historicsitemarkers.com/marker/anthony-wayne', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mallows Bay Ghost Fleet', 'mallows-bay-ghost-fleet', 'weird-history', 38.47195, -77.26863, 'Nanjemoy', 'MD', 'More than 100 wrecks from a fleet of World War I-era wooden steamships remain in and around Mallows Bay, forming one of the largest concentrations of shipwrecks in the Western Hemisphere. The best views come by kayak or other small craft from the public launch, though some remains can also be seen from shore and trails.', 'limited', null, 'https://dnr.maryland.gov/ccs/Pages/mallowsbay.aspx', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Market Street Catacombs', 'market-street-catacombs', 'weird-history', 39.76858, -86.15344, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'Beneath Indianapolis'' historic City Market lies roughly 20,000 square feet of brick and limestone passages once used for cool storage beneath the market halls. The catacombs have historically opened only for scheduled tours and were closed during City Market redevelopment, so access should be verified before OddWay routes a traveler inside.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/market-street-catacombs', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.indianalandmarks.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Marshall Hall Ruins', 'marshall-hall-ruins', 'weird-history', 38.68496, -77.09883, 'Accokeek', 'MD', 'The Marshall family built its Potomac River estate here in the 18th century, and the property later became a popular amusement park complete with rides and a roller coaster. The amusement park closed in 1979, but remnants of the old mansion and later recreational history survive within today''s Piscataway Park.', 'open', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/pisc/learn/historyculture/about-marshall-hall.htm', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Martin Augustine Mining Camp', 'martin-augustine-mining-camp', 'weird-history', 33.484085, -115.236058, 'Riverside County', 'CA', 'A remote mining locality near Augustine Pass, associated with the prospector Martin Augustine, photographed at his desert camp by the early 1930s. There is no attraction, museum or maintained buildings — treat it as backcountry mining history rather than a destination.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.parkrecord.com/2024/03/05/park-city-museum-puts-its-stamp-on-postcards-from-mecca/', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Matewan Massacre Historical Marker', 'matewan-massacre-historical-marker', 'weird-history', 37.62283, -82.1655, 'Matewan', 'WV', 'This downtown marker identifies the setting of the May 19, 1920 gunfight between Baldwin-Felts agents, local officials and miners during the struggle to unionize the southern West Virginia coalfields. Ten men were killed, and the confrontation helped trigger the escalation that ultimately led toward the Battle of Blair Mountain.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=169678', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Meadowcroft Rockshelter', 'meadowcroft-rockshelter', 'weird-history', 40.28618, -80.49063, 'Jefferson Township', 'PA', 'Meadowcroft preserves a rock shelter containing evidence of human occupation dating back thousands of years and central to debates about the earliest settlement of North America. The archaeological site is protected beneath a modern enclosure and can be seen on guided tours during the museum''s operating season.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.heinzhistorycenter.org/visit/meadowcroft/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Missouri State Penitentiary Museum', 'missouri-state-penitentiary-museum', 'weird-history', 38.572044, -92.163583, 'Jefferson City', 'MO', 'The Missouri State Penitentiary Museum displays prison artifacts, photographs, a replica cell and exhibits covering inmate life, prison industries and the institution''s long history. It complements the nearby penitentiary tours and is more accurately a history museum than a haunted attraction.', 'open', null, 'https://www.missouripentours.com/museum/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.missouripentours.com/history/museum/', null, 'node', 9694350011, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Modoc''s Market', 'modocs-market', 'weird-history', 40.79663, -85.82198, 'Wabash', 'IN', 'The shop''s name recalls Modoc, a circus elephant that escaped in Wabash in 1942 and famously crashed through a downtown drugstore during the commotion. A business now operating at the historic location keeps the story alive with elephant imagery and local memorabilia.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/modocs-market', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Morgan County Dungeon', 'morgan-county-dungeon', 'weird-history', 39.64924, -81.86208, 'Malta', 'OH', 'An underground holding cell used for prisoners in the 1830s was forgotten for more than a century before being rediscovered during excavation in 1964. The dungeon survives near the county jail complex with a historical marker and artifacts, but interior access is not a normal anytime attraction and should be confirmed locally before visiting.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/morgan-county-dungeon-ohio', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Morgantown Personal Rapid Transit', 'morgantown-personal-rapid-transit', 'weird-history', 39.62953, -79.9559, 'Morgantown', 'WV', 'Morgantown''s Personal Rapid Transit system is a 1970s federal transportation experiment that became a permanent part of West Virginia University. Small automated cars move riders between stations on a dedicated guideway, making the system itself an unusual piece of living transportation history; rides follow WVU''s current operating schedule.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/morgantown-prt', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mounds State Park Earthworks', 'mounds-state-park-earthworks', 'weird-history', 40.09576, -85.62007, 'Anderson', 'IN', 'Mounds State Park protects a group of prehistoric earthworks constructed by Indigenous peoples beginning more than two thousand years ago. The largest, the Great Mound, is an impressive circular earthwork that can be reached from maintained park trails.', 'open', null, 'https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/mounds-state-park/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Mount Moriah Cemetery', 'mount-moriah-cemetery', 'weird-history', 39.93106, -75.23583, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Once one of Pennsylvania''s largest Victorian cemeteries, Mount Moriah fell into severe abandonment after its old cemetery association disappeared, leaving mausoleums and graves swallowed by vegetation. Volunteers have reopened substantial sections, but public access is normally limited to weather-dependent weekend gate hours and visitors should stay on cleared routes.', 'limited', null, 'https://friendsofmountmoriahcemetery.org/visit/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Murray Hall', 'murray-hall', 'weird-history', 41.809501, -96.024678, 'Little Sioux', 'IA', 'Built in 1877 as a two-storey false-front general store for the merchant Michael Murray, and a rare survivor of that kind of frontier commercial building. It is a museum and reception space in Little Sioux, Iowa — not Tekamah, Nebraska, as the mapping suggested. Walk-in hours are not clearly published, so check before making a special trip.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/places/little-sioux-iowa.htm', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Nancy Kerlin Barnett Grave', 'nancy-kerlin-barnett-grave', 'weird-history', 39.41989, -85.97592, 'Amity', 'IN', 'Nancy Kerlin Barnett was buried here in 1831, and when officials later wanted to build a road through the burial ground, her descendants resisted moving her grave. The compromise left the burial site protected in the middle of County Road 400 South, where traffic still splits around the fenced grave and the additional remains discovered there in 2016.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/nancy-kerlin-barnett-grave', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('New Hope''s Sodom Renaming Marker', 'new-hopes-sodom-renaming-marker', 'weird-history', 42.7979, -76.34678, 'Moravia', 'NY', 'This hamlet was once known as Sodom until, according to local lore, a man climbed the ridgepole of a new gristmill in 1823 with a jug of whiskey and proclaimed that the struggling village had "new hope." The story of the unusual christening is now preserved on a Legends & Lore marker along NY-41A.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/new-hope-named/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('North Brother Island', 'north-brother-island', 'weird-history', 40.80066, -73.89875, 'Bronx', 'NY', 'North Brother Island held Riverside Hospital, where New York isolated patients with contagious diseases and where Mary Mallon, better known as Typhoid Mary, spent years in quarantine. Hospital ruins remain overgrown across the island, but it is a protected wildlife area with no ordinary public access, so travelers should not attempt to land there.', 'closed', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/North_and_South_Brother_Islands_(New_York_City)', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Nuttallburg', 'nuttallburg', 'weird-history', 38.05019, -81.03976, 'Nuttallburg', 'WV', 'Nuttallburg was once a major New River Gorge coal town and later became associated with Henry Ford''s attempt to control his own industrial supply chain. Today the National Park Service preserves mine structures, foundations and the enormous coal conveyor, but getting into the site involves narrow roads, trails and steep terrain.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/neri/learn/historyculture/nuttallburg.htm', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ohio Statehouse Fossils', 'ohio-statehouse-fossils', 'weird-history', 39.9601, -82.99946, 'Columbus', 'OH', 'The limestone used throughout the Ohio Statehouse contains visible fossils from ancient seas, including corals, brachiopods, sponges and other marine life hundreds of millions of years old. Visitors can use the state''s fossil guide to hunt for them in public portions of the Capitol building during open hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ohio-statehouse-fossils', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('O''Hurley''s General Store', 'ohurleys-general-store', 'weird-history', 39.42788, -77.80427, 'Shepherdstown', 'WV', 'O''Hurley''s operates as an old-fashioned general store filled with hardware, household goods, musical instruments and objects that feel pulled from an earlier version of the town. The working store is open to visitors and is also known for recurring traditional music gatherings.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ohurleys.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old Catskill Game Farm', 'old-catskill-game-farm', 'weird-history', 42.23924, -74.00823, 'Catskill', 'NY', 'The Catskill Game Farm operated from 1933 to 2006 and was once promoted as America''s largest privately owned zoo. Many empty cages, paths and zoo buildings still survive, but the property is now an inn and campground and only overnight guests currently have permission to explore the abandoned zoo grounds.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.theoldgamefarm.com/faqs', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old City Hall Subway Station', 'old-city-hall-subway-station', 'weird-history', 40.71264, -74.00668, 'New York', 'NY', 'The ornate original City Hall subway station opened with New York''s first subway line in 1904 and closed to passengers in 1945, leaving its Guastavino tile vaults and chandeliers intact underground. Entry is restricted to rare New York Transit Museum member tours that require advance tickets and a security background check.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nytransitmuseum.org/old-city-hall/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old Economy Village', 'old-economy-village', 'weird-history', 40.59611, -80.23194, 'Ambridge', 'PA', 'The Harmony Society established Economy in 1824 as a highly organized religious communal settlement while its members awaited the Second Coming. Seventeen historic buildings, gardens and original artifacts survive as a state historic site, with public access during its seasonal operating schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/phmc/historic-sites-and-museums/rural-farm-and-village-history-trail/old-economy', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old Lake County Sheriff''s House and Jail', 'old-lake-county-sheriffs-house-and-jail', 'weird-history', 41.41563, -87.36373, 'Crown Point', 'IN', 'This historic jail became nationally famous after John Dillinger escaped from it in March 1934, reportedly using a fake gun to bluff his way past guards. The preserved complex has also developed a reputation among paranormal groups, but visitors should use official tours and events rather than attempting unscheduled access.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hauntedplaces.org/item/crown-point-sheriffs-house-and-jail/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Old Molson Ghost Town Museum', 'old-molson-ghost-town-museum', 'weird-history', 48.976171, -119.19968, 'Oroville', 'WA', 'Old Molson Ghost Town Museum preserves a collection of pioneer buildings, farm machinery, mining equipment and other artifacts in the former townsite of Molson. The outdoor museum is free to explore, but remote location, snow and seasonal conditions can affect practical access.', 'limited', null, 'https://molsonmuseums.org/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://molsonmuseums.org/gallery1/', '+1-509-485-3292', 'way', 428128256, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Old Post Sanitarium', 'old-post-sanitarium', 'weird-history', 33.19201, -101.38364, 'Post', 'TX', 'The Old Post Sanitarium marker documents the early hospital established in Post in the 1910s and the development of organized medical care in the area. OddWay visitors are primarily stopping for the roadside historical plaque and exterior historic setting rather than a haunted-hospital experience.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://atlas.thc.texas.gov/Details/5169003783', null, 'node', 12403562982, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Oldest Metal Bridge in Virginia', 'oldest-metal-bridge-in-virginia', 'weird-history', 37.23912, -80.2249, 'Elliston', 'VA', 'Built in 1878, this metal truss bridge carried traffic until 1971 before being preserved at the northbound Ironto Safety Rest Area on Interstate 81. It has been restored as a pedestrian bridge, turning a highway rest stop into an unexpectedly good piece of surviving nineteenth-century transportation history.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/40448', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Oneida Community Mansion House', 'oneida-community-mansion-house', 'weird-history', 43.06034, -75.60462, 'Oneida', 'NY', 'Nearly 300 members of the radical Oneida Community once lived communally in this enormous mansion while practicing group marriage, communal child rearing and religious Perfectionism. The 93,000-square-foot building survives as a museum, inn and residence with daily self-guided museum access and scheduled deeper tours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.oneidacommunity.org/our-history', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Original Site of St. Mary''s Orphan Asylum', 'original-site-of-st-mary-s-orphan-asylum', 'weird-history', 29.26287, -94.83266, 'Galveston', 'TX', 'A roadside historical marker near Galveston''s seawall commemorates the original St. Mary''s Orphan Asylum and the devastating loss of the orphanage during the 1900 hurricane. The institution itself no longer stands here, so visitors are stopping for the plaque and the history of the former site.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://atlas.thc.texas.gov/Details/5167007175', null, 'node', 12403616528, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Overlook Mountain House Ruins', 'overlook-mountain-house-ruins', 'weird-history', 42.08439, -74.09972, 'Woodstock', 'NY', 'Concrete walls and staircases from the abandoned Overlook Mountain House still stand high above Woodstock after repeated fires and unfinished rebuilding attempts ended the resort''s history. The ruins are reached by a steep multi-mile hike, and the state warns visitors not to enter or climb the unstable structures.', 'limited', null, 'https://dec.ny.gov/places/overlook-mountain-wild-forest', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Palmyra Mining Camp', 'palmyra-mining-camp', 'weird-history', 39.165714, -119.500106, 'Dayton', 'NV', 'Gold in the Pine Nut Mountains drew several hundred miners and merchants here from about 1860. The neighbouring camp of Como overtook it within a few years and Palmyra vanished. Reached over a long rocky unpaved road southeast of Dayton; scattered ruins only.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nvexpeditions.com/lyon/como.php', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Paw Paw Tunnel', 'paw-paw-tunnel', 'weird-history', 39.55556, -78.46278, 'Oldtown', 'MD', 'Construction of this 3,118-foot C&O Canal tunnel began in 1836 and took 14 years amid unstable rock, funding problems and violent labor disputes. The towpath still passes through the completely dark tunnel, which is reached on foot or bicycle; bring a flashlight and follow any temporary NPS closure notices.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/places/paw-paw-tunnel.htm', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Penitentiary Avenue', 'penitentiary-avenue', 'weird-history', 32.72843, -114.615586, 'Yuma', 'AZ', 'Penitentiary Avenue is a historic roadway beside Yuma''s Territorial Prison area and formed part of the old Ocean-to-Ocean Highway route through Yuma. There is no standalone haunted attraction here; the meaningful visitor stops are the nearby Yuma Territorial Prison and historic Ocean-to-Ocean Bridge.', 'roadside', null, 'https://npgallery.nps.gov/NRHP/GetAsset/NHLS/66000197_text', null, null, null, null, 'way', 337523589, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Phoenix Shot Tower', 'phoenix-shot-tower', 'weird-history', 39.29073, -76.60547, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Completed in 1828, the 234-foot brick tower was briefly the tallest structure in the United States and manufactured lead shot by dropping molten metal from its upper levels. The landmark remains standing downtown, with interior access available only during limited tour hours and events.', 'limited', null, 'https://baltimore.org/listings/phoenix-shot-tower/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pigeon Roost State Historic Site', 'pigeon-roost-state-historic-site', 'weird-history', 38.617, -85.77644, 'Scottsburg', 'IN', 'This rural memorial marks the location of the Pigeon Roost settlement and a deadly 1812 attack during the violent frontier conflict surrounding the War of 1812. The state historic site preserves the location and memorial while modern interpretation places the event within the larger conflict between Indigenous nations, settlers and U.S. expansion.', 'open', null, 'https://secure.in.gov/history/state-historical-markers/find-a-marker/pigeon-roost/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Pocket Watch Grave', 'pocket-watch-grave', 'weird-history', 40.48559, -85.98776, 'Greentown', 'IN', 'A grave in Greenlawn Cemetery is marked with an oversized stone pocket watch rather than a standard rectangular monument. The carved watch face and chain make the memorial immediately recognizable and give travelers a specific, respectful cemetery oddity to locate.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/76259', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Porter Creek Bridge Ruins', 'porter-creek-bridge-ruins', 'weird-history', 41.48764, -81.93649, 'Bay Village', 'OH', 'Concrete bridge piers from an early-twentieth-century electric railway still rise from the wooded Porter Creek valley after the line was abandoned and dismantled. The ruins can be reached legally on foot from the Lake Erie Nature & Science Center area using public paths, but visitors need to hike into the valley rather than drive directly to them.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/porter-creek-bridge-ruins', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Prophet''s Rock', 'prophets-rock', 'weird-history', 40.50458, -86.85153, 'Battle Ground', 'IN', 'Tradition identifies this rocky overlook as the place where Tenskwatawa, known as the Prophet, watched or encouraged Native forces during the Battle of Tippecanoe in November 1811. A marker and public pull-off identify the location today, though interpretations of the battle should be understood within the larger history of Indigenous resistance to U.S. expansion.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=6434', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Quecreek Mine Rescue Site', 'quecreek-mine-rescue-site', 'weird-history', 40.07781, -79.08605, 'Somerset', 'PA', 'Nine miners were trapped underground by flooding at Quecreek in July 2002 and were brought out alive after a highly publicized 77-hour rescue. The rescue field is now Monument for Life Memorial Park, where visitors can see the rescue shaft, a miner statue and outdoor memorials; the educational center has separate operating hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.quecreekrescue.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rausch Gap Ghost Town', 'rausch-gap-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 40.49953, -76.59774, 'Cold Spring Township', 'PA', 'Rausch Gap was a nineteenth-century railroad and coal settlement that disappeared after industry moved away, leaving foundations, a cemetery and other traces in the forest. The abandoned town site is reached on foot along the Appalachian Trail and related trails, so it requires a hike rather than a roadside visit.', 'limited', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rausch_Gap,_Pennsylvania', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Reading Pagoda', 'reading-pagoda', 'weird-history', 40.33609, -75.90567, 'Reading', 'PA', 'William Abbott Witman constructed Reading''s Japanese-inspired Pagoda in 1908 as the centerpiece of a proposed mountaintop resort, but the resort plan collapsed after he failed to secure a liquor license. The city acquired it for $1 in 1911; following a major restoration, the grounds are open daily while the building itself currently opens only for selected ticketed walkthroughs and arranged group tours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.readingpagoda.com/visit', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rees Sanitarium', 'rees-sanitarium', 'weird-history', 30.1615, -96.39863, 'Brenham', 'TX', 'This stop is a Texas historical marker identifying the site of Rees Sanitarium, Brenham''s first hospital, rather than an abandoned hospital visitors can enter. Travelers will find a roadside plaque explaining the former institution and its place in local medical history.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://atlas.thc.texas.gov/Details/5477008379', null, 'node', 12454130589, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Rehmeyer''s Hollow Hex House', 'rehmeyers-hollow-hex-house', 'weird-history', 39.80208, -76.64471, 'Stewartstown', 'PA', 'Powwow practitioner Nelson Rehmeyer was murdered inside this house in 1928 by men who believed he had placed a hex on one of them, producing the sensational case remembered as the York Witch Trial. The house survives, but it no longer has dependable public tour hours, so treat it as private property and view only from the public road unless an official event specifically grants access.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/rehmeyers-hollow', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Remains of the Truxton Circle Fountain', 'remains-of-the-truxton-circle-fountain', 'weird-history', 38.71027, -77.02762, 'Fort Washington', 'MD', 'A fountain once stood in Washington, D.C.''s Truxton Circle before the traffic circle was removed in the 1940s and the monument seemingly disappeared. Pieces were later identified among discarded stone at Fort Washington Park, where the surviving fragments can be seen in the park rather than at their original D.C. location.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/remains-of-truxton-circle-fountain', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Renwick Smallpox Hospital Ruin', 'renwick-smallpox-hospital-ruin', 'weird-history', 40.75159, -73.95956, 'New York', 'NY', 'This Gothic Revival ruin on Roosevelt Island opened as a smallpox hospital in the nineteenth century and later became a nurses'' residence before abandonment. The shell remains fenced and cannot be entered, but it is clearly visible from the public paths in Southpoint Park while preservation groups work toward eventual safe access.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.theruin.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rhyolite Ghost Town', 'rhyolite-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 36.900897, -116.829335, 'Beatty', 'NV', 'Rhyolite appeared during the Bullfrog gold rush of the early 1900s and emptied almost as fast when the boom collapsed. The BLM manages the townsite, where you can walk freely among the ruins including the Cook Bank and the bottle house. Day use, four miles west of Beatty.', 'open', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/rhyolite-historic-area', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Richardson Olmsted Campus', 'richardson-olmsted-campus', 'weird-history', 42.93001, -78.88258, 'Buffalo', 'NY', 'H.H. Richardson designed this monumental complex as the Buffalo State Asylum for the Insane, with Frederick Law Olmsted and Calvert Vaux shaping the grounds around it. The grounds remain accessible and scheduled seasonal tours enter portions of the restored complex, while other former hospital buildings are not open for exploration.', 'limited', null, 'https://richardson-olmsted.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rose Island Ruins', 'rose-island-ruins', 'weird-history', 38.44975, -85.64556, 'Charlestown', 'IN', 'Rose Island was once a popular amusement park with rides, a swimming pool, zoo attractions and river access before the catastrophic Ohio River flood of 1937 left it beyond repair. Charlestown State Park now maintains a trail to the former park area, where visitors can see surviving foundations, the old pool and other ruins in the woods.', 'open', null, 'https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/charlestown-state-park/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Schoellkopf Power Station Ruins', 'schoellkopf-power-station-ruins', 'weird-history', 43.0928, -79.06283, 'Niagara Falls', 'NY', 'The Schoellkopf complex was once the world''s largest hydroelectric power station before a catastrophic rockslide and collapse destroyed most of it in 1956. A seasonal elevator at Niagara Falls State Park now carries visitors into the gorge, where surviving walls and industrial remnants can be seen along the official ruins trail.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.niagarafallsstatepark.com/attractions/schoellkopf-power-station-ruins-site/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Seneca Quarry', 'seneca-quarry', 'weird-history', 39.06988, -77.34408, 'Poolesville', 'MD', 'This abandoned quarry supplied the distinctive reddish Seneca sandstone used in major Washington-area buildings, most famously the Smithsonian Castle. Quarry cuts, ruins and related historic features remain within the C&O Canal National Historical Park landscape and are reached on foot.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/seneca-quarry', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Serpent Mound', 'serpent-mound', 'weird-history', 39.02414, -83.4296, 'Bratton Township', 'OH', 'Serpent Mound is a massive prehistoric effigy earthwork shaped like an undulating snake and is one of the most distinctive archaeological sites in North America. Visitors can follow the path around the protected mound, use the observation tower and visit the museum during posted hours; climbing on the earthwork or entering the site after the gates close is prohibited.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ohiohistory.org/visit/browse-historical-sites/serpent-mound/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Shakespeare Ghost Town Tours', 'shakespeare-ghost-town-tours', 'weird-history', 32.32479, -108.738557, 'Lordsburg', 'NM', 'Several mining booms passed through before the town took its present name in 1879. The Hill family began preserving the surviving buildings after buying the property in 1935. This National Historic Site is private and can only be seen on a guided tour — unescorted access is prohibited, and the owners warn about rattlesnakes and open shafts.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.shakespeareghostown.com/tours', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Shot Tower Historical State Park', 'shot-tower-historical-state-park', 'weird-history', 36.8838, -80.8529, 'Max Meadows', 'VA', 'This roughly 75-foot stone tower was built in the early 1800s to manufacture lead shot by dropping molten lead from the top so it formed into spheres while falling. The grounds are accessible as part of Virginia''s state park system, while entry into the tower itself is restricted to scheduled openings and programs.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.dcr.virginia.gov/state-parks/shot-tower', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Sideling Hill Tunnel on the Abandoned Pennsylvania Turnpike', 'sideling-hill-tunnel-on-the-abandoned-pennsylvania-turnpike', 'weird-history', 40.04851, -78.12915, 'Fulton County', 'PA', 'Sideling Hill Tunnel is a 6,782-foot former Pennsylvania Turnpike tunnel abandoned when the highway was rerouted in 1968. It is now part of the informal Pike2Bike route; reaching it requires hiking or cycling, and the interior is completely unlit, wet and rough, so visitors need lights and should use the established access points.', 'limited', null, 'https://highways.dot.gov/highway-history/general-highway-history/back-time/abandoned-pennsylvania-turnpike', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Silver City Ghost Town', 'silver-city-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 35.597694, -118.4916, 'Bodfish', 'CA', 'More than twenty historic structures rescued from abandoned Kern Valley mining camps since the 1970s. The Corlew family bought the property in 1988, restored it and reopened in 1992. Now a small museum and film location with posted daily hours that depend on the weather.', 'limited', null, 'https://linktr.ee/silvercityghosttown', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Site of Edgar Allan Poe''s Death', 'site-of-edgar-allan-poes-death', 'weird-history', 39.29293, -76.59421, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Edgar Allan Poe died on October 7, 1849 at what was then Washington College Hospital after being found delirious several days earlier, and the circumstances of his final days remain disputed. The original hospital is gone, but a plaque on the later hospital complex marks the location traditionally associated with the room where Poe died.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/edgar-allen-poes-site-of-death', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Site of Sanitarium of Alonzo Orrin Scarborough (1860-1952) Pioneer Doctor', 'site-of-sanitarium-of-alonzo-orrin-scarborough-1860-1952-pioneer-doctor', 'weird-history', 32.716, -100.91725, 'Snyder', 'TX', 'This roadside Texas historical marker on Snyder''s courthouse square identifies the site of Dr. Alonzo Orrin Scarborough''s early sanitarium. No sanitarium attraction remains to tour; the value of the stop is the plaque and its short piece of local medical history.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://atlas.thc.texas.gov/Details/5415004883', null, 'node', 12453536656, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Site of The Odessa Sanitarium', 'site-of-the-odessa-sanitarium', 'weird-history', 31.84679, -102.36865, 'Odessa', 'TX', 'A Texas historical marker in downtown Odessa identifies the former site of an early sanitarium that opened in the 1880s and later became part of the city''s civic history. The sanitarium no longer survives as an attraction, so this is a roadside plaque stop rather than a building visitors can enter.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://atlas.thc.texas.gov/Details/5135004898', null, 'node', 12403576671, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Snyder Sanitarium', 'snyder-sanitarium', 'weird-history', 32.23366, -97.756, 'Glen Rose', 'TX', 'Snyder Sanitarium is a historic Glen Rose medical building associated with early local health care, with a Texas historical marker explaining its story. Travelers should treat it primarily as a roadside historic-site/exterior stop unless a current occupant specifically permits interior access.', 'roadside', null, 'https://atlas.thc.state.tx.us/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 12453473996, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Spencer´s Mining Camp', 'spencer-s-mining-camp', 'weird-history', 37.246992, -111.952239, 'Kanab', 'UT', 'Mapped within the same small Pahreah historic area as the cellar and the chimney. No reliable source establishes a separate history for Spencer''s as its own settlement, so treat it as one mining-era remnant of the larger site, on the same dirt-road route.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/glca/planyourvisit/day-hikes.htm', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Spocott Windmill Village', 'spocott-windmill-village', 'weird-history', 38.58958, -76.18149, 'Cambridge', 'MD', 'The current post windmill is a reconstruction of a 19th-century mill destroyed by a blizzard, surrounded by a collection of relocated and restored historic buildings. The grounds are generally accessible from dawn to dusk, while buildings and milling demonstrations have more limited schedules.', 'open', null, 'https://visitdorchester.org/spocott-windmill/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Squire Boone Caverns', 'squire-boone-caverns', 'weird-history', 38.065, -86.13355, 'Mauckport', 'IN', 'Squire Boone, younger brother of Daniel Boone, settled in this area and developed a gristmill near the cave system in the early nineteenth century. His remains are associated with the cavern property, where guided tours descend through underground rooms, streams and formations around a site carrying both natural and frontier history.', 'limited', null, 'https://squireboonecaverns.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://squireboonecaverns.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('State Penitentiary C.S.A. and Texas Civil War Manufacturing', 'state-penitentiary-c-s-a-and-texas-civil-war-manufacturing', 'weird-history', 30.72307, -95.54688, 'Huntsville', 'TX', 'This Huntsville stop is a roadside Texas historical marker describing the state penitentiary''s role in Confederate-era manufacturing during the Civil War. It is not an abandoned prison attraction or paranormal tour, so visitors should expect a plaque and exterior historical context rather than building access.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, null, null, 'node', 12454128116, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Stonewall Jackson''s Arm Grave', 'stonewall-jacksons-arm-grave', 'weird-history', 38.31803, -77.73239, 'Locust Grove', 'VA', 'After Stonewall Jackson was accidentally shot by Confederate troops at Chancellorsville in 1863, surgeons amputated his left arm and a chaplain buried it in the Lacy family cemetery at Ellwood Manor. Jackson himself died days later and was buried in Lexington, leaving this small marked arm grave as one of Virginia''s strangest Civil War burial sites; access follows National Park Service and Ellwood hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/places/000/stonewall-jackson-arm.htm', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Surratt House Museum', 'surratt-house-museum', 'weird-history', 38.76417, -76.89729, 'Clinton', 'MD', 'Mary Surratt''s country home and tavern became a meeting point and supply stop connected to the Lincoln assassination conspiracy. Restored as a museum, it focuses on the Surratt family, the Confederate underground and Booth''s escape; current public access is limited to scheduled tour and walk-in hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.surrattmuseum.org/visitor-information', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Tahawus Ghost Town', 'tahawus-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 44.05061, -74.05098, 'Newcomb', 'NY', 'The abandoned mining settlement of Tahawus sits deep in the Adirondacks near the old iron and titanium works where Theodore Roosevelt began his famous 1901 ride to the presidency. Furnace ruins and surviving structures remain around the remote historic district, reached by a long drive into public forest lands and short walks from established access areas.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.adirondackhub.com/history/tahawus', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Girl in Blue Grave', 'the-girl-in-blue-grave', 'weird-history', 41.63921, -81.4115, 'Willoughby', 'OH', 'An unidentified young woman dressed entirely in blue was struck and killed by a train in Willoughby on Christmas Eve 1933, and local residents paid for her burial and a marker reading "Unknown but not forgotten." She was identified decades later as Josephine "Sophie" Klimczak, and a second marker now gives her name beside the original grave in Willoughby Village Cemetery.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-girl-in-blue-willoughby-ohio', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Leatherman Grave and Marker', 'the-leatherman-grave-and-marker', 'weird-history', 41.1369, -73.86219, 'Ossining', 'NY', 'The mysterious wanderer known as the Leatherman repeatedly walked a roughly 365-mile circuit through New York and Connecticut in the 1880s while wearing a handmade suit of heavy leather. He died in 1889 and is buried in Ossining, where a Legends & Lore marker records one of New York''s strangest real-life folk figures.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wgpfoundation.org/historic-markers/the-leatherman/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thomas Bullitt''s Lone Grave', 'thomas-bullitts-lone-grave', 'weird-history', 38.33835, -81.62033, 'Charleston', 'WV', 'A single 18th-century grave sits by itself inside a modern Charleston park, the burial place of colonial-era surveyor and soldier Thomas Bullitt. The isolated stone is an unusual survival from a much earlier landscape and can be visited from the park during public hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-grave-of-thomas-bullitt', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thurmond Historic District', 'thurmond-historic-district', 'weird-history', 37.95712, -81.07879, 'Thurmond', 'WV', 'Once one of the busiest railroad towns in the New River Gorge, Thurmond declined until its preserved commercial district became an almost ghost-town-like National Park Service site. Visitors can walk past the old bank, hotel buildings and rail structures, while the restored depot operates seasonally as a visitor center.', 'open', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/neri/learn/historyculture/thurmond.htm', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Tombstone House', 'tombstone-house', 'weird-history', 37.20209, -77.42703, 'Petersburg', 'VA', 'Oswald Young built this house in 1934 using pieces of thousands of discarded government headstones that had once marked Union graves at nearby Poplar Grove National Cemetery. The strange stone residence still survives on Youngs Road, but it is private property and should be viewed only from the public roadway.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-tombstone-house', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Tu-Endie-Wei State Park and Battle Monument', 'tu-endie-wei-state-park-and-battle-monument', 'weird-history', 38.83919, -82.14081, 'Point Pleasant', 'WV', 'At the confluence of the Ohio and Kanawha rivers, this small state park preserves the site and memory of the 1774 Battle of Point Pleasant. Visitors find an imposing granite monument, historical markers and the seasonal Mansion House museum, all just a short distance from Point Pleasant''s Mothman attractions.', 'open', null, 'https://wvstateparks.com/parks/tu-endie-wei-state-park/park-history/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Upper Big Branch Miners Memorial', 'upper-big-branch-miners-memorial', 'weird-history', 37.97968, -81.53437, 'Whitesville', 'WV', 'This public memorial honors the 29 miners killed in the Upper Big Branch Mine disaster on April 5, 2010. Dedicated in 2012, its long granite wall includes life-size silhouettes and the names of the victims, with parking and year-round public access.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ubbminersmemorial.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('USS Maine Bathtub', 'uss-maine-bathtub', 'weird-history', 41.0374, -83.6561, 'Findlay', 'OH', 'The Hancock Historical Museum preserves a bathtub recovered from the wreckage of the USS Maine, whose 1898 destruction in Havana Harbor helped push the United States toward the Spanish-American War. The oddly domestic survivor is displayed inside the museum and can be seen during regular public hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.ohiomagazine.com/ohio-life/article/bathtub-from-the-uss-maine-findlay', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Venezia', 'venezia', 'weird-history', 34.393082, -112.416834, 'Mayer', 'AZ', 'A gold-mining and milling settlement on Senator Highway, named after Venice by the Italian settler F. Scopel in the early 1900s. It had a twenty-stamp mill, store, saloon, stage stop and post office. Today the rugged backroad passes collapsed structures and mining remnants.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.arizonahighways.com/archive/issues/chapter/Doc.705.Chapter.6', '2026-09-07T01:28:12.240723+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Volcano Historic Boomtown Ruins', 'volcano-historic-boomtown-ruins', 'weird-history', 39.23138, -81.29039, 'Walker', 'WV', 'Volcano exploded into existence during the 1860s West Virginia oil boom and was largely destroyed by fire in 1879. Scattered industrial and community remains survive in the woods near Mountwood Park, but reaching them requires a moderately challenging hike rather than a roadside stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ghost-town-volcano-west-virginia', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Vulture Mine Tours / Vulture City Ghost Town', 'vulture-mine-tours-vulture-city-ghost-town', 'weird-history', 33.816527, -112.828828, 'Wickenburg', 'AZ', 'Vulture City preserves the remains of the historic mining settlement that grew around Arizona''s Vulture Mine, with restored buildings, mining equipment and artifacts spread across the property. Visitors can explore on self-guided or scheduled history tours, with occasional paranormal and special-event programming.', 'open', null, 'https://vulturecityghosttown.com/', '2026-09-05T22:12:28.444612+00:00', null, 'https://www.vultureminetours.com/', '+1-877-425-9229', 'node', 3274100436, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Waldameer Pirates Cove', 'waldameer-pirates-cove', 'weird-history', 42.1083, -80.1581, 'Erie', 'PA', 'Bill Tracy created this walk-through pirate funhouse for Waldameer in 1972, combining tilted rooms, blacklight figures, optical illusions and deliberately disorienting passages. It remains an operating piece of vintage amusement architecture inside the seasonal park rather than a modern haunted-house attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.weirderie.com/pirates-cove', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Waldameer Whacky Shack', 'waldameer-whacky-shack', 'weird-history', 42.10864, -80.15767, 'Erie', 'PA', 'Dark-ride designer Bill Tracy built Waldameer''s Whacky Shack in 1970, filling the tracked ride with blacklight monsters, optical gags and old-school funhouse effects. It is still operating at Waldameer and is a rare surviving example of Tracy''s once-widespread amusement-park work, but it is available only when the seasonal park is operating.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.weirderie.com/the-wacky-shack', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('War Correspondents Memorial Arch', 'war-correspondents-memorial-arch', 'weird-history', 39.40571, -77.63931, 'Jefferson', 'MD', 'Journalist George Alfred Townsend erected this unusual stone arch in 1896 as a memorial to journalists and artists who covered wars. The roughly 50-foot monument now stands in Gathland State Park beside the Appalachian Trail and can be visited from the park''s public grounds.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/war-correspondents-memorial', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Waters Mill Ruins', 'waters-mill-ruins', 'weird-history', 39.19995, -77.28416, 'Germantown', 'MD', 'The remains of an early-19th-century saw and grist mill sit near Little Seneca Creek along the Black Hill trail system. The site is made darker by the 1920 dynamiting of the nearby miller''s house, an attack that killed three people and eventually led to the execution of Guy Thompson.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/waters-mill-ruins', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('West Baden Springs Hotel', 'west-baden-springs-hotel', 'weird-history', 38.56722, -86.61806, 'West Baden Springs', 'IN', 'When the present hotel opened in 1902, its enormous free-spanning atrium dome was considered an engineering marvel and was promoted as the "Eighth Wonder of the World." The restored building is again an operating hotel, but public areas and scheduled tours allow travelers to see the surreal circular interior legally.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.asce.org/about-civil-engineering/history-and-heritage/historic-landmarks/west-baden-springs-hotel/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.frenchlick.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Whipple Company Store', 'whipple-company-store', 'weird-history', 37.95882, -81.1656, 'Whipple', 'WV', 'Built in the 1890s, this unusual coal-company store once served the surrounding mining community and later operated as a museum interpreting company-town life. The museum closed and the building was sold to a private owner in 2018, so OddWay travelers should only view the exterior from the public road unless a new authorized access program is announced.', 'private', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=140168', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('White Cliffs of Conoy', 'white-cliffs-of-conoy', 'weird-history', 40.07237, -76.65304, 'Conoy Township', 'PA', 'These stark white cliffs above the Susquehanna are not natural limestone bluffs but piles of industrial waste left by a nineteenth- and twentieth-century quarry operation. They are reached by walking or cycling the Northwest Lancaster County River Trail, with additional ruins from the former company town of Billmyer nearby.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.discovermariettapa.org/business-directory/white-cliffs-of-conoy', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Widow Jane Mine', 'widow-jane-mine', 'weird-history', 41.84284, -74.09827, 'Rosendale', 'NY', 'This enormous former cement mine is part of the Snyder Estate, where Rosendale cement was once quarried for major American construction projects. The cavernous mine now hosts concerts and special events, so interior access is limited to scheduled programs rather than unrestricted exploration.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.centuryhouse.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Wood County Museum', 'wood-county-museum', 'weird-history', 41.35028, -83.61586, 'Bowling Green', 'OH', 'The Wood County Museum occupies the county''s former nineteenth-century infirmary and poor farm complex. Visitors can explore exhibits on the people who lived and died there along with the grounds, paupers cemetery, former Lunatic Asylum site and Pestilence House, making it far stranger than a typical county history museum.', 'open', null, 'https://woodcountyhistory.org/visit/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Air Power Park', 'air-power-park', 'museums', 37.04272, -76.36602, 'Hampton', 'VA', 'This free city park displays aircraft, rockets, missiles and space hardware outdoors in a landscape tied closely to Hampton''s aerospace history. The outdoor collection is accessible daily during park hours, while the indoor museum adds exhibits on aviation and space exploration.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hampton.gov/4233/Air-Power-Park', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('American Celebration on Parade', 'american-celebration-on-parade', 'museums', 38.71551, -78.66929, 'Quicksburg', 'VA', 'A warehouse beside Shenandoah Caverns is packed with enormous retired parade floats from presidential inaugurations, Rose Parades and other major celebrations. Visitors walk among giant genies, animals, patriotic displays and repurposed float pieces on seasonal guided tours, generally from Memorial Day through Labor Day with selected additional dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://shenandoahcaverns.com/attractions/american-celebration-on-parade/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('American Sign Museum', 'american-sign-museum', 'museums', 39.14354, -84.53986, 'Cincinnati', 'OH', 'The American Sign Museum preserves more than a century of American commercial signage, from hand-painted storefronts and roadside signs to enormous glowing neon displays. Visitors can walk through recreated streetscapes and see neon craftsmanship during regular museum hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.americansignmuseum.org/visit/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('American Treasure Tour Museum', 'american-treasure-tour-museum', 'museums', 40.12749, -75.45356, 'Upper Providence Township', 'PA', 'The American Treasure Tour fills a huge former industrial building with automatic music machines, classic automobiles, animated store displays, advertisements and other pieces of American popular culture. Much of the collection is seen from a guided tram ride through rows of densely packed artifacts.', 'open', null, 'https://americantreasuretour.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('American Visionary Art Museum', 'american-visionary-art-museum', 'museums', 39.2804, -76.60689, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Rather than concentrating on conventionally trained artists, this Baltimore museum is devoted to self-taught and visionary creators. The campus is packed with giant sculptures, mosaics, kinetic pieces and objects made from unexpected materials, making the exterior alone an OddWay-worthy stop.', 'open', null, 'https://www.avam.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Anna Jarvis Birthplace Museum', 'anna-jarvis-birthplace-museum', 'museums', 39.29458, -80.04447, 'Webster', 'WV', 'Anna Jarvis, the woman who successfully campaigned for the creation of Mother''s Day, was born at this house in Webster in 1864. The restored home now interprets Jarvis''s life as well as its Civil War connection to Union General George B. McClellan, but it is a small attraction with a limited operating season.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/people/anna-maria-jarvis.htm', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Anti-Saloon League Museum', 'anti-saloon-league-museum', 'museums', 40.12295, -82.92939, 'Westerville', 'OH', 'Westerville was national headquarters of the Anti-Saloon League, one of the organizations most responsible for pushing the United States toward Prohibition. The Westerville History Museum occupies part of the League''s former headquarters and preserves its propaganda, publications and archives; walk-in visitors can view current exhibits during library museum hours.', 'open', null, 'https://westervillelibrary.org/museum/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Archive of the Afterlife: The National Museum of the Paranormal', 'archive-of-the-afterlife-the-national-museum-of-the-paranormal', 'museums', 39.82631, -80.56853, 'Cameron', 'WV', 'This small paranormal museum houses allegedly haunted and unusual artifacts collected by investigator Steve Hummel, with displays built around the stories attached to each object. Its official information lists an April–November tour season but currently also displays a temporary-closure notice, so it should be verified before OddWay actively routes someone there.', 'limited', null, 'https://archive-afterlife.weebly.com/hours--admission.html', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Auburn Cord Duesenberg Automobile Museum', 'auburn-cord-duesenberg-automobile-museum', 'museums', 41.35579, -85.0573, 'Auburn', 'IN', 'This museum occupies the restored 1930 Art Deco headquarters of the Auburn Automobile Company and preserves more than a century of Indiana automotive history. The building itself is part of the attraction, with period offices and showrooms surrounding rare Auburn, Cord and Duesenberg automobiles.', 'open', null, 'https://automobilemuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://automobilemuseum.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Babe Ruth Birthplace Museum', 'babe-ruth-birthplace-museum', 'museums', 39.28558, -76.6248, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'George Herman “Babe” Ruth was born in this Baltimore rowhouse in 1895, just a few blocks from what is now Camden Yards. The restored house operates as a museum containing Ruth memorabilia, photographs and exhibits covering his life and baseball career.', 'open', null, 'https://baberuthmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Baker Mansion History Museum', 'baker-mansion-history-museum', 'museums', 40.4906, -78.4083, 'Altoona', 'PA', 'Ironmaster Elias Baker completed this imposing Greek Revival mansion in 1849 after construction costs pushed him close to financial ruin. The Blair County Historical Society now fills the house with period rooms and regional artifacts, with public tours offered during its seasonal museum schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blairhistory.org/baker-mansion.html', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bayernhof Museum', 'bayernhof-museum', 'museums', 40.49839, -79.91589, 'O''Hara Township', 'PA', 'This eccentric mansion was built by Charles Brown III and hides secret doors, concealed passages, unusual architecture and a large collection of antique automatic music machines. Tours are by advance appointment only, so this is a planned stop rather than a walk-in museum.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.bayernhofmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Belle Boyd House', 'belle-boyd-house', 'museums', 39.45966, -77.96177, 'Martinsburg', 'WV', 'Built in 1853, this was the childhood home of Confederate spy Belle Boyd, one of the Civil War''s most notorious civilian intelligence figures. The restored house now serves as a historical museum and visitor center with exhibits on Boyd, local history and the surrounding region.', 'open', null, 'https://www.cityofmartinsburg.org/about-us/belle-boyd-house', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Belle Gunness Exhibit — La Porte County Historical Society Museum', 'belle-gunness-exhibit-la-porte-county-historical-society-museum', 'museums', 41.58711, -86.70125, 'La Porte', 'IN', 'La Porte''s museum maintains an exhibit on Belle Gunness, the Norwegian-born woman linked to a series of killings discovered after her farm burned in 1908. The case remains unusually murky because the headless woman''s body recovered from the house was never conclusively established to be Gunness, and her ultimate fate is still debated.', 'open', null, 'https://laportecountyhistory.org/exhibits/belle-gunness/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://laportecountyhistory.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('BibleWalk', 'biblewalk', 'museums', 40.78577, -82.49666, 'Mansfield', 'OH', 'BibleWalk is a wax museum containing more than 300 figures arranged in dozens of life-sized scenes drawn from the Bible. Built largely through the work of the neighboring church congregation, it now offers multiple self-guided ticketed tours alongside smaller free exhibits.', 'open', null, 'https://biblewalk.us/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bicycle Heaven', 'bicycle-heaven', 'museums', 40.45631, -80.03241, 'Pittsburgh', 'PA', 'Bicycle Heaven combines a working bike shop with a sprawling museum packed with vintage bicycles, rare models, movie bikes and unusual cycling memorabilia. The collection fills multiple rooms and is open to visitors during posted business hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.bicycleheaven.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Big Mac Museum', 'big-mac-museum', 'museums', 40.32091, -79.69198, 'North Huntingdon Township', 'PA', 'This McDonald''s contains a small museum devoted to the Big Mac, which was created by western Pennsylvania franchisee Jim Delligatti in 1967. Displays include memorabilia and an oversized Big Mac sculpture inside an otherwise operating restaurant.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/big-mac-museum', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bob Ross Experience', 'bob-ross-experience', 'museums', 40.20269, -85.39274, 'Muncie', 'IN', 'Many episodes of The Joy of Painting were recorded in an unassuming studio inside Muncie''s historic Lucius L. Ball home. The room has been recreated as part of the Bob Ross Experience, with original paintings, artifacts and the actual setting associated with one of television''s most recognizable painters.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitindiana.in.gov/listing/bob-ross-experience/11963/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.minnetrista.net/bobrossexperience', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Boonsborough Museum of History', 'boonsborough-museum-of-history', 'museums', 39.50829, -77.65283, 'Boonsboro', 'MD', 'This eccentric small-town collection ranges far beyond local history, with Civil War weapons sitting alongside Egyptian material, carved bullets, unusual medical and military objects, and a bouquet made from human hair. Tours operate on selected weekends from May through December or by appointment.', 'limited', null, 'https://boonsboroughmoh.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Buckland Museum of Witchcraft and Magick', 'buckland-museum-of-witchcraft-and-magick', 'museums', 41.43812, -81.69976, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'Raymond Buckland created the collection that became the Buckland Museum of Witchcraft and Magick, one of the oldest collections of its kind in the United States. The Cleveland museum displays ritual objects, occult artifacts and material connected to modern witchcraft and ceremonial magic, and visitors can enter during ticketed public hours.', 'open', null, 'https://bucklandmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Camera Heritage Museum', 'camera-heritage-museum', 'museums', 38.14964, -79.07276, 'Staunton', 'VA', 'This independent museum has assembled thousands of cameras spanning the history of photography, including espionage cameras disguised as everyday objects, early daguerreotype equipment and hundreds of Brownie models. The collection also includes historic photographs and material connected to figures such as John Wilkes Booth.', 'open', null, 'https://cameraheritagemuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cardboard Boat Museum', 'cardboard-boat-museum', 'museums', 38.95218, -84.28484, 'New Richmond', 'OH', 'The Cardboard Boat Museum calls itself the world''s only museum devoted entirely to boats made from cardboard and preserves vessels, photographs and history connected to New Richmond''s famous cardboard-boat races. Admission is free during its posted seasonal or weekend hours.', 'open', null, 'https://cardboardboatmuseum.com/visitors/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Castle Halloween Museum', 'castle-halloween-museum', 'museums', 40.50766, -78.40791, 'Altoona', 'PA', 'More than 35,000 Halloween and macabre objects fill this private museum, ranging from nineteenth-century decorations and costumes to funeral-related pieces and modern holiday collectibles. Tours are arranged in advance rather than offered as normal daily walk-in admission.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/castle-halloween-museum', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Castle Noel', 'castle-noel', 'museums', 41.13689, -81.86363, 'Medina', 'OH', 'Castle Noel is a year-round Christmas museum built around an enormous collection of Hollywood holiday-movie props, costumes, department-store displays and animated window scenes. It opened in Medina in 2013 and operates as a guided ticketed attraction, so reservations are recommended even though it is not limited to the Christmas season.', 'open', null, 'https://castlenoel.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cliff''s Museum of Car Memorabilia', 'cliffs-museum-of-car-memorabilia', 'museums', 39.21006, -81.05037, 'Harrisville', 'WV', 'This privately owned collection packs thousands of pieces of automobile, gasoline-station and roadside memorabilia into a roughly 13,000-square-foot building. The owner welcomes visitors without a normal admission charge, but the museum operates largely by appointment or when someone is available, so call before making a detour.', 'limited', null, 'https://cliffwvathebuilding.com/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('College Park Aviation Museum', 'college-park-aviation-museum', 'museums', 38.97883, -76.92231, 'College Park', 'MD', 'The museum stands beside the world''s oldest continuously operating airport, where the Wright brothers trained military pilots beginning in 1909. Exhibits cover early flight, unusual aircraft and the airport''s long experimental history, with active aircraft often visible just outside.', 'open', null, 'https://www.pgparks.com/facilities/college-park-aviation-museum', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Columbus Chapel and Boal Mansion Museum', 'columbus-chapel-and-boal-mansion-museum', 'museums', 40.77906, -77.79929, 'Boalsburg', 'PA', 'The Boal estate contains an imported European chapel associated with the Columbus family along with an unusually eclectic collection of historic objects. Guided tours include claims of Columbus-family artifacts, religious pieces, weapons, carriages and other material gathered by generations of the Boal family.', 'limited', null, 'https://boalmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('DEA Museum', 'dea-museum', 'museums', 38.86467, -77.05821, 'Arlington', 'VA', 'The Drug Enforcement Administration''s museum documents the history of illicit drugs, federal enforcement and major investigations through seized objects, undercover material and unusual artifacts. Admission is free, but the museum is inside a federal building and adult visitors must meet current government identification and security-screening requirements.', 'open', null, 'https://museum.dea.gov/visit', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Devil Anse Hatfield Homeplace & Museum', 'devil-anse-hatfield-homeplace-museum', 'museums', 37.69978, -81.99419, 'Sarah Ann', 'WV', 'This museum occupies the Hatfield homeplace area and preserves family material connected with Devil Anse, the famous feud and later generations of the family. It operates with varying hours and visitors should call ahead.', 'limited', null, 'https://hatfieldmccoyfoundation.org/devil-anse-homeplace-museum/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Donora Smog Museum', 'donora-smog-museum', 'museums', 40.1777, -79.85649, 'Donora', 'PA', 'The museum documents the deadly 1948 Donora smog, when industrial air pollution became trapped over the Monongahela Valley and sickened thousands of residents. Photographs, newspapers and artifacts explain the disaster''s role in the development of modern American air-pollution law; public hours are limited, so check before traveling.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.donorahistoricalsociety.org/donora-smog-museum/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dr. Ted''s Musical Marvels', 'dr-teds-musical-marvels', 'museums', 38.20816, -86.97477, 'Dale', 'IN', 'Dr. Ted Waflart assembled a collection of self-playing musical machines ranging from small music boxes to enormous orchestrions and dance organs. The unusual part is that many of the instruments are demonstrated rather than left silent, but access is generally arranged for pre-scheduled groups, so travelers should call before routing here.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/dr-teds-musical-marvels', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Vincennes'),
  ('Early Television Museum', 'early-television-museum', 'museums', 40.03451, -83.16161, 'Hilliard', 'OH', 'The Early Television Museum preserves more than 150 television sets and related artifacts spanning mechanical television, early electronic sets, color television and broadcast history. Visitors can see restored equipment and rare experimental technology during the museum''s posted weekend hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.earlytelevision.org/museum.html', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Edgar Allan Poe Cottage', 'edgar-allan-poe-cottage', 'museums', 40.86551, -73.89424, 'Bronx', 'NY', 'Edgar Allan Poe lived in this small Fordham cottage from 1846 until shortly before his death, and his wife Virginia died here in 1847. The preserved house is now a museum containing exhibits and period furnishings connected to Poe''s final years, with regular weekend hours and additional private tours by arrangement.', 'open', null, 'https://bronxhistoricalsociety.org/poe-cottage', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Edgar Allan Poe House & Museum', 'edgar-allan-poe-house-museum', 'museums', 39.2913, -76.63313, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Edgar Allan Poe lived in this tiny Baltimore rowhouse with members of his family from roughly 1833 to 1835. The preserved house now operates as a museum devoted to Poe''s life and writing, with period rooms, exhibits and artifacts connected to one of America''s most enduring masters of the macabre.', 'open', null, 'https://www.poeinbaltimore.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Edgar Allan Poe Museum', 'edgar-allan-poe-museum', 'museums', 37.53216, -77.42608, 'Richmond', 'VA', 'Richmond''s Poe Museum holds the world''s largest collection of Edgar Allan Poe manuscripts, letters, first editions, personal belongings and memorabilia. The museum opened in 1922 in Richmond''s oldest surviving residential building and includes the atmospheric Enchanted Garden inspired by Poe''s writing.', 'open', null, 'https://poemuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Edgar Allan Poe National Historic Site', 'edgar-allan-poe-national-historic-site', 'museums', 39.962, -75.15, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Edgar Allan Poe lived in this Philadelphia house during one of the most productive periods of his writing career in the 1840s. The National Park Service preserves the empty rooms and exhibits about Poe''s work, including the dark stories that helped define American horror literature.', 'open', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/edal/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ernest Warther Museum & Gardens', 'ernest-warther-museum-gardens', 'museums', 40.52566, -81.48804, 'Dover', 'OH', 'Master carver Ernest "Mooney" Warther spent decades creating extraordinarily detailed working models of steam engines from wood, ivory and other materials. His workshop, family home, carvings, button collection and gardens are preserved together as a museum complex that visitors can tour during posted hours.', 'open', null, 'https://thewarthermuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ernie Pyle World War II Museum', 'ernie-pyle-world-war-ii-museum', 'museums', 39.80438, -87.49514, 'Dana', 'IN', 'Pulitzer Prize-winning war correspondent Ernie Pyle was born outside the tiny town of Dana, and his birthplace farmhouse has been preserved beside museum galleries housed in Quonset-style buildings. The exhibits focus on Pyle''s reporting and the ordinary soldiers whose experiences made his wartime columns famous.', 'limited', null, 'https://erniepyle.org/visit-the-ernie-pyle-wwii-museum/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://erniepyle.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Flatwoods Monster Museum', 'flatwoods-monster-museum', 'museums', 38.6651, -80.7059, 'Sutton', 'WV', 'In September 1952 a group of Braxton County children went up a hill after a light in the sky and came back down describing something ten feet tall in a pleated metal skirt. The museum grew out of a single display case in the county visitor centre and now holds the clippings, the witness accounts and a wall of Flatwoods Monster memorabilia. Admission is free, and it doubles as the Braxton County Visitors Center.', 'open', null, 'https://braxtonwv.org/the-flatwoods-monster/visit-the-museum/', '2026-09-06T01:56:28.154232+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fostoria Glass Museum', 'fostoria-glass-museum', 'museums', 39.91956, -80.74539, 'Moundsville', 'WV', 'This museum preserves glass made by the Fostoria Glass Company, which moved from Ohio to Moundsville in 1891 and became one of the city''s major manufacturers. Displays include tableware, specialty pieces and company history, with limited seasonal afternoon hours rather than daily year-round access.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.fostoriaglass.org/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Frost Entomological Museum', 'frost-entomological-museum', 'museums', 40.80296, -77.86241, 'State College', 'PA', 'Penn State''s entomology museum maintains a research collection of more than one million arthropod specimens representing thousands of species. A free public gallery displays insects, collecting equipment and other entomological material on weekdays during university operating hours.', 'open', null, 'https://ento.psu.edu/about/facilities/frost/visit', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Gary Bowling''s House of Art', 'gary-bowlings-house-of-art', 'museums', 37.26753, -81.22354, 'Bluefield', 'WV', 'This Appalachian art center occupies the former Ramsey School, a 1926 hillside building with entrances on seven different levels. Inside are rotating works by regional artists, but hours are limited and appointment visits are also used, so check before making a dedicated detour.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitmercercounty.com/company/gary-bowlings-house-of-art/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('George Peabody Library', 'george-peabody-library', 'museums', 39.2972, -76.61502, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Completed in the 19th century, the Peabody Library''s soaring atrium is lined with multiple tiers of cast-iron balconies and hundreds of thousands of books. Often described as a cathedral of books, the historic research library is open to visitors during posted public hours when not closed for events.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/george-peabody-library', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Gilboa Fossil Forest', 'gilboa-fossil-forest', 'museums', 42.40046, -74.45014, 'Gilboa', 'NY', 'Gilboa became famous after quarrying exposed fossilized tree stumps from one of the oldest known forests on Earth, dating back roughly 380 million years. The local museum and outdoor fossil displays preserve examples from the site, with regular public hours concentrated on summer and early-fall weekends.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/gilboa-fossil-forest', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Glencairn Museum', 'glencairn-museum', 'museums', 40.13694, -75.06389, 'Bryn Athyn', 'PA', 'Glencairn is a castle-like former residence built between the 1920s and 1930s for the Pitcairn family and now used as a museum of religious art and history. Its galleries contain medieval stained glass, ancient artifacts and objects from religious traditions around the world, with access through the museum''s posted visit schedule.', 'open', null, 'https://www.glencairnmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Grissom Air Museum', 'grissom-air-museum', 'museums', 40.66952, -86.13061, 'Peru', 'IN', 'Located just outside the former Grissom Air Force Base, the museum preserves a large outdoor air park of military aircraft along with indoor Cold War and aviation exhibits. The collection includes fighters, bombers, transports and other aircraft that make the site visually distinct from a conventional local museum.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.grissomairmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.grissomairmuseum.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Gus Grissom Boyhood Home', 'gus-grissom-boyhood-home', 'museums', 38.72994, -86.47267, 'Mitchell', 'IN', 'Virgil "Gus" Grissom grew up in this modest Mitchell house before becoming one of the original Mercury Seven astronauts and later commanding Gemini 3. The preserved home is operated as a small museum devoted to his childhood and early life, providing a more personal counterpoint to large space museums.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=195330', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Hall of Heroes Superhero Museum', 'hall-of-heroes-superhero-museum', 'museums', 41.71065, -85.97253, 'Elkhart', 'IN', 'The Hall of Heroes is a museum devoted specifically to the history of superheroes across comics, film, animation, toys and related memorabilia. Its large collection includes rare comics, original art and screen-related artifacts, giving OddWay a strong niche museum stop rather than a general history museum.', 'limited', null, 'https://hallofheroesmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://hallofheroesmuseum.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Havre de Grace Decoy Museum', 'havre-de-grace-decoy-museum', 'museums', 39.53966, -76.08693, 'Havre de Grace', 'MD', 'The Decoy Museum preserves the Chesapeake Bay tradition of carved waterfowl decoys, working boats, hunting gear and folk art. Its large collection includes historic and contemporary carvings that turn an otherwise ordinary hunting tool into a distinctly regional art form.', 'open', null, 'https://www.decoymuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Heritage Farm Museum & Village', 'heritage-farm-museum-village', 'museums', 38.37643, -82.46994, 'Huntington', 'WV', 'Heritage Farm recreates an Appalachian village with historic-style buildings, craft demonstrations, machinery and multiple museums devoted to regional life. The attraction first opened in the 1990s and now operates on a seasonal schedule, so check current dates before routing travelers there.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.heritagefarmwv.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Houdini Museum', 'houdini-museum', 'museums', 41.4326, -75.66307, 'Scranton', 'PA', 'This Scranton museum is devoted to escape artist and magician Harry Houdini, with memorabilia, photographs, props and material examining his career and his campaigns against fraudulent spiritualists. Visits are structured as scheduled museum-and-magic experiences rather than ordinary anytime walk-in admission.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.houdinimuseum.net/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('House of Frankenstein Wax Museum', 'house-of-frankenstein-wax-museum', 'museums', 43.42436, -73.71361, 'Lake George', 'NY', 'This old-fashioned horror wax museum fills a Canada Street building with moving monsters, gruesome tableaux and classic horror characters. It operates seasonally in Lake George, so current opening dates should be checked before treating it as a guaranteed walk-in stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://frankensteinwaxmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hugh Mercer Apothecary Shop', 'hugh-mercer-apothecary-shop', 'museums', 38.30409, -77.45987, 'Fredericksburg', 'VA', 'This restored 18th-century apothecary interprets medicine from an era when treatments included bloodletting, leeches, lancets, snakeroot and other remedies that look alarming by modern standards. Costumed interpretation and demonstrations make the small museum much stranger than a conventional colonial house tour.', 'limited', null, 'https://washingtonheritagemuseums.org/hugh-mercer-apothecary-shop/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Indiana Dinosaur Museum', 'indiana-dinosaur-museum', 'museums', 41.70768, -86.34659, 'South Bend', 'IN', 'This newer South Bend museum is devoted to dinosaurs and paleontology, with large fossil displays, mounted skeletons and working scientific material rather than only fiberglass roadside models. Its unusual pairing with the adjacent South Bend Chocolate Company destination makes it a strong family-friendly OddWay stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.indianadinosaurmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.indianadinosaurmuseum.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Indiana Medical History Museum', 'indiana-medical-history-museum', 'museums', 39.7699, -86.21336, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'The museum occupies the 1896 Old Pathology Building of the former Central State Hospital, the oldest surviving pathology facility in the United States. Guided tours retain original laboratories, an autopsy room and an anatomical museum containing preserved specimens, while the remaining former hospital buildings and tunnels elsewhere on the property are posted no-trespassing.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.imhm.org/about/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://imhm.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('International Circus Hall of Fame', 'international-circus-hall-of-fame', 'museums', 40.75444, -86.01972, 'Peru', 'IN', 'The museum occupies part of the former Wallace Circus winter quarters, a site that helped make Peru one of America''s most important circus towns. Historic wagons, circus buildings, memorabilia and performers'' history survive on the property, which is designated a National Historic Landmark.', 'limited', null, 'https://circushalloffame.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://circushalloffame.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('James Dean Museum and Garfield Museum', 'james-dean-museum-and-garfield-museum', 'museums', 40.41582, -85.65035, 'Fairmount', 'IN', 'Fairmount manages to combine two very different pieces of pop culture in one small museum: hometown actor James Dean and Garfield creator Jim Davis, who grew up nearby. The collection contains Dean memorabilia alongside Garfield material, including a Garfield Trail statue dressed as Dean.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/james-dean-museum-and-garfield-museum', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Jell-O Gallery Museum', 'jell-o-gallery-museum', 'museums', 42.97885, -77.98569, 'Le Roy', 'NY', 'Jell-O was developed in Le Roy in 1897, and this museum preserves advertising, packaging, recipes and artifacts from the dessert''s unusually successful history. The gallery operates seasonally from spring until shortly before Christmas, so check its current schedule before routing here.', 'limited', null, 'https://leroyhistoricalsociety.org/visit-us/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Johnson-Shaw Stereoscopic Museum', 'johnson-shaw-stereoscopic-museum', 'museums', 41.63738, -80.1469, 'Meadville', 'PA', 'Meadville was once home to the Keystone View Company, which became one of the world''s largest producers of stereoscopic photographs. This small museum preserves cameras, viewers and three-dimensional image sets from that industry and is normally open Saturdays from April through November, with other visits by appointment.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.johnsonshawmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kruger Street Toy & Train Museum', 'kruger-street-toy-train-museum', 'museums', 40.04055, -80.65832, 'Wheeling', 'WV', 'Opened to the public in 1998 inside a former 1906 schoolhouse, this museum is packed with model trains, dolls, games, toys and pop-culture collectibles. It maintains regular seasonal public hours and is a substantial stop rather than a single roadside display.', 'open', null, 'https://www.toyandtrain.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lackawanna Coal Mine Tour', 'lackawanna-coal-mine-tour', 'museums', 41.4167, -75.71524, 'Taylor', 'PA', 'Visitors descend roughly 300 feet underground into a former anthracite mine beneath McDade Park. Guides lead groups through old gangways and coal veins while explaining the dangerous work of northeastern Pennsylvania miners; tours operate seasonally.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitnepa.org/things-to-do/attractions/lackawanna-coal-mine-tour/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Langsdon Mineral Collection', 'langsdon-mineral-collection', 'museums', 40.55122, -84.57146, 'Celina', 'OH', 'The Mercer County District Library displays the Ron and Ruth Langsdon Mineral Collection, containing hundreds of colorful and rare mineral specimens from around the world. The collection is free to view during library hours, with occasional guided programs offering a closer look at the specimens.', 'open', null, 'https://mercerlibrary.org/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lily Dale Museum', 'lily-dale-museum', 'museums', 42.35302, -79.3231, 'Lily Dale', 'NY', 'Lily Dale has operated as a Spiritualist community since the nineteenth century, and its museum occupies a former schoolhouse filled with photographs, documents and artifacts from generations of mediums and séances. Access is tied to the Lily Dale grounds and its seasonal programming, with a gate fee required during the summer season.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.lilydaleassembly.org/pointsofinterest', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Little Sorrel — Stonewall Jackson''s Stuffed Horse', 'little-sorrel-stonewall-jacksons-stuffed-horse', 'museums', 37.79006, -79.4358, 'Lexington', 'VA', 'Stonewall Jackson''s small sorrel horse survived the Civil War and lived for decades after the general''s death before being preserved by a taxidermist. Little Sorrel is now displayed at the VMI Museum, where visitors can see the actual mounted horse rather than a replica.', 'open', null, 'https://www.vmi.edu/museums-and-archives/vmi-museum/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Living Dead Museum', 'living-dead-museum', 'museums', 40.42916, -79.79536, 'Monroeville', 'PA', 'The Living Dead Museum sits inside Monroeville Mall, the shopping center used for George A. Romero''s 1978 *Dawn of the Dead*. The museum follows zombies through cinema and pop culture with props, memorabilia and interactive displays, turning an actual horror-film location into part of the exhibit.', 'open', null, 'https://monroevillemall.com/store/living\_dead\_museum', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lucky Cat Museum', 'lucky-cat-museum', 'museums', 39.12722, -84.49917, 'Cincinnati', 'OH', 'The Lucky Cat Museum contains thousands of maneki-neko, the Japanese beckoning-cat figures associated with good fortune, inside Cincinnati''s Essex Studios. The collection moved into its current first-floor space in 2016 and is free to visit, but current visits are by appointment during limited afternoon hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitcincy.com/listing/lucky-cat-museum/6267/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Medical Exhibit of Yesteryear', 'medical-exhibit-of-yesteryear', 'museums', 39.47521, -77.98086, 'Martinsburg', 'WV', 'Inside Berkeley Medical Center is a small display of antique medical equipment, old nursing uniforms, wooden wheelchairs, handmade crutches and other artifacts from earlier eras of medicine. Because the exhibit is inside an operating hospital, visit only during permitted public hours and do not interfere with patients or staff.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/40978', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mercer Museum', 'mercer-museum', 'museums', 40.3079, -75.12734, 'Doylestown', 'PA', 'Archaeologist and collector Henry Chapman Mercer filled this castle-like concrete museum with tools and objects documenting preindustrial American life. Thousands of artifacts hang from balconies, walls and ceilings in a towering central atrium, including wagons, boats and machinery suspended overhead.', 'open', null, 'https://www.mercermuseum.org/visit/mercer-museum/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Merry-Go-Round Museum', 'merry-go-round-museum', 'museums', 41.45393, -82.7129, 'Sandusky', 'OH', 'The Merry-Go-Round Museum opened in 1990 inside Sandusky''s former post office to preserve the art and history of carousel carving. Visitors can see restored and in-progress carousel figures, watch carving demonstrations when available and ride the museum''s working indoor carousel.', 'open', null, 'https://merrygoroundmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mister Ed''s Elephant Museum & Candy Emporium', 'mister-eds-elephant-museum-candy-emporium', 'museums', 39.89843, -77.43013, 'Orrtanna', 'PA', 'Ed and Pat Gotwalt opened the original Mister Ed''s roadside store in 1975, and its later incarnation turned Ed''s growing elephant collection into an entire museum-and-candy-store destination. Visitors now find roughly 12,000 elephant objects, a teapot museum, whimsical gardens and a huge candy selection, with free museum admission.', 'open', null, 'https://mistereds.com/pages/visit', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mmuseumm', 'mmuseumm', 'museums', 40.71736, -74.00282, 'New York', 'NY', 'Mmuseumm is a tiny cabinet-of-curiosities museum built inside a former freight elevator in a Tribeca alley. Its displays focus on overlooked everyday objects and contemporary artifacts, and the interior has very limited seasonal hours even though the exhibits can often be viewed through the windows from the alley.', 'limited', null, 'https://mmuseumm.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mummers Museum', 'mummers-museum', 'museums', 39.93345, -75.14757, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Philadelphia''s elaborate Mummers tradition fills this museum with feathered costumes, sequined suits, parade props, photographs and artifacts from more than a century of New Year''s performances. The collection explains one of the city''s strangest long-running civic traditions and is open during posted museum hours.', 'open', null, 'https://mummersmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mummies of Philippi', 'mummies-of-philippi', 'museums', 39.15342, -80.04246, 'Philippi', 'WV', 'In 1888, amateur scientist Graham Hamrick experimented with embalming two cadavers and produced a pair of remarkably preserved mummies that later traveled with sideshows. They eventually returned to Philippi and are now displayed at the Barbour County Historical Museum, whose schedule is more limited than a conventional year-round museum.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=211802', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Museum of Radio and Technology', 'museum-of-radio-and-technology', 'museums', 38.40129, -82.47315, 'Huntington', 'WV', 'This volunteer-run museum fills roughly 10,000 square feet with vintage radios, televisions, broadcast equipment, computers and other pieces of communication technology. It maintains regular weekend public hours and is free to visit, making it an unusually substantial stop for a specialized collection.', 'open', null, 'https://www.radiomuseum.org/museum/usa/museum-of-radio-and-technology-huntington-wv/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Museum of the Middle Appalachians', 'museum-of-the-middle-appalachians', 'museums', 36.88002, -81.76386, 'Saltville', 'VA', 'Saltville''s museum tells an unusually broad story that stretches from Ice Age animals and archaeological finds to salt production, Civil War battles and the town''s chemical industry. Fossils and prehistoric remains from the region make it especially useful as an OddWay stop rather than a standard local-history museum.', 'open', null, 'https://www.museumofthemiddleappalachians.org/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mütter Museum', 'mutter-museum', 'museums', 39.95333, -75.17639, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'The Mütter began with surgeon Thomas Dent Mütter''s 1859 donation of 1,700 objects and money to establish a permanent medical teaching collection. It has grown to more than 25,000 objects covering medical history, anatomical specimens and pathology, with ticketed public galleries at the College of Physicians.', 'open', null, 'https://muttermuseum.org/about/overview/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Auto & Truck Museum', 'national-auto-truck-museum', 'museums', 41.35558, -85.05868, 'Auburn', 'IN', 'NATMUS occupies surviving Auburn Automobile Company factory buildings next door to the Auburn Cord Duesenberg Museum. Its collection includes unusual cars, trucks, prototypes, automotive signs and GM Futurliner No. 10, one of the enormous vehicles built for General Motors'' Parade of Progress.', 'open', null, 'https://natmus.org/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://natmus.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('National Barber Museum and Hall of Fame', 'national-barber-museum-and-hall-of-fame', 'museums', 39.84087, -82.81024, 'Canal Winchester', 'OH', 'The National Barber Museum preserves barber chairs, razors, signs, poles, tools and other material from the history of barbering in America. The collection dates back to the museum''s founding in 1988, but current public hours are limited, so check the museum''s schedule or appointment information before routing here.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nationalbarbermuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Bottle Museum', 'national-bottle-museum', 'museums', 43.00312, -73.84872, 'Ballston Spa', 'NY', 'The National Bottle Museum treats bottle making as America''s first major industry and fills its galleries with historic bottles, molds, tools and glassmaking equipment. It is open year-round on posted Wednesday-through-Saturday hours and also maintains a research collection devoted to historic glass.', 'open', null, 'https://nationalbottlemuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Capital Radio & Television Museum', 'national-capital-radio-television-museum', 'museums', 38.92631, -76.73332, 'Bowie', 'MD', 'A 1906 storekeeper''s house is packed with early radios, televisions, crystal sets, vacuum tubes and broadcasting equipment. The museum traces the rapid transformation from wireless telegraphy to household television and operates on limited weekly public hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.cityofbowie.org/292/National-Capital-Radio-Television-Museum', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Capital Trolley Museum', 'national-capital-trolley-museum', 'museums', 39.09581, -77.03139, 'Colesville', 'MD', 'This volunteer museum preserves historic streetcars and the technology of electric urban transportation. On operating days visitors can inspect restored cars and ride along the museum''s demonstration railway, so access depends on the published schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.dctrolley.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Cleveland-Style Polka Hall of Fame', 'national-cleveland-style-polka-hall-of-fame', 'museums', 41.59907, -81.52569, 'Euclid', 'OH', 'This small museum documents Cleveland-style polka and the musicians, accordions, recordings and immigrant communities that shaped it. Exhibits and the hall of fame are open only on limited weekly hours, making it a niche but very specific destination rather than an anytime stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://clevelandstyle.com/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Cryptologic Museum', 'national-cryptologic-museum', 'museums', 39.11487, -76.77473, 'Annapolis Junction', 'MD', 'The National Security Agency''s public museum explores codebreaking, espionage and communications intelligence from early ciphers through modern computing. Displays include historic cryptographic machines, Cold War equipment and artifacts from some of the most secretive parts of American history.', 'open', null, 'https://www.nsa.gov/museum/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Electronics Museum', 'national-electronics-museum', 'museums', 39.48578, -76.66327, 'Cockeysville', 'MD', 'The National Electronics Museum preserves more than 10,000 objects related to radar, radio, sonar, satellites, communications and electronic warfare. The collection has moved to the Hunt Valley/Cockeysville area, so travelers should use the museum''s current address and check its posted schedule before visiting.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.nationalelectronicsmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Great Blacks In Wax Museum', 'national-great-blacks-in-wax-museum', 'museums', 39.31182, -76.59685, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Founded in 1983, this museum uses more than 100 life-size wax figures and immersive scenes to interpret Black history. Some exhibits intentionally confront slavery, lynching and racial violence in unusually direct and graphic ways, making it very different from a conventional wax museum.', 'open', null, 'https://www.greatblacksinwax.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Museum of Civil War Medicine', 'national-museum-of-civil-war-medicine', 'museums', 39.41379, -77.40932, 'Frederick', 'MD', 'This museum examines the grim realities and surprising advances of medicine during the Civil War through surgical instruments, field-hospital material and stories of doctors, nurses and patients. Its displays include subjects such as battlefield surgery, embalming and wartime disease that fit OddWay''s darker-history side particularly well.', 'open', null, 'https://www.civilwarmed.org/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Museum of Dentistry', 'national-museum-of-dentistry', 'museums', 39.2896, -76.62548, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'The University of Maryland''s dental collection preserves thousands of objects tracing the strange, painful and occasionally ingenious history of dentistry. Holdings include early instruments, dentures, dental advertising and other material from the national collection of the American dental profession; confirm public visiting access before routing because it is housed within the dental school.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.dental.umaryland.edu/museum/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Museum of Health and Medicine', 'national-museum-of-health-and-medicine', 'museums', 39.00889, -77.05389, 'Silver Spring', 'MD', 'Founded during the Civil War as the Army Medical Museum, this institution holds one of America''s most unusual medical collections. Visitors encounter anatomical specimens, pathological material, military medicine exhibits and artifacts tied to major events including the assassination of Abraham Lincoln.', 'open', null, 'https://medicalmuseum.health.mil/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Road Museum', 'national-road-museum', 'museums', 39.50926, -77.65397, 'Boonsboro', 'MD', 'The museum tells the story of the National Road, America''s first federally funded highway and one of the routes that transformed early road travel westward. Exhibits recreate pieces of the road''s tavern, transportation and roadside history, and the museum also serves as Boonsboro''s visitor center during its limited open hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://nationalrdfoundation.org/boonsboro-visitor-center/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Watch and Clock Museum', 'national-watch-and-clock-museum', 'museums', 40.03699, -76.50223, 'Columbia', 'PA', 'The National Watch and Clock Museum houses thousands of timekeeping objects ranging from early sundials and tall clocks to pocket watches and modern precision devices. Its galleries make the mechanics and strange variety of human timekeeping the focus of a dedicated public museum.', 'open', null, 'https://www.nawcc.org/index.php/museum/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('No. 9 Coal Mine and Museum', 'no-9-coal-mine-and-museum', 'museums', 40.82867, -75.89693, 'Lansford', 'PA', 'No. 9 operated as an anthracite mine from the nineteenth century until 1972 and was later reopened as a preserved underground attraction. Seasonal tours take visitors about 1,600 feet into the mountain by rail before a guided walk past the mine shaft, mule way and underground hospital.', 'limited', null, 'https://no9coalmine.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Original American Kazoo Company Museum', 'original-american-kazoo-company-museum', 'museums', 42.64911, -78.89839, 'Eden', 'NY', 'The Original American Kazoo Company began producing metal kazoos here in 1916, and the surviving factory now includes a small museum packed with historic kazoos and production equipment. Visitors can see how the instruments are made and, on operating days, make a kazoo of their own.', 'open', null, 'https://www.edenkazoo.com/museum.php', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Otherworld', 'otherworld', 'museums', 39.92214, -82.83583, 'Columbus', 'OH', 'Otherworld is a 32,000-square-foot immersive art attraction made up of dozens of interconnected rooms filled with large-scale installations, secret passages, surreal creatures and interactive technology. The Columbus experience opened in 2019 and operates as a ticketed indoor attraction during posted sessions.', 'open', null, 'https://www.otherworld.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Paul A. Johnson Pencil Sharpener Museum', 'paul-a-johnson-pencil-sharpener-museum', 'museums', 39.53632, -82.44459, 'Logan', 'OH', 'This tiny museum beside the Hocking Hills Regional Welcome Center holds thousands of pencil sharpeners collected by the late Paul A. Johnson and later expanded through additional donations. The display ranges from ordinary desk sharpeners to novelty designs shaped like animals, landmarks and household objects and can be visited during welcome-center hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.explorehockinghills.com/things-to-do/arts-museums/museums/pencil-sharpener-museum/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Paul Bunyan Historical Museum', 'paul-bunyan-historical-museum', 'museums', 47.003669, -94.730578, 'Akeley', 'MN', 'Opened in 1984, combining Paul Bunyan memorabilia with photographs and artefacts from Akeley''s years as a logging and sawmill town. Volunteer-run, directly behind the town''s giant kneeling Paul Bunyan statue, and generally open in summer when volunteers are available.', 'limited', null, 'https://akeleymn.com/pbhs/', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Paul Bunyan Logging Camp Museum', 'paul-bunyan-logging-camp-museum', 'museums', 44.810459, -91.517919, 'Eau Claire', 'WI', 'A reproduction of an 1890s Wisconsin logging camp, built in Carson Park in 1934-35 with help from men who had actually done the work. Now part of the Chippewa Valley Museum campus: bunkhouse, cook shanty, blacksmith shop and equipment exhibits. Seasonal, and admission is charged.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.cvmuseum.com/explore/museum-exhibits/47/logging-center-and-paul-bunyan-logging-camp/', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Percy Skuy Collection on the History of Contraception', 'percy-skuy-collection-on-the-history-of-contraception', 'museums', 41.50596, -81.60844, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'The Dittrick Medical History Center holds the Percy Skuy Collection, roughly 1,100 historical contraceptive devices, prototypes, packaging pieces and related artifacts assembled into one of the most extensive collections of its kind. The museum is free and open to the public, but as of 2026 its regular gallery hours are limited to Fridays and Saturdays.', 'limited', null, 'https://artsci.case.edu/dittrick/collections/aritfacts/contraception-collection/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pest House Medical Museum', 'pest-house-medical-museum', 'museums', 37.4157, -79.15795, 'Lynchburg', 'VA', 'Lynchburg''s Pest House served as a quarantine facility for contagious patients and later became closely associated with Civil War-era medical history. The building was moved to Old City Cemetery in 1987 and now contains period medical displays that visitors can examine as part of the cemetery''s historic grounds.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/pest-house-medical-museum', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://gravegarden.org/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pioneer Tunnel Coal Mine', 'pioneer-tunnel-coal-mine', 'museums', 40.77821, -76.35255, 'Ashland', 'PA', 'Pioneer Tunnel has taken visitors into an authentic anthracite mine since 1962. Seasonal tours ride underground in mine cars, and a separate narrow-gauge steam train follows the mountainside above Ashland.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.pioneertunnel.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pocahontas Exhibition Coal Mine', 'pocahontas-exhibition-coal-mine', 'museums', 37.30725, -81.34627, 'Pocahontas', 'VA', 'Coal mining began at Pocahontas in the 1880s, helping launch the region''s industrial boom and feed the Norfolk and Western Railway. Part of the historic mine is now preserved as the Pocahontas Exhibition Mine, where seasonal tours take visitors underground to see mining equipment, coal seams and the working environment of early miners.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/pocahontas-exhibition-coal-mine', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://www.pocahontasva.org/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roanoke Pinball Museum', 'roanoke-pinball-museum', 'museums', 37.27156, -79.93956, 'Roanoke', 'VA', 'The Roanoke Pinball Museum preserves dozens of playable machines tracing pinball from early mechanical games through modern electronic tables. Admission is built around actually playing the collection rather than viewing it behind glass, making it an interactive history of arcade technology.', 'open', null, 'https://roanokepinball.org/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rotary Jail Museum', 'rotary-jail-museum', 'museums', 40.04385, -86.90174, 'Crawfordsville', 'IN', 'Built around a rotating circular cell block, Crawfordsville''s 1882 jail used a hand-cranked mechanism to bring individual cells to the only opening. The preserved structure is now a museum and is notable as the only surviving rotary jail whose cell block can still be operated.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.rotaryjailmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.rotaryjailmuseum.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Saint Anthony Chapel', 'saint-anthony-chapel', 'museums', 40.46489, -79.98369, 'Pittsburgh', 'PA', 'Saint Anthony Chapel in Troy Hill houses more than 5,000 religious relics, one of the largest publicly accessible collections outside the Vatican. The active Catholic chapel is open during posted hours, and visitors can see reliquaries containing remains and objects associated with hundreds of saints.', 'open', null, 'https://saintanthonyschapel.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Salt Museum', 'salt-museum', 'museums', 43.10002, -76.20705, 'Liverpool', 'NY', 'Built beside Onondaga Lake in 1933, this small museum preserves the story of the salt industry that gave nearby Syracuse its nickname, the Salt City. Exhibits explain brine wells, boiling blocks and salt production, with free public hours running seasonally from May into October.', 'limited', null, 'https://onondagacountyparks.com/parks/onondaga-lake-park/salt-museum/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Schimpff''s Confectionery and Candy Museum', 'schimpffs-confectionery-and-candy-museum', 'museums', 38.27258, -85.74136, 'Jeffersonville', 'IN', 'The Schimpff family has operated this downtown candy business at its present site since 1891. Its museum preserves antique candy equipment, packaging and memorabilia, and visitors can often watch candy being made on machinery that looks almost as unusual as the collection itself.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/schimpffs-confectionery', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.schimpffs.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Simpson Funeral Museum', 'simpson-funeral-museum', 'museums', 36.82576, -79.39869, 'Chatham', 'VA', 'Tucked into a working funeral home, this small museum preserves antique caskets, embalming equipment, hearses, burial clothing and other artifacts from the funeral profession. Because it is attached to an active business rather than a conventional attraction, visitors should verify hours before making a special trip.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/10262', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Spring Grove Hospital Center Alumni Museum', 'spring-grove-hospital-center-alumni-museum', 'museums', 39.26692, -76.72195, 'Catonsville', 'MD', 'Spring Grove traces its institutional history to 1797, making it one of the oldest continuously operating psychiatric hospitals in the United States. Its small alumni museum preserves early medical equipment, photographs, furniture and records from the hospital''s past, but visits are guided and by appointment.', 'limited', null, 'https://health.maryland.gov/springgrove/phototours/Pages/museum.aspx', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Stabler-Leadbeater Apothecary Museum', 'stabler-leadbeater-apothecary-museum', 'museums', 38.80472, -77.0425, 'Alexandria', 'VA', 'This remarkably preserved pharmacy operated from 1792 until 1933 and reopened almost immediately as a museum, leaving shelves, bottles, medical ingredients and equipment largely frozen in place. Visitors can see thousands of historical medical and commercial objects on scheduled museum tours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.alexandriava.gov/museums/location/visit-stabler-leadbeater-apothecary-museum', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Studebaker National Museum', 'studebaker-national-museum', 'museums', 41.67471, -86.26193, 'South Bend', 'IN', 'South Bend''s Studebaker museum preserves vehicles and artifacts from the company that evolved from nineteenth-century wagon building into a major automobile manufacturer. Among its most unusual historic vehicles are presidential carriages, including the carriage associated with Abraham Lincoln''s final trip to Ford''s Theatre.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.studebakermuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.studebakermuseum.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('The Bone Museum', 'the-bone-museum', 'museums', 40.70589, -73.93718, 'Brooklyn', 'NY', 'This Brooklyn museum displays a large educational collection of real human skeletal material, including unusual pathologies, traumatic injuries and what it describes as the world''s largest public collection of human spines. It operates as a ticketed museum inside the McKibbin Lofts during posted Wednesday-through-Sunday hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.thebonemuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The City Reliquary', 'the-city-reliquary', 'museums', 40.71395, -73.95574, 'Brooklyn', 'NY', 'The City Reliquary is a tiny community museum devoted to ordinary and eccentric pieces of New York life, from subway tokens and fragments of landmarks to collections assembled by neighborhood residents. It began as a window display and now occupies a small Williamsburg storefront with limited weekend public hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.cityreliquary.org/plan-your-visit/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Dowager Empress Crystal Ball', 'the-dowager-empress-crystal-ball', 'museums', 39.9494, -75.1916, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'A massive rock-crystal sphere once owned by China''s Dowager Empress Cixi sits inside the Penn Museum under heavy security. The ball was famously stolen in 1988 and later recovered, adding a bizarre crime story to an already unusual object that visitors can see with normal museum admission.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/crystal-ball-dowager-empress-penn-museum', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Mermaid Museum', 'the-mermaid-museum', 'museums', 38.32432, -75.21907, 'Berlin', 'MD', 'This small upstairs museum in downtown Berlin treats mermaids as a mixture of folklore, art, popular culture and imagined natural history. Displays include mermaid artifacts, stories and curiosities assembled into an intentionally unusual cabinet-of-wonders experience.', 'open', null, 'https://www.berlinmermaidmuseum.com/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Ohio Museum of Horror', 'the-ohio-museum-of-horror', 'museums', 40.73362, -82.78674, 'Galion', 'OH', 'The Ohio Museum of Horror is a year-round multi-floor collection devoted to horror films, true crime, occult material and macabre artifacts. Displays include movie memorabilia, Ouija boards, anatomical and funerary objects and other intentionally unsettling pieces, with public admission during posted museum hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.natethompsonvideo.com/ohio', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Sanctuary Museum', 'the-sanctuary-museum', 'museums', 41.47671, -81.77833, 'Lakewood', 'OH', 'Formerly known as the Museum of Divine Statues, the Sanctuary Museum preserves statues, stained glass and other sacred artwork rescued largely from closed or altered Catholic churches. The collection includes elaborate saints, relic-related objects and large architectural pieces and can be visited during its limited posted public hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.thesanctuarymuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Stoogeum', 'the-stoogeum', 'museums', 40.17797, -75.22414, 'Lower Gwynedd Township', 'PA', 'The Stoogeum is a museum devoted entirely to the Three Stooges, with thousands of photographs, costumes, props, posters, toys and personal artifacts. Public openings are limited and irregular compared with a conventional museum, so travelers should confirm an open house or appointment before routing here.', 'limited', null, 'https://stoogeum.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Tour-Ed Mine', 'tour-ed-mine', 'museums', 40.61677, -79.7592, 'Tarentum', 'PA', 'Tour-Ed Mine preserves a former western Pennsylvania coal mine as an underground educational attraction. Guides take visitors into the mine to see equipment, tunnels and demonstrations of historic mining work, with tours operating on a seasonal schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://tour-edmine.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Troll Hole Museum', 'troll-hole-museum', 'museums', 40.92191, -81.10204, 'Alliance', 'OH', 'The Troll Hole Museum is devoted to trolls and houses a collection recognized for its enormous number of troll dolls and related artifacts. Guided visits wind through themed rooms, troll displays and a fantasy-style troll cave, making it one of Ohio''s more deliberately strange museums.', 'open', null, 'https://www.thetrollhole.com/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Trundle Manor', 'trundle-manor', 'museums', 40.42274, -79.88053, 'Swissvale', 'PA', 'Trundle Manor is an inhabited private home turned appointment-only museum of taxidermy, medical devices, bizarre art and miscellaneous unsettling objects. Visitors can tour the bottom-floor collection, but **appointments are required** and the owners specifically ask people not to simply appear at the house.', 'limited', null, 'https://trundlemanor.com/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('USS LST-325', 'uss-lst-325', 'museums', 37.9525, -87.5768, 'Evansville', 'IN', 'USS LST-325 is a surviving World War II landing ship of the type used to carry tanks, vehicles and troops directly onto beaches. The restored vessel is now permanently based on the Ohio River in Evansville and offers guided tours through a working piece of wartime naval engineering.', 'limited', null, 'https://lstmemorial.org/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://lstmemorial.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Wagner Free Institute of Science', 'wagner-free-institute-of-science', 'museums', 39.9806, -75.1629, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'The Wagner Free Institute preserves a nineteenth-century natural-history museum that has changed remarkably little since its displays were arranged in the 1800s. Thousands of fossils, shells, minerals, skeletons and taxidermy specimens remain in wooden cases under the original gallery structure.', 'open', null, 'https://www.wagnerfreeinstitute.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('West Virginia Bigfoot Museum', 'west-virginia-bigfoot-museum', 'museums', 38.6643, -80.70776, 'Sutton', 'WV', 'Opened in 2021, this downtown Sutton museum is dedicated entirely to Bigfoot research and Appalachian sightings. Inside are footprint casts, hair samples, reports, photographs and other Sasquatch material, including what West Virginia tourism describes as the largest collection of its kind in the Mid-Atlantic.', 'open', null, 'https://wvbigfootmuseum.org/virtual-tour', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('West Virginia Mine Wars Museum', 'west-virginia-mine-wars-museum', 'museums', 37.62277, -82.16538, 'Matewan', 'WV', 'Founded in 2015, this museum preserves the story of the violent early-20th-century struggles between coal miners, mine guards and coal companies, including Matewan and Blair Mountain. Its current Matewan location contains artifacts, weapons, photographs, firsthand accounts and other material from the Mine Wars.', 'open', null, 'https://wvminewars.org/visit-the-museum', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('West Virginia State Farm Museum', 'west-virginia-state-farm-museum', 'museums', 38.92043, -82.08964, 'Point Pleasant', 'WV', 'This sprawling museum recreates a historic West Virginia farming community with relocated buildings, farm machinery and unusual collections spread over dozens of acres. One of its stranger highlights is “General,” an enormous taxidermied horse once reported to weigh 2,850 pounds; the museum operates seasonally from spring into fall.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.wvfarmmuseum.org/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Who North America', 'who-north-america', 'museums', 39.63295, -86.34522, 'Camby', 'IN', 'Who North America began as a Doctor Who merchandise business in 1998 and later opened a dedicated physical location in Camby. Along with the store, visitors can see a museum of Doctor Who merchandise and memorabilia spanning the program''s history, making it one of the country''s most unusually specific pop-culture museums.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.visitindy.com/directory/who-north-america/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.whona.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('William P. Didusch Center for Urologic History', 'william-p-didusch-center-for-urologic-history', 'museums', 39.20978, -76.67239, 'Linthicum Heights', 'MD', 'Housed at the American Urological Association, this highly specialized museum preserves the history of urology through antique cystoscopes, surgical instruments, microscopes, medical illustrations and other unusual artifacts. Public visits are generally arranged in advance, so contact the museum rather than treating it as a drop-in attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://urologichistory.museum/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Witch Board Museum Baltimore', 'witch-board-museum-baltimore', 'museums', 39.33086, -76.62962, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'This Hampden museum is devoted to the history, mythology and pop-culture legacy of the Ouija board, which has deep roots in Baltimore. Opened as the Baltimore branch of the Salem Witch Board Museum, it sits inside Bazaar and covers figures such as Elijah Bond and Helen Peters alongside the board''s stranger cultural history.', 'open', null, 'https://www.salemwitchboardmuseum.com/copy-of-home-2', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Working Men''s Institute', 'working-mens-institute', 'museums', 38.12867, -87.93636, 'New Harmony', 'IN', 'Founded in 1838 with help from scientist and philanthropist William Maclure, the Working Men''s Institute is Indiana''s oldest continuously operating public library. Its upstairs museum contains natural-history specimens, artifacts and collections that preserve New Harmony''s unusually dense legacy of utopian communities and scientific experimentation.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/working-mens-institute', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://workingmensinstitute.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Toy Museum', 'world-s-largest-toy-museum', 'museums', 36.646433, -93.287465, 'Branson', 'MO', 'Started in 2001 when collectors Tom and Wendy Beck moved their collection from Texas to Branson. It now fills more than 26,000 square feet across two buildings — over a million toys in six collections, from the 1800s to modern pop culture. Ticketed, with seasonal hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://worldslargesttoymuseum.com/worlds-largest-toy-museum/', '2026-09-06T22:43:52.581802+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Oldest Edible Ham', 'worlds-oldest-edible-ham', 'museums', 36.98208, -76.63111, 'Smithfield', 'VA', 'A Smithfield ham cured in 1902 was forgotten in storage until meat magnate Pembroke Gwaltney Jr. turned it into a publicity object and carried it to events. The famously ancient ham is now displayed at the Isle of Wight County Museum alongside the museum''s equally odd World''s Oldest Peanut.', 'open', null, 'https://www.historicisleofwight.com/isle-of-wight-county-museum.html', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Wyandot Popcorn Museum', 'wyandot-popcorn-museum', 'museums', 40.58705, -83.12685, 'Marion', 'OH', 'The Wyandot Popcorn Museum fills a large historic building with antique popcorn wagons, peanut roasters and other equipment from the history of America''s popcorn industry. The museum is seasonal and closes for part of the year, so visitors should check current hours before making it a route stop.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.marionhistory.com/explore/wyandot-popcorn-museum/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Zippo/Case Museum & Flagship Store', 'zippo-case-museum-flagship-store', 'museums', 41.94339, -78.65071, 'Bradford Township', 'PA', 'The current Zippo/Case museum opened in 1997 after an earlier museum proved too small for the growing collection. Visitors now find the first Zippo lighter, rare Case knives, military and advertising exhibits, the working Zippo Repair Clinic and an enormous Zippo-and-knife display outside; admission is free.', 'open', null, 'https://zippo.com/pages/zippo-case-museum-flagship-store', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('A Healing Palindrome', 'a-healing-palindrome', 'roadside-oddities', 38.13186, -87.93856, 'New Harmony', 'IN', 'Behind New Harmony''s Atheneum stands a marker for the Kcymaerxthaere project, a worldwide network of plaques and installations describing an invented parallel geography. This piece, titled "A Healing Palindrome," deliberately blurs public art, fictional history and real-world place.', 'open', null, 'https://kcymaerxthaere.com/historicalsite/a-healing-palindrome/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Apple Basket Water Tower', 'apple-basket-water-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 38.7538, -78.6436, 'Mount Jackson', 'VA', 'Mount Jackson turned an otherwise ordinary municipal water tower into an enormous basket of apples as a tribute to the Shenandoah Valley''s apple-growing heritage. The painted tower has been a roadside landmark for decades and remains easily visible from Interstate 81 and nearby public roads.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/30023', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Archbald Pothole', 'archbald-pothole', 'roadside-oddities', 41.51175, -75.57408, 'Archbald', 'PA', 'A glacial waterfall drilled this enormous vertical pothole into bedrock thousands of years ago, leaving a cavity roughly large enough to hold dozens of fire trucks'' worth of water. A viewing platform inside Archbald Pothole State Park lets visitors look directly into the formation during park hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/archbald-pothole', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Armour-Stiner Octagon House', 'armour-stiner-octagon-house', 'roadside-oddities', 41.03085, -73.87047, 'Irvington', 'NY', 'This exuberant pink Victorian residence was transformed in the 1870s into an eight-sided domed house inspired by nineteenth-century octagon-house theories. It remains a private residence, and both the house and grounds are accessible only through advance ticketed guided tours.', 'limited', null, 'https://armourstiner.com/visit/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Arnold Schwarzenegger Statue', 'arnold-schwarzenegger-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 39.9721, -83.00225, 'Columbus', 'OH', 'An approximately eight-foot bronze statue of Arnold Schwarzenegger in a bodybuilding pose stands outside the Greater Columbus Convention Center. The sculpture honors Schwarzenegger''s long connection to Columbus and the Arnold Sports Festival and is freely visible from the public plaza.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/arnold-schwarzenegger-statue', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('ASM International Geodesic Dome', 'asm-international-geodesic-dome', 'roadside-oddities', 41.46009, -81.29941, 'Novelty', 'OH', 'ASM International''s headquarters is covered by a huge open-air geodesic dome built in the late 1950s from an aluminum framework. The office building itself is not a general tourist attraction, but the landscaped Materials Park and exterior dome can be viewed during the property''s posted public-ground hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/asm-international-materials-park', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Aullwood Giant Trolls', 'aullwood-giant-trolls', 'roadside-oddities', 39.88121, -84.27081, 'Dayton', 'OH', 'Artist Thomas Dambo created three enormous trolls named Bo, Bodil and Bibbi from reclaimed wood for Aullwood Audubon, turning the preserve into a giant-creature scavenger hunt. The trolls remain on the nature trails even though the original giant nest was removed in 2025; admission is required and reaching all of them involves roughly one to two miles of walking.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.audubon.org/aullwood/explore/troll-hatched-egg-exhibit', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bealeton''s Giant Roller Skate', 'bealetons-giant-roller-skate', 'roadside-oddities', 38.53652, -77.72916, 'Bealeton', 'VA', 'An enormous fiberglass roller skate has stood outside the former skating-rink property since the roller-disco era of the 1980s. The weathered oversized shoe remains visible from the public-facing commercial area and is best treated as a quick roadside photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.fotospot.com/attractions/virginia/bealetons-giant-roller-skate', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Beasts of Beaver Meadows', 'beasts-of-beaver-meadows', 'roadside-oddities', 40.93178, -75.92267, 'Beaver Meadows', 'PA', 'Dragons, dinosaurs, owls and other monsters made from concrete, scrap metal and old vehicle parts line Route 93 north of Beaver Meadows. The sculptures were created by Joseph J. Woitko and sit on private land, so they should be viewed from the road without wandering onto the property.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/beaver-meadows-roadside-scuptures', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bedford Coffee Pot', 'bedford-coffee-pot', 'roadside-oddities', 40.02303, -78.51759, 'Bedford Township', 'PA', 'Bert Koontz built this 18-foot coffee-pot-shaped building in 1927 to lure Lincoln Highway motorists into his adjacent service station and lunch business. Saved from demolition, it was moved to the Bedford County Fairgrounds and restored in 2003–04; the exterior and historical marker are always the attraction, while the interior has no dependable regular public hours.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.bedboro.com/about-us/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Benson Ford Shiphouse', 'benson-ford-shiphouse', 'roadside-oddities', 41.65072, -82.83951, 'Put-in-Bay', 'OH', 'The forward section of the 1924 lake freighter Benson Ford was removed from the ship and placed on a South Bass Island bluff in 1986, creating a private residence that looks like a ship sailing through the trees. The house is not normally open to the public except for occasional announced charity tours, so view it only from legal public areas and do not enter the property.', 'private', null, 'https://www.shiponthebay.com/', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Berne Clock Tower', 'berne-clock-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 40.65815, -84.95537, 'Berne', 'IN', 'Berne built its 160-foot clock tower in 2010 as an elaborate tribute to the Zytglogge in Bern, Switzerland and the town''s Swiss heritage. The public Muensterberg Plaza also stages a mechanical glockenspiel presentation several times a day, complete with large moving figures.', 'open', null, 'https://www.berneclocktower.org/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.berneclocktower.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Big Apple Time Capsule', 'big-apple-time-capsule', 'roadside-oddities', 39.45754, -77.97133, 'Martinsburg', 'WV', 'This oversized fiberglass apple was installed in 1990 as a Community Pride Project honoring Berkeley County''s apple-growing history. The base contains a time capsule intended to remain sealed until 2040, while the apple itself is a permanent public photo stop.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/big-apple-time-capsule', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Iconic Jamestown Chair', 'big-chair', 'roadside-oddities', 42.095702, -79.244411, 'Jamestown', 'NY', 'Jamestown’s giant chair is the Iconic Jamestown Chair, a public-art tribute to the city’s once-dominant furniture industry. Fancher Chair Co. built the oversized oak club chair from a historic Jamestown Lounge Company design and installed it downtown in July 2019; it remains a public photo spot at West Third and Lafayette streets.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.jamestownrenaissance.org/installation-of-oversized-chair-honors-jamestowns-history/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Big High Heel at Craddock Terry', 'big-high-heel-at-craddock-terry', 'roadside-oddities', 37.4115, -79.1375, 'Lynchburg', 'VA', 'The Craddock Terry complex grew from Lynchburg''s shoe-manufacturing industry, which began here in the late nineteenth century and once produced thousands of pairs a day. A giant red high-heel sculpture with a built-in seat now stands outside the converted hotel, turning that industrial history into a deliberately oversized photo stop.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/58033', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://www.craddockterryhotel.com/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Big Leaping Bass', 'big-leaping-bass', 'roadside-oddities', 37.719, -77.4532, 'Ashland', 'VA', 'A fiberglass bass roughly 27 feet tall leaps from an equally oversized faux splash at the entrance to the Winding Brook development. The sculpture was installed as a commercial landmark in the early 2010s and remains visible from the surrounding public roads near Interstate 95.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/33429', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Big Muskie Bucket', 'big-muskie-bucket', 'roadside-oddities', 39.69927, -81.73128, 'Bristol Township', 'OH', 'Big Muskie was once the world''s largest dragline excavator, working Ohio coal country from 1969 until 1991 before the machine was dismantled. Its enormous surviving bucket now sits at Miner''s Memorial Park, where visitors can walk directly up to it, climb inside and see the mining memorials and overlook.', 'open', null, 'https://www.visitmorgancountyohio.com/Explore/Destinations/Miner-s-Memorial-Park-Big-Muskie-Bucket-68/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Big Walker Lookout', 'big-walker-lookout', 'roadside-oddities', 37.04567, -81.22843, 'Wytheville', 'VA', 'This privately operated mountain stop combines a country store with a 100-foot observation tower perched high on Big Walker Mountain. The attraction has been family-run for more than 75 years and hosts seasonal craftspeople and music; tower and store access follow business hours rather than being a 24-hour overlook.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.scenicbeauty-va.com/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bigger Big Chair by David Ireland', 'bigger-big-chair', 'roadside-oddities', 48.738238, -122.485014, 'Bellingham', 'WA', 'Bellingham artist David Ireland created “Bigger Big Chair” in 2004–06 as a monumental painted-steel version of an ordinary club chair. The 12.5-foot sculpture belongs to Western Washington University’s outdoor art collection and remains publicly viewable on campus.', 'roadside', null, 'https://westerngallery.wwu.edu/david-ireland-bigger-big-chair-2004-06', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Billy Bob''s Wonderland Rock-afire Explosion', 'billy-bobs-wonderland-rock-afire-explosion', 'roadside-oddities', 38.41523, -82.25553, 'Barboursville', 'WV', 'Billy Bob''s Wonderland is a family entertainment center that preserves a working Rock-afire Explosion animatronic band, the characters made famous by ShowBiz Pizza Place in the 1980s. It has become a destination for animatronic enthusiasts because very few complete public shows remain in operation.', 'open', null, 'https://billybobs-wonderland.com/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Blenko Man', 'blenko-man', 'roadside-oddities', 39.03852, -80.46659, 'Weston', 'WV', 'This strange life-size glass figure was constructed from Blenko glass pieces by sculptor John Zidek and is distinctive enough that even its two right feet have become part of the story. It now stands inside the Museum of American Glass, where visitors can see it along with a much broader collection of American glassware.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/blenko-man', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Bluespring Caverns', 'bluespring-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 38.79618, -86.54603, 'Bedford', 'IN', 'Bluespring Caverns contains one of the longest known cave systems in Indiana and an extensive navigable underground river. Commercial tours take visitors by boat through the dark cave system rather than along a standard walking path.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/bluespring-caverns', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.bluespringcaverns.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Bromo-Seltzer Arts Tower', 'bromo-seltzer-arts-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 39.28768, -76.62065, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Built between 1907 and 1911 for the company behind Bromo-Seltzer headache remedy, this clock tower was originally crowned by a giant glowing blue medicine bottle. The bottle is gone, but the tower now contains artist studios and a Bromo-Seltzer museum, with scheduled access to the clock room.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.bromoseltzertower.com/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cadillac Ranch', 'cadillac-ranch', 'roadside-oddities', 35.187229, -101.987069, 'Amarillo', 'TX', 'The Ant Farm art collective created Cadillac Ranch in 1974 for Amarillo millionaire Stanley Marsh 3, burying ten Cadillacs nose-first in a field at matching angles. The installation was moved west in 1997 as Amarillo expanded, and today it remains free to visit, with travelers walking out into the field and commonly adding their own spray paint.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.visitamarillo.com/listing/cadillac-ranch/595/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Carhenge', 'carhenge', 'roadside-oddities', 42.142284, -102.85796, 'Alliance', 'NE', 'Artist Jim Reinders and about 35 family members built Carhenge in the summer of 1987 as a memorial to Reinders’ father. Thirty-eight gray-painted American cars recreate the scale and arrangement of Stonehenge, and today visitors can freely walk the outdoor site and see additional automobile sculptures in the surrounding Car Art Reserve.', 'roadside', null, 'https://history.nebraska.gov/carhenge/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Carlisle Futuro House', 'carlisle-futuro-house', 'roadside-oddities', 39.58866, -84.33806, 'Carlisle', 'OH', 'This flying-saucer-shaped residence is an example of the Futuro, the late-1960s prefabricated plastic house designed by Finnish architect Matti Suuronen. The Carlisle property is privately owned, so it should be viewed only from a legal public roadside position without entering the driveway, yard or property.', 'private', null, 'https://www.ohiomagazine.com/ohio-life/article/-the-futuro-house', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Champ the Giant Great Dane', 'champ-the-giant-great-dane', 'roadside-oddities', 39.5395, -87.0577, 'Brazil', 'IN', 'A towering fiberglass Great Dane named Champ has watched over this US 40 property for decades. The dog dates to the classic era of oversized roadside advertising and has been restored and repainted several times while remaining a recognizable Brazil-area landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/16289', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Charlie the Coal Miner', 'charlie-the-coal-miner', 'roadside-oddities', 39.38024, -80.31443, 'Shinnston', 'WV', 'Charlie is a 21-foot scrap-metal coal miner with a lunch pail and a working light in his helmet, unveiled in 1999 as a memorial to local miners. He stands outside the Repair King property at 253 Lincoln Drive and can be photographed from the parking-area approach without entering any restricted industrial space.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/charlie-coal-miner', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Chuang Yen Monastery Giant Buddha', 'chuang-yen-monastery-giant-buddha', 'roadside-oddities', 41.48333, -73.79444, 'Kent', 'NY', 'Chuang Yen Monastery occupies more than 200 wooded acres and houses an enormous indoor Buddha surrounded by thousands of smaller Buddha images. The Buddhist Association of the United States welcomes visitors to the monastery at designated times, but religious services and current visitor schedules should be respected.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.baus.org/en/visit-us/chuang-yen-monastery/introducing-cym/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cincinnati Mushroom House', 'cincinnati-mushroom-house', 'roadside-oddities', 39.14118, -84.42371, 'Cincinnati', 'OH', 'Architect and University of Cincinnati professor Terry Brown spent more than a decade transforming a small Hyde Park house into an organic structure covered with warped shingles, stained glass, porthole windows and a bright spiral staircase. It remains private property, so OddWay visitors should admire and photograph the exterior only from the public sidewalk without entering the lot or stairs.', 'private', null, 'https://www.ohiomagazine.com/ohio-life/article/mushroom-house-cincinnati', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Clayshire Castle', 'clayshire-castle', 'roadside-oddities', 39.39782, -86.94701, 'Bowling Green', 'IN', 'This modern medieval-style castle was built in the Indiana countryside as a private residence and bed-and-breakfast, complete with towers, stonework and themed rooms. It is not an abandoned castle or public park, so interior access should be limited to booked guests or scheduled events.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/43906', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://clayshirecastle.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Clothespin', 'clothespin', 'roadside-oddities', 39.9524, -75.1657, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Claes Oldenburg installed *Clothespin* in 1976, turning an ordinary spring clothespin into monumental public art opposite Philadelphia City Hall. It stands directly above the downtown transit concourse at 15th and Market and is freely visible from the public plaza at any time.', 'open', null, 'https://www.philart.net/art/Clothespin/75.html', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Colgate Clock', 'colgate-clock', 'roadside-oddities', 38.27463, -85.75287, 'Clarksville', 'IN', 'The enormous Colgate Clock was originally installed at the company''s Jersey City plant before being moved to the Clarksville factory complex in the 1920s. Its roughly 40-foot face survives as a giant industrial landmark along the Ohio River even though toothpaste production at the old plant has ended.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/colgate-clock', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Columcille Megalith Park', 'columcille-megalith-park', 'roadside-oddities', 40.92692, -75.20227, 'Bangor', 'PA', 'This privately owned but publicly accessible sanctuary contains more than 90 large stone settings spread across more than 20 wooded acres, with most placed between 1980 and 2005. Visitors can wander several miles of rough trails from dawn to dusk for free; climbing the stones is prohibited and organized activities require permission.', 'open', null, 'https://www.columcille.org/visitingthepark', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Conewago Potholes at Falmouth', 'conewago-potholes-at-falmouth', 'roadside-oddities', 40.11921, -76.70916, 'Conoy Township', 'PA', 'When the Susquehanna River drops low enough, the exposed diabase bedrock at Conewago Falls reveals deep circular potholes, sculpted channels and ripple-like forms carved by powerful water and sediment. The formations are only safely visible at low river levels; use the public boat-launch access and never walk onto exposed river rock during high or rising water.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/conewago-potholes', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Coney Island Circus Sideshow', 'coney-island-circus-sideshow', 'roadside-oddities', 40.5753, -73.9798, 'Brooklyn', 'NY', 'Coney Island USA''s Sideshows by the Seashore continues the neighborhood''s freak-show and circus-sideshow tradition with sword swallowers, fire performers and other live acts. The organization describes it as the last permanently housed circus sideshow in the United States, but performances follow a seasonal schedule rather than running every day of the year.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.coneyisland.com/coneyislandcircussideshow', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Coudersport Ice Mine', 'coudersport-ice-mine', 'roadside-oddities', 41.75456, -77.95533, 'Sweden Township', 'PA', 'Billy O''Neil discovered this strange cavity in 1894 while prospecting, and it became famous because ice forms inside as outside temperatures rise and retreats again as the weather cools. After decades as a roadside attraction and a long closure beginning in 1990, new owners restored and reopened it in 2014; visitation remains seasonal.', 'limited', null, 'https://coudersporticemineonline.com/pages/about-the-coudersport-ice-mine', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Cross Island Chapel', 'cross-island-chapel', 'roadside-oddities', 43.0995, -75.6374, 'Oneida', 'NY', 'Built in 1989 on a tiny platform in the middle of Mason''s Pond, Cross Island Chapel measures only about 28 square feet and has been promoted as the world''s smallest church. The chapel is reached by boat for private ceremonies, but ordinary travelers should view it from the public roadside rather than attempting to cross the pond.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.oneidacityny.gov/sites/default/files/fileattachments/community/page/3217/may_newsletter.pdf', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Crystal Cave', 'crystal-cave', 'roadside-oddities', 41.64661, -82.82672, 'Put-in-Bay', 'OH', 'Crystal Cave was discovered in 1887 beneath what is now Heineman''s Winery and is actually the interior of an enormous celestite geode. Visitors can descend into the sparkling blue-purple chamber on seasonal guided tours, generally during the Lake Erie island tourism season.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/crystal-cave', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Crystal Cave', 'crystal-cave-kutztown', 'roadside-oddities', 40.52614, -75.84249, 'Richmond Township', 'PA', 'Crystal Cave was discovered in 1871 and became one of Pennsylvania''s earliest commercial show caves. Seasonal guided tours descend into passages filled with stalactites, stalagmites and crystalline formations, with additional exhibits and attractions above ground.', 'limited', null, 'https://crystalcavepa.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Crystal Grottoes Caverns', 'crystal-grottoes-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 39.49806, -77.67694, 'Boonsboro', 'MD', 'Discovered during quarry work in 1920, Crystal Grottoes developed into Maryland''s only commercial show cave. Guided tours descend into chambers filled with stalactites, flowstone and other formations, so visitors must enter during the attraction''s operating season and tour hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.mgs.md.gov/geology/caves/crystal_grottoes.html', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dark Star Park', 'dark-star-park', 'roadside-oddities', 38.89375, -77.07176, 'Arlington', 'VA', 'Artist Nancy Holt designed Dark Star Park as Arlington''s first county-commissioned public artwork, and it was installed in 1984. Its concrete spheres, tunnels, poles and carefully placed shadows form a strange astronomical landscape, with a famous annual alignment occurring around 9:32 a.m. every August 1.', 'open', null, 'https://www.arlingtonva.us/Government/Departments/Parks-Recreation/Locations/Parks/Dark-Star-Park', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dawes Arboretum Hedge Letters', 'dawes-arboretum-hedge-letters', 'roadside-oddities', 39.98013, -82.4131, 'Newark', 'OH', 'More than a thousand northern white cedars planted beginning in 1942 form enormous letters spelling out DAWES ARBORETUM across the landscape. Visitors can walk near the hedge and climb the arboretum''s observation tower for a better view, with entry subject to the arboretum''s current admission and operating hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/dawes-arboretum-hedge-letters', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dinosaur Kingdom II', 'dinosaur-kingdom-ii', 'roadside-oddities', 37.64899, -79.52483, 'Natural Bridge', 'VA', 'Artist Mark Cline''s Dinosaur Kingdom II imagines an alternate Civil War in which Union soldiers discover dinosaurs and attempt to use them as weapons. The walk-through attraction is packed with life-size fiberglass dinosaurs, soldiers and absurd battle scenes and operates seasonally rather than year-round.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.dinosaurkingdomii.com/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Dinosaur Land', 'dinosaur-land', 'roadside-oddities', 39.06003, -78.13997, 'White Post', 'VA', 'Opened in the early 1960s, Dinosaur Land is an old-school roadside attraction filled with more than 50 large prehistoric creature statues. Its deliberately dated dinosaurs, giant shark, octopus and other oversized beasts preserve the feel of mid-century American roadside tourism.', 'open', null, 'https://dinosaurlandva.com/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Don Knotts Statue', 'don-knotts-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 39.63075, -79.95524, 'Morgantown', 'WV', 'Morgantown unveiled this life-size bronze statue of hometown actor Don Knotts in 2016 outside the Metropolitan Theatre. The sculpture includes references to his best-known roles and is freely accessible from the downtown sidewalk area.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/statue-of-don-knotts', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Duquesne Brewery Clock', 'duquesne-brewery-clock', 'roadside-oddities', 40.42615, -79.97652, 'Pittsburgh', 'PA', 'This enormous 60-foot-square clock was built in 1933 and later moved onto the former Duquesne Brewing Company building. Its face and hands dwarf those of many traditional clock towers, and it remains visible from surrounding public streets and bridges even though the old brewery itself is not a visitor attraction.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/duquesne-brewery-clock', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Earthoid Water Tower', 'earthoid-water-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 39.18472, -77.24961, 'Germantown', 'MD', 'A huge spherical water tank has been painted as a remarkably detailed globe of the Earth, turning a piece of utility infrastructure into a giant roadside planet. It is best viewed from nearby public roads and areas around the Montgomery College Germantown campus rather than approached as an attraction with its own visitor entrance.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/location/md/all', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Enchanted Forest at Clark''s Elioak Farm', 'enchanted-forest-at-clarks-elioak-farm', 'roadside-oddities', 39.23701, -76.87535, 'Ellicott City', 'MD', 'Maryland''s original Enchanted Forest storybook park opened in 1955 and eventually closed, but many of its giant fairy-tale structures were rescued and restored at Clark''s Elioak Farm. Visitors can now wander among pieces such as Cinderella''s pumpkin coach and the Old Woman''s Shoe during the farm''s seasonal operating dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://clarklandfarm.com/enchanted_forest.html', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Eternal Flame Falls', 'eternal-flame-falls', 'roadside-oddities', 42.70158, -78.75113, 'Orchard Park', 'NY', 'A natural gas seep burns inside a small grotto behind this waterfall in Chestnut Ridge Park, creating the strange sight of fire flickering through falling water. Reaching the flame requires a wooded hike and a walk along Shale Creek, and muddy or wet conditions are common.', 'limited', null, 'https://www3.erie.gov/parks/chestnut-ridge', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Falls of the Ohio Fossil Beds', 'falls-of-the-ohio-fossil-beds', 'roadside-oddities', 38.2725, -85.7609, 'Clarksville', 'IN', 'When river conditions are low, enormous exposed limestone beds reveal fossils from a Devonian sea that covered the region roughly 390 million years ago. The state park protects one of the world''s largest exposed Devonian fossil beds and provides a visitor center overlooking the site.', 'open', null, 'https://www.in.gov/dnr/state-parks/parks-lakes/falls-of-the-ohio-state-park/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Field of Corn', 'field-of-corn', 'roadside-oddities', 40.08501, -83.12333, 'Dublin', 'OH', 'Field of Corn, also known as Cornhenge, consists of 109 human-sized concrete ears of corn arranged in rows in Frantz Park. The public artwork was commissioned in 1993 as a reference to the area''s agricultural history and remains free to walk around during park hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.dublinarts.org/fieldofcorn', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fighter Jet in Pennies', 'fighter-jet-in-pennies', 'roadside-oddities', 38.87275, -77.16028, 'Falls Church', 'VA', 'Artist Courtney Stevens Hengerer created "Pennies from Heaven" in 2008 by covering a miniature fiberglass F-14 jet with roughly 14,000 pennies as part of a public-art project. The sculpture was later moved to Falls Church and now sits in the open-air plaza between office buildings at Seven Corners.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/60805', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Flying Saucer by Jene Highstein', 'flying-saucer-university-park', 'roadside-oddities', 41.451633, -87.718737, 'University Park', 'IL', 'A 1977 sculpture by Jene Highstein: concrete over a steel frame, a dark oval sitting in the prairie grass like something that landed and settled. It is part of the permanent collection at Governors State University''s Nathan Manilow Sculpture Park, which is free, has free parking, and is open dawn to dusk every day of the year. Walk out to it — just don''t climb on it.', 'open', null, 'https://www.govst.edu/theNate', '2026-09-06T01:53:15.49385+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Foamhenge at Cox Farms', 'foamhenge-at-cox-farms', 'roadside-oddities', 38.88162, -77.4863, 'Centreville', 'VA', 'Artist Mark Cline built this full-size Stonehenge replica from giant Styrofoam blocks in 2004, and it later moved from Natural Bridge to Cox Farms. Foamhenge is on private property and is accessible only during designated Cox Farms seasons and hours, including Fall Festival and very limited shuttle access at other times.', 'limited', null, 'https://coxfarmsva.com/about/foamhenge/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Fonthill Castle', 'fonthill-castle', 'roadside-oddities', 40.32113, -75.12293, 'Doylestown Township', 'PA', 'Henry Chapman Mercer built Fonthill between 1908 and 1912 as an experimental reinforced-concrete home filled with handmade tiles and architectural fragments. Guided tours wind through dozens of irregular rooms, stairways, terraces and alcoves in one of Pennsylvania''s strangest private homes turned museum.', 'open', null, 'https://www.mercermuseum.org/visit/fonthill-castle/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Future Birthplace of Captain Kathryn Janeway', 'future-birthplace-of-captain-kathryn-janeway', 'roadside-oddities', 39.16589, -86.53617, 'Bloomington', 'IN', 'Star Trek: Voyager establishes Captain Kathryn Janeway as being born in Bloomington in the twenty-fourth century, giving the real city the unusual opportunity to commemorate a person who has not technically been born yet. A dedicated monument marks her "future birthplace" downtown and has become a pilgrimage stop for Star Trek fans.', 'open', null, 'https://janewaystatue.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://janewaystatue.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('GE Chandelier', 'ge-chandelier', 'roadside-oddities', 41.50068, -81.68159, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'Playhouse Square''s outdoor chandelier was installed in 2014 above East 14th Street and was promoted as the largest outdoor chandelier in North America. Thousands of crystals and LED lights hang above the theater district, and visitors can walk beneath it from the public sidewalk and plaza.', 'open', null, 'https://www.playhousesquare.org/news/detail/all-about-our-ge-chandelier', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('George Washington''s Bathtub', 'george-washingtons-bathtub', 'roadside-oddities', 39.62556, -78.22694, 'Berkeley Springs', 'WV', 'A small stone-lined outdoor bath in Berkeley Springs State Park marks the tradition of George Washington bathing in the warm mineral springs here during the 18th century. The present structure is a reconstruction rather than Washington''s literal surviving bathtub, but it has become one of the state''s most photographed historical oddities.', 'open', null, 'https://washingtonheritagetrail.com/morgan-county/george-washingtons-bathtub/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Giant Ball Sculpture', 'giant-ball', 'roadside-oddities', 34.154524, -118.281061, 'Glendale', 'CA', 'This OpenStreetMap-mapped outdoor artwork is a large ball sculpture near the Ferraro Soccer Fields and the Glendale/Los Angeles boundary. I could not find a reliable published artist, official title or construction date, so the safest description is simply a public-facing oversized sculpture that travelers can view as a quick roadside curiosity.', 'roadside', null, 'https://mapcarta.com/N6862517420', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Giant Cootie', 'giant-cootie', 'roadside-oddities', 38.71444, -78.66767, 'Shenandoah Caverns', 'VA', 'This enormous version of the classic Cootie toy began life as a parade float and was later retired to the Shenandoah Caverns complex. The colorful bug now sits outside near American Celebration on Parade, where it can be seen as a roadside curiosity even when the neighboring museum is closed.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/68787', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Giant Crash Test Dummy', 'giant-crash-test-dummy', 'roadside-oddities', 39.19661, -76.60995, 'Glen Burnie', 'MD', 'A 34-foot-tall yellow crash-test dummy stands outside Maryland Motor Vehicle Administration headquarters as an oversized traffic-safety mascot. Installed in 2012, it is a permanent outdoor photo stop visible from the public MVA complex.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/36232', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Giant Quarter', 'giant-quarter', 'roadside-oddities', 40.01599, -78.36026, 'Everett', 'PA', 'Students at Bedford County Technical Center built this roughly 20-foot-wide quarter as a tribute to George Washington''s connections to Bedford County. The nearly one-ton coin stands near Down River Golf Course and makes an easy oversized-object photo stop from the public-facing area.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/giant-quarter-everett-pennsylvania', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Giant Santa', 'giant-santa', 'roadside-oddities', 38.08585, -87.55695, 'Evansville', 'IN', 'Built in 1974, this approximately 35-foot Santa spent years moving between displays, a truck stop and even a junkyard before supporters restored it in 2016. It now stands upright again beside US 41, with a walkway and parking specifically allowing travelers to stop for photos.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/11853', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('God''s Ark of Safety', 'gods-ark-of-safety', 'roadside-oddities', 39.63428, -78.92898, 'Frostburg', 'MD', 'A church congregation began planning a full-scale Noah''s Ark beside Interstate 68 after its pastor said he received a divine command to build it in 1976. The enormous steel skeleton remains an unfinished landmark decades later; view it from legitimate public roadside areas and do not enter the construction property without permission.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/gods-ark-of-safety', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Graffiti Alley', 'graffiti-alley', 'roadside-oddities', 39.31153, -76.61881, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'This alley behind Baltimore''s Motor House is one of the city''s best-known legal graffiti spaces, with nearly every wall and surface repeatedly covered by new layers of paint. Because the artwork constantly changes, repeat travelers may find an almost entirely different alley from one visit to the next.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/graffiti-alley', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Grand Kugel', 'grand-kugel', 'roadside-oddities', 37.56064, -77.46627, 'Richmond', 'VA', 'The Grand Kugel outside the Science Museum of Virginia is a roughly 29-ton granite globe that appears to float and rotate on an extremely thin layer of pressurized water. The current globe replaced an earlier damaged version, and visitors can still push the enormous stone sphere by hand when the fountain system is operating.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-grand-kugel-richmond-virginia', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://smv.org/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Great Stalacpipe Organ at Luray Caverns', 'great-stalacpipe-organ-at-luray-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 38.66407, -78.48383, 'Luray', 'VA', 'The Great Stalacpipe Organ is a working musical instrument that uses rubber-tipped strikers to play carefully selected stalactites spread through Luray Caverns. Built in the 1950s, it turns the cave itself into the instrument and can be heard as part of the normal cavern tour.', 'open', null, 'https://luraycaverns.com/discover/caverns/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Green Bank Telescope', 'green-bank-telescope', 'roadside-oddities', 38.43312, -79.83984, 'Green Bank', 'WV', 'The Robert C. Byrd Green Bank Telescope is one of the largest fully steerable radio telescopes on Earth and dominates the landscape inside the National Radio Quiet Zone. Visitors can explore Green Bank Observatory through its science center and public programs, although access immediately around the telescope itself is controlled rather than a casual walk-up.', 'open', null, 'https://greenbankobservatory.org/portal/gbt/instruments/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Griffis Sculpture Park', 'griffis-sculpture-park', 'roadside-oddities', 42.36938, -78.69151, 'East Otto', 'NY', 'More than 250 large-scale sculptures are scattered through fields, forests and ponds across one of the oldest outdoor sculpture parks in the country. The main Mill Valley Road section is generally open from May through October and involves walking trails over varied terrain.', 'limited', null, 'https://griffissculpturepark.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haines Shoe House', 'haines-shoe-house', 'roadside-oddities', 39.99899, -76.63714, 'Hellam Township', 'PA', 'Shoe magnate Mahlon Haines built this five-level work-boot-shaped house in 1948–49 as an enormous advertisement and promotional guesthouse for his shoe business. It is now a short-term rental rather than a public museum: **only registered guests may enter**, although the owners explicitly welcome photographs from the public roadside.', 'private', null, 'https://www.hainesshoehouse.com/history', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hanging Rock National Natural Landmark', 'hanging-rock-national-natural-landmark', 'roadside-oddities', 40.83, -85.70733, 'Lagro', 'IN', 'Hanging Rock is the exposed remnant of an ancient coral reef formed hundreds of millions of years before Indiana existed as dry land. The limestone bluff rises abruptly over the Wabash River and is protected as a National Natural Landmark.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/hanging-rock-national-natural-landmark', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Hanging Rock Raptor Observatory', 'hanging-rock-raptor-observatory', 'roadside-oddities', 37.50448, -80.45293, 'Waiteville', 'WV', 'This former fire lookout sits on a narrow ridge reached by roughly a 1.2-mile hike and became a famous place for watching migrating hawks and other raptors. The trail remains open, but the tourism authority currently reports the observation structure itself as temporarily closed, so check status before building a route around it.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitwv.com/partners/hanging-rock-raptor-observatory/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Harborcreek Dinosaur Family', 'harborcreek-dinosaur-family', 'roadside-oddities', 42.18045, -79.95712, 'Harborcreek', 'PA', 'A field of large metal sculptures on Bartlett Road east of Erie: a tyrannosaurus and its young, a triceratops, a woolly mammoth, and a welder among them. They stand on private land beside the road, so look from public ground rather than crossing the grass. Catalogues of the work list it under North East, which is the wrong township and about ten miles off — this entry is placed from the sculptures themselves.', 'private', null, 'https://maps.app.goo.gl/', '2026-09-08T01:45:42.030388+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Harlan — World''s Largest Anatomically Accurate Brain Sculpture', 'harlan-worlds-largest-anatomically-accurate-brain-sculpture', 'roadside-oddities', 39.17207, -86.52017, 'Bloomington', 'IN', 'Indiana University''s Psychological and Brain Sciences building has a seven-foot-tall, roughly 10,000-pound human brain carved from Indiana limestone outside its entrance. Artist Amy Brier and carver Mike Donham created the anatomically detailed sculpture, nicknamed Harlan, for the department''s 125th anniversary.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-world-s-largest-anatomically-accurate-limestone-brain-sculpture-bloomington-indiana', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://psych.indiana.edu/about/harlan-brain/index.html', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Hartman Rock Garden', 'hartman-rock-garden', 'roadside-oddities', 39.90498, -83.83247, 'Springfield', 'OH', 'Ben Hartman began building this elaborate folk-art garden in 1932 after losing his job during the Great Depression. Miniature castles, cathedrals, historical scenes and hundreds of figures made from concrete, stone, glass and other materials fill the yard, which is preserved as a free public attraction from dawn to dusk.', 'open', null, 'https://hartmanrocks.org/visit/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Haserot Angel', 'haserot-angel', 'roadside-oddities', 41.51302, -81.59038, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'The Haserot family memorial in Lake View Cemetery features a life-sized bronze angel created by sculptor Herman Matzen in 1919. Weathering has produced dark streaks beneath its eyes that make the figure appear to cry black tears, earning it the nickname Angel of Death; visitors can see it in Section 9 during cemetery hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-haserot-angel', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Herkimer Diamond Mines', 'herkimer-diamond-mines', 'roadside-oddities', 43.12871, -74.97665, 'Newport', 'NY', 'Visitors break apart exposed dolostone to search for naturally double-terminated quartz crystals known as Herkimer diamonds, which formed roughly 500 million years ago. The fee-dig surface mine operates seasonally and provides basic tools and instruction, with anything found by visitors theirs to keep.', 'limited', null, 'https://herkimerdiamond.com/mine/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hiawatha Statue', 'hiawatha-world-s-largest-indian-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 46.449723, -90.162138, 'Ironwood', 'MI', 'Ironwood’s 52-foot fiberglass Hiawatha statue was built in 1964 as a roadside tourist attraction and local landmark. It has since been refurbished and remains the centerpiece of Hiawatha Park, where travelers can walk up for photos.', 'roadside', null, 'https://travelironwood.com/hiawatha-statue/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Menominee'),
  ('Hickory Run Boulder Field', 'hickory-run-boulder-field', 'roadside-oddities', 41.0501, -75.6436, 'Kidder Township', 'PA', 'A roughly 16-acre field of bare sandstone boulders stretches across Hickory Run State Park with almost no soil or vegetation between the rocks. The formation dates to cold-climate conditions near the end of the Ice Age; a gravel road reaches it in warmer months, while winter closures can require a much longer hike.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/hickory-run-state-park', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Hillbilly Hot Dogs', 'hillbilly-hot-dogs', 'roadside-oddities', 38.50659, -82.29823, 'Lesage', 'WV', 'This deliberately over-the-top roadside restaurant is built around buses, junkyard art, hand-painted signs and hillbilly-themed structures along the Ohio River. It has been operating for more than two decades and remains a working restaurant, so visitors can explore the public grounds while stopping for food.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hillbillyhotdogs.com/', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pine River Depot 1887 Caboose', 'historic-caboose', 'roadside-oddities', 46.716906, -94.403555, 'Pine River', 'MN', 'This is the historic 1887 caboose displayed near the Pine River Depot in Pine River, not Pequot Lakes. Heritage Group North restored the aging railroad car in 2019, and travelers now find it beside the depot as an outdoor piece of local railroad history.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.pineandlakes.com/news/pine-river-pine-ridge-cemetery-historic-caboose-repaired', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Historic Santa Claus Statue', 'historic-santa-claus-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 38.11567, -86.91013, 'Santa Claus', 'IN', 'This large Santa statue was dedicated in 1935 and became an early physical symbol of the town that had already turned its unusual name into a Christmas identity. Restored and now standing at the Santa Claus Museum & Village, it gives visitors a historic roadside Santa rather than a modern seasonal decoration.', 'open', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=286726', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://santaclausmuseum.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Hot Air Balloon Water Tower', 'hot-air-balloon-water-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 36.96459, -81.07928, 'Wytheville', 'VA', 'Wytheville''s municipal water tower has been painted to resemble a colorful hot-air balloon, turning a piece of utility infrastructure into a highway landmark. The balloon design has become a recognizable local oddity and is best treated as a drive-by or public-road photo stop rather than a site to approach directly.', 'roadside', null, 'https://fotospot.com/attractions/virginia/hot-air-balloon-water-tower', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Howe Caverns', 'howe-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 42.69624, -74.39852, 'Howes Cave', 'NY', 'Howe Caverns takes visitors deep underground through limestone passages, enormous chambers and an underground lake first explored commercially in the nineteenth century. The cave operates as a guided attraction with scheduled tours from its Discovery Drive visitor complex.', 'open', null, 'https://howecaverns.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Indiana Caverns', 'indiana-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 38.1825, -86.15017, 'Corydon', 'IN', 'Indiana Caverns provides public access to part of the Binkley Cave system, one of the state''s major underground networks. Cave exploration in the system has revealed Ice Age animal remains and other paleontological material, while the commercial tour combines walking and underground boat travel.', 'limited', null, 'https://indianacaverns.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://indianacaverns.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Jacques the World''s Largest Bobblehead', 'jacques-the-worlds-largest-bobblehead', 'roadside-oddities', 40.64728, -82.54066, 'Bellville', 'OH', 'Jacques is a roughly 35-foot-tall fiberglass chef standing outside the Buckeye Express Diner along Route 97. The giant figure was restored after weather damage and remains an easy public-facing stop on the diner property.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/jacques-worlds-largest-bobblehead', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jenny Globe', 'jenny-globe', 'roadside-oddities', 40.0151, -79.07583, 'Somerset', 'PA', 'A huge rotating fiberglass globe has stood outside Jenny Products since the late 1960s, built to celebrate the company''s growth as a maker of pressure-washing equipment. It resembles a water tower but is actually a giant spinning advertisement, with parking available at the business for visitors who want a closer look.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/jenny-globe', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jim Henson and Kermit the Frog Statue', 'jim-henson-and-kermit-the-frog-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 38.98763, -76.94505, 'College Park', 'MD', 'A life-size bronze Jim Henson sits on a bench beside Kermit the Frog on the University of Maryland campus, where Henson studied before creating the Muppets. The memorial garden is outdoors and publicly viewable while campus access is open.', 'open', null, 'https://arboretum.umd.edu/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jolly Green Giant', 'jolly-green-giant', 'roadside-oddities', 43.650675, -94.095708, 'Blue Earth', 'MN', 'Blue Earth’s 55-foot Jolly Green Giant was fabricated in 1978 and dedicated that September, becoming a permanent installation in 1979. The fiberglass advertising icon now stands in Giant Statue Park, where travelers can walk up to the pedestal, take photos and visit the surrounding Green Giant-themed displays.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.si.edu/object/jolly-green-giant-sculpture%3Asiris_ari_336561', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Judy''s Jungle', 'judys-jungle', 'roadside-oddities', 41.68056, -81.32993, 'Mentor', 'OH', 'Judy''s Jungle is a collection of large fiberglass animals gathered outside an industrial property in Mentor, including elephants, giraffes and other oversized creatures. The quirky display is intentionally visible to passersby and visitors can stop to see the figures without entering restricted industrial areas.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/judys-jungle', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Jug Rock', 'jug-rock', 'roadside-oddities', 38.67593, -86.79715, 'Shoals', 'IN', 'Jug Rock is an isolated sandstone formation shaped like a giant stone vessel and is one of the largest free-standing table-rock formations east of the Mississippi River. It sits beside a short public access trail near Shoals, giving OddWay a natural oddity that can be visited without a major hike.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/jug-rock', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Vincennes'),
  ('Jungle Jim''s International Market', 'jungle-jims-international-market', 'roadside-oddities', 39.33508, -84.52425, 'Fairfield', 'OH', 'Jungle Jim''s is a massive international grocery store that doubles as a roadside attraction, filling its aisles with oversized decorations, animatronics, themed storefronts and deliberately bizarre displays. Travelers can shop normally while finding features such as singing characters and the famous faux portable-toilet entrance to the restrooms.', 'open', null, 'https://junglejims.com/', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kenova Pumpkin House', 'kenova-pumpkin-house', 'roadside-oddities', 38.39974, -82.56686, 'Kenova', 'WV', 'What began with a handful of carved pumpkins in 1978 has grown into an annual display covering the historic Griffith house and grounds with roughly 3,000 jack-o''-lanterns. It is a private residence transformed into a public attraction around Halloween, so this should only route travelers during the seasonal display.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/the-pumpkin-house-how-this-small-town-home-became-a-national-attraction/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('King Neptune Statue', 'king-neptune-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 36.85963, -75.9773, 'Virginia Beach', 'VA', 'A massive bronze King Neptune rises over the Virginia Beach Boardwalk at 31st Street, surrounded by sculpted sea creatures and holding an enormous trident. Installed in 2005, the roughly 12-ton monument has become one of the city''s defining roadside-scale photo stops.', 'open', null, 'https://www.visitvirginiabeach.com/listing/king-neptune-statue/1173/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Kinzua Bridge Skywalk and Tornado Ruins', 'kinzua-bridge-skywalk-and-tornado-ruins', 'roadside-oddities', 41.75952, -78.58694, 'Hamlin Township', 'PA', 'The Kinzua Viaduct once stretched more than 2,000 feet across Kinzua Gorge before a tornado tore away much of the structure in 2003. The surviving towers now form a public skywalk with a glass viewing area, while the twisted fallen towers remain visible across the valley below.', 'open', null, 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/kinzua-bridge-state-park', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('KokoMantis', 'kokomantis', 'roadside-oddities', 40.48658, -86.13351, 'Kokomo', 'IN', 'KokoMantis is a giant praying mantis assembled from salvaged industrial material, including World War II-era fuel pontoons and recycled traffic-light poles. The roughly 17-foot-high sculpture stands downtown at Washington and Sycamore Streets and is one of Kokomo''s most recognizable modern roadside oddities.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/kokomantis-scrap-art-sculpture', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Lake George Mystery Spot', 'lake-george-mystery-spot', 'roadside-oddities', 43.42263, -73.713, 'Lake George', 'NY', 'Stand on the marked X behind the Lake George Visitor Center and speak toward the lake; your voice returns as a strange focused echo that people standing only a few feet away may not hear the same way. The free public spot has accumulated both acoustic explanations and supernatural folklore and remains physically marked in Blais Park.', 'open', null, 'https://www.lakegeorge.com/guides/things-to-do/mystery-spot/', '2026-09-08T01:35:27.513733+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Largest Shotgun Shell', 'largest-shotgun-shell', 'roadside-oddities', 37.68458, -77.45387, 'Ashland', 'VA', 'A roughly 30-foot-tall green shotgun shell stands outside Green Top as a giant tribute to the area''s hunting culture. Built by Hudson Sheet Metal, the oversized shell is positioned along the store property and works as a quick roadside photo stop during normal access to the commercial site.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/84714', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://www.greentophuntfish.com/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Laurel Caverns', 'laurel-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 39.7996, -79.7113, 'Wharton Township', 'PA', 'Pennsylvania''s largest cave system by volume extends beneath Chestnut Ridge in Fayette County. The underground caverns are open only from mid-April through late October for guided and self-guided experiences, closing each winter to protect hibernating bats.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.pa.gov/agencies/dcnr/recreation/where-to-go/state-parks/find-a-park/laurel-caverns-state-park', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Leatherlips Monument', 'leatherlips-monument', 'roadside-oddities', 40.11702, -83.11057, 'Dublin', 'OH', 'This 12-foot stone portrait of Wyandot leader Leatherlips was created by artist Ralph Helmick and installed at Scioto Park in 1990 near the area traditionally associated with Leatherlips'' 1810 execution. Visitors can walk into the limestone sculpture and look through it toward the Scioto River; the City of Dublin and Wyandotte Nation have also worked to correct a later, inaccurate "curse" legend attached to his name.', 'open', null, 'https://www.dublinarts.org/leatherlips', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lincoln Caverns', 'lincoln-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 40.50735, -78.07132, 'Porter Township', 'PA', 'Lincoln Caverns and adjoining Whisper Rocks contain passageways filled with flowstone, crystals and other limestone formations discovered during road construction in the 1930s. Guided underground tours operate from the visitor center, with special black-light and themed programs offered on selected dates.', 'open', null, 'https://lincolncaverns.com/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Longaberger Basket Building', 'longaberger-basket-building', 'roadside-oddities', 40.06376, -82.34646, 'Newark', 'OH', 'Longaberger opened this seven-story headquarters in 1997 in the shape of one of the company''s Medium Market Baskets, complete with enormous handles. The office building has spent years largely vacant and was again being marketed for sale in 2026, so treat it as an exterior roadside stop unless an officially announced tour or event specifically allows entry.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.axios.com/local/columbus/2026/07/10/longaberger-basket-building-history-for-sale-newark', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lost World Caverns', 'lost-world-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 37.83265, -80.44684, 'Lewisburg', 'WV', 'Discovered through a surface opening and developed as a show cave, Lost World Caverns takes visitors through a huge underground chamber filled with stalactites and other formations. The standard attraction is self-guided, while a separate wild-cave experience goes much deeper and requires advance arrangements.', 'open', null, 'https://www.showcaves.com/english/usa/showcaves/LostWorld.html', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Loveland Castle', 'loveland-castle', 'roadside-oddities', 39.28358, -84.266, 'Loveland', 'OH', 'Harry Andrews began building Château Laroche, better known as Loveland Castle, along the Little Miami River in the 1920s using stone and hand-formed construction methods. The medieval-style castle became headquarters for his Knights of the Golden Trail and now operates as a museum where visitors can explore the rooms, towers and grounds during posted hours.', 'open', null, 'https://lovelandcastle.com/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Lucette Statue (Paul Bunyan''s Sweetheart)', 'lucette-statue-paul-bunyan-s-sweetheart', 'roadside-oddities', 46.930974, -94.523008, 'Hackensack', 'MN', 'Lucette is in Hackensack, not Walker, and was created as Paul Bunyan’s fictional sweetheart for the town’s 1952 celebration. The statue has been repaired after weather damage over the decades and still stands in Birch Lake Park near the visitor center as a free public landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=235099', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Richwood Lumberjack Muffler Man', 'lumberjack-muffler-man-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 38.225668, -80.5261, 'Richwood', 'WV', 'Richwood’s giant lumberjack is a modified fiberglass Muffler Man used as the Richwood High School Lumberjacks mascot beside the football field. Roadside America was tracking the figure in Richwood by 1990, though its original manufacture date is not documented; it has been repaired and repainted repeatedly and is best viewed from permitted public areas around school events.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/2832', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Madonna of the Trail', 'madonna-of-the-trail', 'roadside-oddities', 38.98392, -77.09425, 'Bethesda', 'MD', 'Maryland''s Madonna of the Trail is one of 12 nearly identical pioneer-woman monuments installed across the country along the National Old Trails Road in 1928 and 1929. Dedicated in Bethesda in 1929, the massive stone figure has been moved several times as the surrounding downtown developed but remains publicly viewable beside Wisconsin Avenue.', 'open', null, 'https://highways.dot.gov/highway-history/general-highway-history/part-4-named-trails-us-numbered-highways/part-j', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Marengo Cave', 'marengo-cave', 'roadside-oddities', 38.37552, -86.3395, 'Marengo', 'IN', 'Discovered by children in 1883, Marengo Cave grew into one of Indiana''s best-known commercial cave systems and is designated a U.S. National Natural Landmark. Guided routes take visitors through large underground rooms and extensive formations while preserving a very old-school roadside cave-attraction feel.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.marengocave.com/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://www.marengocave.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Marengo'),
  ('Mars Flying Saucer', 'mars-flying-saucer', 'roadside-oddities', 40.69615, -80.01032, 'Mars', 'PA', 'Mars embraces its name with a nearly 3,000-pound flying-saucer sculpture assembled from industrial tanks and displayed downtown. The statue was already documented by 1989 and has become one of Butler County''s recognizable roadside landmarks, sitting in a public downtown space for easy photographs.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/mars-flying-saucer', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Martini-Drinking Pink Elephant', 'martini-drinking-pink-elephant', 'roadside-oddities', 39.92987, -85.85252, 'Fortville', 'IN', 'A huge pink elephant holding a martini glass sits on a trailer outside a Fortville beverage business, turning the old "seeing pink elephants" expression into literal advertising. The statue is occasionally moved for parades but normally serves as one of central Indiana''s most unmistakable roadside photo stops.', 'roadside', null, 'https://visitindiana.in.gov/blog/post/roadside-attractions/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Maxie, The World''s Largest Goose', 'maxie-the-world-s-largest-goose', 'roadside-oddities', 39.652974, -93.24626, 'Sumner', 'MO', 'Maxie is in Sumner, not Brookfield. Sculptor David Jackson built the 40-foot-tall, 62-foot-wingspan Canada goose in 1974 and it was formally dedicated October 30, 1975; today the fiberglass-and-steel bird stands in a public park and can pivot with the wind.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/7248', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Mercury Cougar Statue', 'mercury-cougar-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 38.8266, -76.9261, 'Temple Hills', 'MD', 'This enormous fiberglass cougar survives from the days when the property operated as a Lincoln-Mercury dealership. Once mounted on the roof, the 1960s advertising cat now sits at ground level near the dealership and is easily visible from the public-facing commercial area.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/46420', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mortar Man', 'mortar-man', 'roadside-oddities', 38.34931, -81.63556, 'Charleston', 'WV', 'High on a downtown Charleston wall is an absurdly tiny human figure only a few inches tall, installed in a mortar joint by artist P. Joseph Mullins. It is around twelve feet above street level and intended to be spotted from the public sidewalk rather than approached or climbed toward.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/mortar-man', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mount Trashmore', 'mount-trashmore', 'roadside-oddities', 36.83096, -76.12425, 'Virginia Beach', 'VA', 'Virginia Beach converted an abandoned landfill into this 165-acre public park beginning in the 1970s, covering compacted layers of trash with soil to form its signature artificial hills. What was once a dump is now a landscaped recreation area with trails, playgrounds, lakes and one of the most literal odd-place names in the state.', 'open', null, 'https://parks.virginiabeach.gov/outdoors/city-parks/mount-trashmore-park', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mount Wood Castle and Cemetery', 'mount-wood-castle-and-cemetery', 'roadside-oddities', 40.08042, -80.72227, 'Wheeling', 'WV', 'This unfinished stone mansion above Wheeling was begun in the 1920s by a physician whose grand plans collapsed after legal trouble, leaving a castle-like shell overlooking the Ohio Valley. The city-owned Mount Wood Cemetery and overlook can be visited, but the deteriorating ruins and steep overgrown areas should be treated as look-don''t-climb features.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/mount-wood-castle-and-cemetery', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Mr. Bendo Muffler Man', 'mr-bendo-muffler-man', 'roadside-oddities', 39.78887, -86.18398, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'Mr. Bendo is a towering fiberglass Muffler Man that has served as an Indianapolis auto-shop landmark for decades. The giant figure has survived moves, repairs and changing businesses and remains a recognizable piece of classic American roadside advertising on West 16th Street.', 'roadside', null, 'https://fotospot.com/attractions/indiana/mr-bendo-muffler-man', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Mr. Peanut Statue — Suffolk Visitor Center', 'mr-peanut-statue-suffolk-visitor-center', 'roadside-oddities', 36.73745, -76.58227, 'Suffolk', 'VA', 'Mr. Peanut''s familiar character traces back to a 1916 Planters logo contest won by a young Suffolk-area boy, linking the advertising icon directly to the city''s peanut history. A Mr. Peanut statue at the Suffolk Visitor Center gives travelers an easy public photo stop while the center interprets Suffolk''s broader agricultural story.', 'open', null, 'https://www.visitsuffolkva.com/itineraries/all-about-mr-peanut-itinerary/', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, 'https://www.visitsuffolkva.com/', null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Joor Muffler Man', 'muffler-man', 'roadside-oddities', 33.124128, -117.079365, 'Escondido', 'CA', 'This is the Joor Muffler Man, a classic oversized fiberglass roadside figure associated with Joor Muffler in Escondido. Escondido tourism material dates the figure to 1969, and travelers still find the giant as a piece of old-school roadside Americana outside the business.', 'roadside', null, 'https://visitescondido.com/info/maps-getting-around/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Mystery Spot', 'mystery-spot', 'roadside-oddities', 37.017283, -122.003751, 'Santa Cruz', 'CA', 'The Mystery Spot is a classic gravity-house roadside attraction in the redwoods outside Santa Cruz, where tilted structures and forced perspective make visitors appear to lean at impossible angles. It was discovered in 1939 and opened to the public around 1940; today visitors buy tickets for a roughly 45-minute guided experience and can also use the hiking trail and gift shop.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.mysteryspot.com/what-is-it', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('NASA Goddard Rocket Garden and Moon Tree', 'nasa-goddard-rocket-garden-and-moon-tree', 'roadside-oddities', 38.9928, -76.84699, 'Greenbelt', 'MD', 'Outside NASA''s Goddard Visitor Center is a collection of rockets and space hardware that gives travelers an up-close look at the scale of sounding rockets and launch technology. The grounds also include a Moon Tree descended from seeds carried around the Moon during Apollo 14, while the visitor center contains additional free exhibits.', 'open', null, 'https://www.nasa.gov/goddard/visitor-center/', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('National Park Seminary', 'national-park-seminary', 'roadside-oddities', 39.0121, -77.05641, 'Silver Spring', 'MD', 'This former women''s school developed an extraordinary campus of architectural fantasies including a Japanese pagoda, Dutch windmill, Swiss chalet and English-style buildings before becoming part of an Army medical complex. Much of the property has since been redeveloped as residences, so visitors should stick to public roads, sidewalks and designated public areas rather than entering private buildings.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.loc.gov/pictures/item/md1503/', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Natural Stone Bridge and Caves', 'natural-stone-bridge-and-caves', 'roadside-oddities', 43.74739, -73.85192, 'Pottersville', 'NY', 'A massive marble arch spans Trout Brook here, forming what is promoted as the largest marble cave entrance in the eastern United States. Seasonal trails lead through caves, potholes and unusual rock formations, with access dependent on the attraction''s operating schedule and weather.', 'limited', null, 'https://stonebridgeandcaves.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Natural Tunnel State Park', 'natural-tunnel-state-park', 'roadside-oddities', 36.69698, -82.73858, 'Duffield', 'VA', 'A naturally carved limestone tunnel about 850 feet long and up to roughly 100 feet high forms the centerpiece of this Southwest Virginia state park, with an active railroad still passing through it. Visitors can hike or use the seasonal chairlift toward the gorge and observation areas, but the railroad tunnel itself is not a pedestrian passage.', 'open', null, 'https://www.dcr.virginia.gov/state-parks/natural-tunnel', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Neah Bay Big Chair', 'neah-bay-big-chair', 'roadside-oddities', 48.368772, -124.601439, 'Neah Bay', 'WA', 'This oversized chair is in Neah Bay, not Forks, and is mapped near the Makah Museum/harbor area as a local roadside attraction. I could not locate a reliable artist or construction date in current published sources, so OddWay should keep the history minimal and present it simply as a giant chair photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://mapcarta.com/N12247217710', null, null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Neighborhood Menagerie', 'neighborhood-menagerie', 'roadside-oddities', 37.79443, -81.18773, 'Beckley', 'WV', 'Dozens of fiberglass animals, dinosaurs and a Bigfoot fill several residential yards along Conway Street, all part of a collection owned by the same local resident. The owner has welcomed visitors, but these are still private residential properties, so OddWay travelers should view the figures from the public street unless they receive clear permission to enter a yard.', 'private', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/69799', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ocean Gallery World Center', 'ocean-gallery-world-center', 'roadside-oddities', 38.33335, -75.08409, 'Ocean City', 'MD', 'Ocean Gallery''s boardwalk building looks like a chaotic collision of scrap metal, signs, art and old vehicles rather than a normal gallery storefront. The family-run business has evolved into one of Ocean City''s most recognizable visual oddities, and the exterior is worth seeing even without shopping.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/location/md/all', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ohio Caverns', 'ohio-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 40.23853, -83.69922, 'West Liberty', 'OH', 'Ohio Caverns was discovered in 1897 and contains extensive passageways filled with stalactites, stalagmites and other mineral formations, including the enormous white formation known as the Crystal King. The privately operated attraction offers guided underground tours during posted hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/ohio-caverns', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Old Ben and the Giant Sycamore Stump', 'old-ben-and-the-giant-sycamore-stump', 'roadside-oddities', 40.46917, -86.14389, 'Kokomo', 'IN', 'Highland Park preserves two major Kokomo oddities under neighboring shelters: Old Ben, a famously enormous steer born in 1902 and preserved by taxidermy after his death, and the huge stump of an ancient sycamore. Combining them into one stop avoids sending travelers to duplicate coordinates while preserving both pieces of Kokomo roadside history.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/old-ben-pavilion-worlds-largest-steer', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Opus 40', 'opus-40', 'roadside-oddities', 42.05067, -74.03169, 'Saugerties', 'NY', 'Sculptor Harvey Fite spent nearly four decades assembling this sprawling bluestone earthwork by hand from millions of pieces of local stone. The six-acre labyrinth of ramps, terraces, walls and platforms is open seasonally as an outdoor arts site.', 'limited', null, 'https://opus40.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Our Lady of the Pines', 'our-lady-of-the-pines', 'roadside-oddities', 39.25242, -79.49874, 'Eglon', 'WV', 'Built in 1958, this tiny stone church measures only about 24 by 12 feet and was once promoted as the smallest church in the 48 contiguous states. Six small pews, an altar and religious statuary fit inside, and the carefully maintained building remains a peaceful roadside curiosity open to respectful visitors.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/our-lady-of-the-pines', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Panama Rocks', 'panama-rocks', 'roadside-oddities', 42.07322, -79.48881, 'Panama', 'NY', 'Towering conglomerate formations create narrow passageways, caves and crevices through an old-growth forest at this privately operated park. The one-mile rock trail is open seasonally with paid admission, and visitors can walk directly among the formations rather than viewing them from a distance.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.panamarocks.com/visitforday.html', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Papermoon Diner', 'papermoon-diner', 'roadside-oddities', 39.32244, -76.62123, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Papermoon is less a normal diner than a giant assemblage artwork with mannequins, toys, Pez dispensers, dolls, brightly painted objects and bizarre decorations covering nearly every available surface. The restaurant is still operating, so travelers can actually go inside rather than merely photographing the exterior.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/37475', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Patriot Fireworks Mega Missile', 'patriot-fireworks-mega-missile', 'roadside-oddities', 39.33426, -78.06315, 'Bunker Hill', 'WV', 'A tall grain silo beside Patriot Fireworks has been transformed into a fake missile labeled as a giant roadside weapon. The "Mega Missile" is visible from the road and business parking area, making it a quick photo stop rather than an attraction that requires entering the structure.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/63258', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Patterson Park Pagoda', 'patterson-park-pagoda', 'roadside-oddities', 39.28995, -76.58349, 'Baltimore', 'MD', 'Built in 1891 as an observation tower, this brightly painted four-story structure is popularly called a pagoda despite being designed in a fanciful Victorian interpretation of Asian architecture. The exterior can be visited in Patterson Park year-round, while interior stair access is limited to scheduled open hours and events.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/patterson-park-observatory', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Paul Bunyan & Babe the Blue Ox', 'paul-bunyan', 'roadside-oddities', 44.902028, -83.443236, 'Ossineke', 'MI', 'This record refers to the concrete Paul Bunyan and Babe the Blue Ox now standing in Ossineke, not Hubbard Lake. Paul N. Domke built the pair in the 1940s; after being moved to a site near Hubbard Lake/Spruce for years, they were returned to their original Ossineke roadside location in 2006, where travelers can see them today.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/2125', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Detroit'),
  ('Paul Bunyan and Babe', 'paul-bunyan-and-babe', 'roadside-oddities', 41.584584, -124.085805, 'Klamath', 'CA', 'The giant Paul Bunyan and Babe the Blue Ox guard the entrance to Trees of Mystery on California’s Redwood Highway. The attraction’s Bunyan figures evolved through several versions beginning in the 1940s, with Babe added in 1951 and the current giant Paul dating to the late 1950s/early 1960s; travelers can photograph the statues at the entrance while the forest attraction beyond them is ticketed.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/2040', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Paul Bunyan and Babe', 'paul-bunyan-and-babe-nitro', 'roadside-oddities', 38.44557, -81.8231, 'Nitro', 'WV', 'A giant fiberglass Paul Bunyan and blue Babe the Ox stand along First Avenue outside a local supply business in Nitro. These classic oversized advertising figures are visible from the road and are best treated as a quick public-road photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://fotospot.com/attractions/west-virginia/paul-bunyan-and-babe', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Paul Bunyan and Babe the Blue Ox Statue', 'paul-bunyan-and-babe-the-blue-ox-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 47.470418, -94.878892, 'Bemidji', 'MN', 'Bemidji’s Paul Bunyan and Babe the Blue Ox statues were built in 1937 for the city’s winter carnival and quickly became one of Minnesota’s defining roadside images. They remain beside Lake Bemidji near the visitor center, where travelers can walk up and photograph the historic pair for free.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.exploreminnesota.com/profile/paul-bunyan-babe-blue-ox/1982', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Paul Bunyan & Babe the Blue Ox', 'paul-bunyan-babe-the-blue-ox', 'roadside-oddities', 44.542467, -70.548499, 'Rumford', 'ME', 'Rumford’s Paul Bunyan is an approximately 18-foot fiberglass Muffler Man that has stood in the area since at least the mid-20th century and was later donated to the town and rebuilt with internal supports. Babe the Blue Ox joined him at the visitor-center site much later, and travelers can photograph the pair for free beside Route 2.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/2556', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Paul Bunyan Bouquet no. 2', 'paul-bunyan-bouquet-no-2', 'roadside-oddities', 29.716318, -95.397803, 'Houston', 'TX', 'Jim Love created “Paul Bunyan Bouquet No. 2” in 1968, turning heavy industrial forms into a whimsical monumental bouquet. The sculpture is on the Rice University campus in Houston rather than West University Place, and travelers can see it as part of the university’s outdoor public-art collection.', 'roadside', null, 'https://publicart.rice.edu/artworks/paul-bunyan-bouquet-no-2', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Paul Bunyan Muffler Man', 'paul-bunyan-muffler-man', 'roadside-oddities', 40.18319, -85.4207, 'Muncie', 'IN', 'A roughly 25-foot Paul Bunyan-style fiberglass giant has stood in Muncie since the mid-twentieth-century roadside-advertising era. Originally connected to a lumber business, the figure later moved to the property near Kilgore Avenue and remains one of Indiana''s classic Muffler Man survivors.', 'roadside', null, 'https://visitindiana.in.gov/blog/post/roadside-attractions/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Paul Bunyan''s Boat-Anchor', 'paul-bunyan-s-boat-anchor', 'roadside-oddities', 45.29691, -96.432457, 'Ortonville', 'MN', 'Paul Bunyan’s “Boat-Anchor” is a 110-ton granite-and-iron monument dedicated in 1958 for Minnesota’s statehood centennial. It sits on a hilltop at the Big Stone County Historical Society Museum grounds in Ortonville, where travelers can view the enormous tongue-in-cheek Bunyan relic and the surrounding lake country.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=101378', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Paul Bunyan''s Woodpile', 'paul-bunyan-s-woodpile', 'roadside-oddities', 39.766429, -112.115293, 'Mona', 'UT', 'Paul Bunyan’s Woodpile is a natural geologic formation of columnar volcanic rock, not a man-made Bunyan prop. The “logs” formed roughly 30 million years ago, and travelers reach them on BLM land by driving about 3.5 miles on a dirt road and then hiking roughly one mile to the formation.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/paul-bunyons-woodpile', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Paul Bunyan''s Woodpile Overlook', 'paul-bunyan-s-woodpile-overlook', 'roadside-oddities', 39.765628, -112.115667, 'Mona', 'UT', 'This viewpoint looks across the same Paul Bunyan’s Woodpile geologic formation rather than being a separate constructed attraction. The volcanic columns formed about 30 million years ago, and reaching the overlook involves the same rough BLM access road and hiking route used for the Woodpile itself.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.blm.gov/visit/paul-bunyons-woodpile', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('Paul Bunyan Statue', 'paul-bunyan-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 40.260799, -89.23153, 'Atlanta', 'IL', 'Atlanta’s giant is the famous Bunyon Giant, an original fiberglass Muffler Man installed at Bunyon’s restaurant in Cicero when it opened in 1966. After the restaurant closed, the figure was moved to Atlanta in November 2003 and dedicated there in 2004; travelers now find him standing along the town’s Route 66 corridor holding a giant hot dog.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=270597', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Paul Bunyan Tree', 'paul-bunyan-tree', 'roadside-oddities', 43.135958, -70.944342, 'Durham', 'NH', 'The Paul Bunyan Tree was a famously massive old tree in the University of New Hampshire’s College Woods, estimated to be more than two centuries old rather than something “built.” Current map data identifies the individual tree as deceased, so a traveler should not expect to find the living giant that originally earned the nickname.', 'closed', null, 'https://mapcarta.com/N2581720749', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Paulverizer — Cyborg Muffler Man', 'paulverizer-cyborg-muffler-man', 'roadside-oddities', 37.72855, -79.3581, 'Buena Vista', 'VA', 'Artist Mark Cline unveiled the 24-foot Paulverizer in 2013, transforming the familiar Muffler Man form into a giant science-fiction cyborg with a control pod and robotic details. It remains outside the Auto Recyclers property on Sycamore Avenue and can be appreciated as a roadside photo stop without interfering with the operating business.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/40615', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('PennDOT Road Sign Sculpture Garden', 'penndot-road-sign-sculpture-garden', 'roadside-oddities', 41.62086, -80.16704, 'Vernon Township', 'PA', 'A roughly quarter-mile art wall outside PennDOT''s Crawford County offices turns retired road signs into barns, animals, a Ferris wheel, a roller coaster, oil wells and other Pennsylvania scenes. It grew from a collaboration between PennDOT employees and Allegheny College artists; there is no dedicated attraction parking, so it works best as a roadside view along Smock Highway.', 'roadside', null, 'https://paroute6.com/art-culture/penndot-road-sign-sculpture-garden/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Penn''s Cave', 'penns-cave', 'roadside-oddities', 40.88256, -77.61223, 'Gregg Township', 'PA', 'Penn''s Cave is a limestone cavern explored almost entirely by boat, with tours traveling along an underground stream before emerging onto the property''s lake. The attraction operates on a seasonal schedule and also includes wildlife and farm tours above ground.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.pennscave.com/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Philadelphia''s Magic Gardens', 'philadelphias-magic-gardens', 'roadside-oddities', 39.94274, -75.15941, 'Philadelphia', 'PA', 'Artist Isaiah Zagar transformed buildings and vacant lots along South Street into a dense mosaic environment of mirrors, tiles, bottles, bicycle wheels and found objects. The nonprofit attraction preserves a multi-level indoor and outdoor labyrinth that visitors can enter with a timed ticket.', 'open', null, 'https://www.phillymagicgardens.org/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Piatt Castle Mac-A-Cheek', 'piatt-castle-mac-a-cheek', 'roadside-oddities', 40.25106, -83.72691, 'West Liberty', 'OH', 'Mac-A-Cheek is an elaborate nineteenth-century stone mansion built by the Piatt family and filled with unusual carved woodwork, painted ceilings and family collections. It survives as the publicly toured half of the Piatt Castles property, with access generally limited to seasonal scheduled hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/piatt-castles', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pioneer Mom and Daughter Roadside Statue', 'pioneer-mom-and-daughter-roadside-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 40.77563, -76.2256, 'Frackville', 'PA', 'This roughly 15-foot roadside figure of a bonneted mother holding a pie beside her daughter became a famously unsettling piece of Pennsylvania roadside kitsch outside a former motel. The attraction is now listed as permanently closed and no longer reliably accessible, but its former location is worth recording as part of the state''s roadside-history layer.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/pioneer-mom-and-daughter-roadside-statue', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Playthings Etc. Spaceship Toy Store', 'playthings-etc-spaceship-toy-store', 'roadside-oddities', 40.96719, -79.96891, 'Clay Township', 'PA', 'Playthings Etc. opened in 2005 inside a purpose-built futuristic building the business itself describes as spaceship-shaped, complete with "engine doors." More than 7,000 toys fill the interior and many are available to try, making the strange building an actual walk-in destination rather than just novelty architecture.', 'open', null, 'https://playthings-etc.com/about/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Poki, World''s Largest Desert Tortoise', 'poki-world-s-largest-desert-tortoise', 'roadside-oddities', 35.138551, -114.570245, 'Bullhead City', 'AZ', 'Poki is a roughly two-ton desert-tortoise sculpture commissioned by local resident Bill Hayes and originally displayed on his property. Hayes donated it to the community when he moved in late 2013, and it was moved to a public location in January 2014; travelers can still see Poki as a roadside photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/41526', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Phoenix'),
  ('Prabhupada''s Palace of Gold', 'prabhupadas-palace-of-gold', 'roadside-oddities', 39.96199, -80.60407, 'New Vrindaban', 'WV', 'Started in the 1970s as a residence for ISKCON founder A. C. Bhaktivedanta Swami Prabhupada, the project evolved into an ornate gold-covered palace decorated with stained glass, marble and elaborate interior work. It now operates as a public attraction within the New Vrindaban community and looks wildly out of place in rural West Virginia.', 'open', null, 'https://www.palaceofgold.com/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Pratt Rock', 'pratt-rock', 'roadside-oddities', 42.30982, -74.42314, 'Prattsville', 'NY', 'Nineteenth-century businessman and congressman Zadock Pratt commissioned enormous carvings of himself, his family and symbols of his life directly into a Catskills cliff face. The free public park requires a steep climb from the road to reach the carvings, including an unfinished chamber originally intended as Pratt''s tomb.', 'limited', null, 'https://townofprattsville.com/historic-prattsville', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Providence Home Geode Grotto', 'providence-home-geode-grotto', 'roadside-oddities', 38.3943, -86.93718, 'Jasper', 'IN', 'Beginning in the 1960s, Father Phillip Ottavi directed the creation of an enormous religious art environment using geodes, concrete, stone and imported statuary. The resulting shrines, grottoes, planters and garden structures spread across several blocks and remain free and open to the public.', 'open', null, 'https://spacesarchives.org/explore/search-the-online-collection/o1182449609/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Vincennes'),
  ('Calcite Quarry Viewpoint', 'quarry-view', 'roadside-oddities', 45.389405, -83.801163, 'Rogers City', 'MI', 'Quarry View is a public turnout overlooking the enormous active Calcite limestone quarry outside Rogers City. The quarry began operating in 1911–1912 and a formal visitor overlook was first developed in 1949; today travelers stop at the roadside viewpoint to look into the working mine rather than entering the industrial site itself.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.rogerscity.com/harbor-view.html', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Detroit'),
  ('Randyland', 'randyland', 'roadside-oddities', 40.45793, -80.00975, 'Pittsburgh', 'PA', 'Artist Randy Gilson transformed his North Side property into a brightly painted outdoor folk-art environment beginning in the 1990s. Visitors can walk through courtyards filled with murals, mannequins, mirrors, signs and repurposed objects during posted hours.', 'open', null, 'https://randy.land/', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Ringing Rocks County Park', 'ringing-rocks-county-park', 'roadside-oddities', 40.56448, -75.12997, 'Bridgeton Township', 'PA', 'This county park contains a field of unusual diabase boulders that produce bell-like metallic tones when struck, turning the rocks themselves into a natural percussion instrument. A trail from the parking area reaches the boulder field, with High Falls elsewhere in the 128-acre park; bring a small hammer if you want to test the rocks yourself.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.buckscounty.gov/Facilities/Facility/Details/Ringing-Rocks-Park-5', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roadside America Miniature Village', 'roadside-america-miniature-village', 'roadside-oddities', 40.51667, -76.11806, 'Shartlesville', 'PA', 'Roadside America was a massive hand-built miniature landscape that grew for decades into an elaborate model of small-town America filled with trains, buildings, lights and moving figures. The attraction permanently closed in 2020 and the collection was dispersed, so the former location is worth recording historically but there is nothing to enter today.', 'closed', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roadside_America', '2026-09-08T02:16:36.257931+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roanoke Bunyan Muffler Man', 'roanoke-bunyan-muffler-man', 'roadside-oddities', 37.29893, -79.94041, 'Roanoke', 'VA', 'This roughly 25-foot fiberglass Paul Bunyan figure has served as a Williamson Road landmark for decades, with local accounts placing a giant figure at the site by the mid-twentieth century. The statue has been repeatedly repainted and still stands outside the auto-service property, where it is easily visible from the public road.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/11784', '2026-09-08T04:17:48.352537+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roanoke Star', 'roanoke-star', 'roadside-oddities', 37.25083, -79.9325, 'Roanoke', 'VA', 'Built in 1949 as a temporary Christmas-season publicity stunt, the 88.5-foot neon star on Mill Mountain proved so popular that it became permanent. It remains the world''s largest freestanding illuminated man-made star and overlooks Roanoke from a public park and scenic viewpoint.', 'open', null, 'https://www.playroanoke.com/parks-facilities/mill-mountain-park/', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Roofless Church', 'roofless-church', 'roadside-oddities', 38.13138, -87.93501, 'New Harmony', 'IN', 'Architect Philip Johnson designed this open-air sacred space in 1960 around a central sculptural canopy rather than enclosing the congregation beneath a conventional roof. Its stark walls, gates and dome make it one of New Harmony''s most visually unusual structures.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-roofless-church-new-harmony-indiana', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Roscoe the Rooster Statue', 'roscoe-the-rooster-statue', 'roadside-oddities', 38.97433, -77.01216, 'Takoma Park', 'MD', 'Roscoe was a free-roaming rooster that wandered Takoma Park for roughly a decade and became so beloved that residents memorialized him after he was killed by a vehicle in 1999. A life-size bronze statue now stands along Laurel Avenue and is occasionally dressed or decorated by locals.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/roscoe-the-rooster', '2026-09-08T03:48:11.440333+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Rotting President Heads', 'rotting-president-heads', 'roadside-oddities', 37.38258, -76.75431, 'Croaker', 'VA', 'Forty-two enormous presidential busts rescued from the failed Presidents Park now decay together in a field on private industrial property near Williamsburg. The heads cannot be seen through normal walk-in access and trespassing is prohibited; visits are allowed only during occasional pre-ticketed tours and photography events.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/2502', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Saint Anne Shell Chapel', 'saint-anne-shell-chapel', 'roadside-oddities', 39.5093, -87.4579, 'Saint Mary-of-the-Woods', 'IN', 'Sisters of Providence constructed this tiny nineteenth-century chapel and covered its interior with shells, creating an unexpectedly ornate space in the Indiana woods. The historic structure has undergone preservation work, so interior access can vary and tours should be checked before visiting.', 'limited', null, 'https://spsmw.org/visit/must-sees/saint-anne-shell-chapel/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Santa Claus Post Office', 'santa-claus-post-office', 'roadside-oddities', 38.12065, -86.92477, 'Santa Claus', 'IN', 'The real U.S. Post Office in a town genuinely named Santa Claus receives huge volumes of holiday mail from people seeking the town''s distinctive postmark. Local volunteers have answered children''s Santa letters for generations, turning an otherwise ordinary federal post office into a functioning piece of Christmas folklore.', 'open', null, 'https://tools.usps.com/locations/details/1380746', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Santa''s Workshop at North Pole', 'santas-workshop-at-north-pole', 'roadside-oddities', 44.40088, -73.84889, 'Wilmington', 'NY', 'This vintage Christmas theme park opened in 1949 and helped pioneer the modern American theme-park concept with a year-round North Pole village built around Santa Claus. The park is closed for much of 2026 for improvements but has announced limited winter-season reopening dates, so verify the calendar before routing visitors here.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.northpoleny.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Schaefer''s Auto Art', 'schaefers-auto-art', 'roadside-oddities', 42.04365, -80.13418, 'Erie', 'PA', 'Richard Schaefer transformed discarded automotive parts into an outdoor collection of enormous bugs, a rocket, "Automan," and a two-headed dinosaur along Hershey Road. The installation has existed for more than 25 years and SPACES still lists it as extant; there is a small roadside pull-off, but visitors should not park in the driveway.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.spacesarchives.org/explore/search-the-online-collection/richard-schaefer/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Secret Caverns', 'secret-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 42.70934, -74.39185, 'Howes Cave', 'NY', 'Secret Caverns is a deliberately old-school show cave reached by descending 103 steps into a winding underground passage. The guided route ends at a roughly 100-foot underground waterfall, and the attraction is open daily during its 2026 season.', 'open', null, 'https://secretcaverns.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Seneca White Deer at Deer Haven Park', 'seneca-white-deer-at-deer-haven-park', 'roadside-oddities', 42.74418, -76.86922, 'Romulus', 'NY', 'The fenced former Seneca Army Depot became home to the world''s largest known herd of all-white white-tailed deer, descended from animals protected inside the military property for decades. Deer Haven Park now runs seasonal driving and bus tours through the old depot, combining the unusual herd with abandoned ammunition igloos and Cold War history.', 'limited', null, 'https://deerhavenpark.org/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Serenity Glass Park', 'serenity-glass-park', 'roadside-oddities', 41.811, -78.28001, 'Port Allegany', 'PA', 'Dedicated in 2017, this small public park uses etched glass-block towers, a glass castle and other artwork to tell Port Allegany''s glassmaking, lumber and natural-gas story. Travelers can walk through it freely at Route 6 and Mill Street.', 'open', null, 'https://visitanf.com/serenity-glass-park/', '2026-09-07T15:27:08.742137+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Seven Tubs Recreation Area', 'seven-tubs-recreation-area', 'roadside-oddities', 41.23544, -75.81026, 'Plains Township', 'PA', 'Glacial meltwater and Kitchen Creek carved a chain of smooth bowls, chutes and potholes into the bedrock here, creating the formations known as the Seven Tubs. The features are reached on foot from the public recreation-area parking lot, and wet rock around the creek can be extremely slippery.', 'limited', null, 'https://pennsylvaniastateparks.reserveamerica.com/camping/pinchot-state-forest/r/facilityDetails.do?contractCode=PA&parkId=880252', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Sherman Memorial Lighthouse', 'sherman-memorial-lighthouse', 'roadside-oddities', 41.49008, -79.45822, 'Tionesta', 'PA', 'A 75-foot lighthouse rises beside the Allegheny River in inland Forest County, far from any place where a navigation lighthouse would normally be needed. Jack Sherman built it as a family memorial and filled its seven floors with lighthouse-related exhibits; Peace Park and the exterior are freely accessible, while tower tours are offered only on selected dates.', 'limited', null, 'https://pabucketlist.com/exploring-the-sherman-memorial-lighthouse-in-forest-county/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Shoney''s Big Boy Museum', 'shoneys-big-boy-museum', 'roadside-oddities', 38.36651, -81.6663, 'Charleston', 'WV', 'At the site where Alex Schoenbaum opened the Parkette Drive-In in 1947 stands a small outdoor monument and display telling the story of the chain that became Shoney''s Big Boy. It is more roadside kiosk than full museum, but the Big Boy-topped structure and vintage display panels remain accessible from the public parking area.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/34673', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Shrine of Christ''s Passion', 'shrine-of-christs-passion', 'roadside-oddities', 41.42581, -87.47078, 'St. John', 'IN', 'This large outdoor devotional attraction uses dozens of life-size bronze sculptures to create an immersive walking route through scenes from the Passion of Christ. Regardless of religious interest, its scale and elaborate staged environments make it an unusually ambitious roadside art installation.', 'open', null, 'https://shrineofchristspassion.org/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://shrineofchristspassion.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Singer Castle', 'singer-castle', 'roadside-oddities', 44.45223, -75.81216, 'Hammond', 'NY', 'This stone castle on Dark Island was built beginning in 1902 for Frederick Gilbert Bourne, president of the Singer Sewing Machine Company. Guided seasonal tours reveal hidden passageways, concealed doors and secret observation spaces, but reaching the island requires a boat.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.singercastle.com/', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Smiley Face Water Tower', 'smiley-face-water-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 41.52581, -85.06694, 'Ashley', 'IN', 'Ashley''s municipal water tower has a giant smiling face painted across it and has become so recognizable that the town itself promotes the "Smiley Face" identity. The tower stands by Ashley Memorial Park, providing a public place to stop rather than forcing visitors to photograph it from a highway shoulder.', 'open', null, 'https://ashley.in.gov/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Smoke Hole Caverns', 'smoke-hole-caverns', 'roadside-oddities', 38.98614, -79.26592, 'Cabins', 'WV', 'These commercial caverns descend beneath the mountains of Pendleton County and feature flowstone, underground pools and other formations. Access to the cave itself is by guided tour, making it a limited stop even though the associated visitor facilities are open to the public.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.smokehole.com/contact.html', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Stone Quarry Hill Art Park', 'stone-quarry-hill-art-park', 'roadside-oddities', 42.91344, -75.83343, 'Cazenovia', 'NY', 'Large contemporary sculptures are scattered across more than 100 acres of fields, woods and trails at this outdoor art park founded in 1991. Visitors can wander the grounds from dawn to dusk and encounter the work as part of the landscape rather than inside a conventional gallery.', 'open', null, 'https://sqhap.org/visit', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Summersville Lake Lighthouse', 'summersville-lake-lighthouse', 'roadside-oddities', 38.19965, -80.86446, 'Mount Nebo', 'WV', 'Built from a recycled wind-turbine tower and dedicated in 2012, this 104-foot lighthouse is an intentionally landlocked oddity overlooking Summersville Lake. The tower can be climbed during its operating season, while off-season access may require a reservation and is weather dependent.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/summersville-lake-lighthouse', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Swannanoa Palace', 'swannanoa-palace', 'roadside-oddities', 37.9614, -78.8542, 'Afton', 'VA', 'Built beginning in 1912 as a lavish marble estate for James and Sallie Dooley, Swannanoa resembles a European palace unexpectedly planted atop Virginia''s Blue Ridge. The property is privately owned and is not a normal daily attraction, but occasional scheduled tours and open-house dates have allowed public access; do not enter outside an advertised event.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/swannanoa-palace', '2026-09-08T04:02:08.563059+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Sweeney Punch Bowl', 'sweeney-punch-bowl', 'roadside-oddities', 40.10422, -80.66643, 'Wheeling', 'WV', 'This enormous cut-glass punch bowl was produced in the 1840s and weighs roughly 225 pounds, with a height of about five feet when assembled. It spent decades associated with the Sweeney family grave before being moved to the Oglebay Glass Museum in 1949, where it can now be seen indoors.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/sweeney-punch-bowl', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Temple of Tolerance', 'temple-of-tolerance', 'roadside-oddities', 40.56866, -84.18397, 'Wapakoneta', 'OH', 'Jim Bowsher began assembling the Temple of Tolerance from enormous stones, found objects and historic artifacts in his Wapakoneta backyard in 1981. Despite looking like a private residential property from the street, the stone sanctuary is intentionally open to the public for free; visitors should use the designated entrance and stay within the areas opened for guests.', 'open', null, 'https://jimbowsher.com/visit/', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Awakening', 'the-awakening', 'roadside-oddities', 38.78512, -77.01723, 'National Harbor', 'MD', 'J. Seward Johnson Jr.''s enormous sculpture depicts a giant apparently clawing his way out of the earth, with separate head, hand, arm, knee and foot emerging from the sand. The work was moved from Washington, D.C. to National Harbor in 2008 and is freely accessible on the waterfront.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-awakening-dc', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Big Chair', 'the-big-chair', 'roadside-oddities', 35.882914, -80.082031, 'Thomasville', 'NC', 'Thomasville’s current Big Chair was erected in 1950 as a steel-and-concrete replacement for an earlier wooden giant chair built in 1922. The 30-foot landmark stands in the downtown Town Common and continues to symbolize Thomasville’s long furniture-manufacturing history.', 'roadside', null, 'https://files.nc.gov/ncdcr/nr/DV0696.pdf', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Big Duck', 'the-big-duck', 'roadside-oddities', 40.90694, -72.62306, 'Flanders', 'NY', 'Built in 1931 to sell ducks and eggs, this roughly 20-foot-tall duck-shaped building became such a famous example of novelty architecture that similar buildings are sometimes called "ducks." It is now owned by Suffolk County and operates as a visitor center and gift shop, generally open seven days a week.', 'open', null, 'https://www.suffolkcountyny.gov/Departments/Parks/Historic-Sites/The-Big-Duck', '2026-09-07T16:22:52.387536+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Big Peach', 'the-big-peach', 'roadside-oddities', 38.78835, -87.47035, 'Bruceville', 'IN', 'A giant peach rises beside this seasonal farm market in southern Indiana, a deliberately oversized symbol for a business promoting locally grown fruit. The market traditionally operates during the warmer growing season, so the sculpture is best treated as a seasonal business stop rather than guaranteed year-round access.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitindiana.in.gov/blog/post/roadside-attractions/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Vincennes'),
  ('The Broken Kilometer', 'the-broken-kilometer', 'roadside-oddities', 40.72408, -74.00211, 'New York', 'NY', 'Walter De Maria arranged 500 polished brass rods in five precisely spaced rows inside this SoHo storefront, creating a total combined length of one kilometer. The 1979 installation remains permanently maintained by Dia Art Foundation and is free to visit during posted hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.diaart.org/visit/visit-our-locations-sites/walter-de-maria-the-broken-kilometer-new-york-united-states', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Cider Barrel', 'the-cider-barrel', 'roadside-oddities', 39.19008, -77.24192, 'Germantown', 'MD', 'This barrel-shaped building is a surviving example of novelty roadside architecture from the era when businesses were designed to look like the products they sold. The former cider stand is no longer a normal walk-in attraction, but the oversized barrel remains visible from public roadside areas.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/location/md/all', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Free Stamp', 'the-free-stamp', 'roadside-oddities', 41.5055, -81.69245, 'Cleveland', 'OH', 'Claes Oldenburg and Coosje van Bruggen designed this enormous steel office stamp for Standard Oil of Ohio in the 1980s, but it spent years in storage before finally being installed in Willard Park. The sculpture measures roughly 28 feet tall and 48 feet long and spells out "FREE," making it one of downtown Cleveland''s easiest oversized-object stops.', 'open', null, 'https://clevelandhistorical.org/items/show/571', '2026-09-08T01:49:16.338406+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Lady and the Winds of Change', 'the-lady-and-the-winds-of-change', 'roadside-oddities', 38.2862, -85.7413, 'Jeffersonville', 'IN', 'In an industrial corner of Jeffersonville, a large welded-metal female figure is paired with poetry and environmental elements designed to make the piece more than a conventional statue. The unexpected placement and scale turn the installation into a particularly strange public-art stop.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-lady-and-the-winds-of-change', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('The Little Village', 'the-little-village', 'roadside-oddities', 40.19536, -78.64417, 'Pleasantville', 'PA', 'A miniature roadside settlement of tiny buildings includes a school, diner, filling station and other hand-built structures beside Route 56. The display sits on private residential property, so admire it from the public roadside and do not enter the lawn unless the owners explicitly invite visitors in.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/little-village-pennsylvania', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Mystery Hole', 'the-mystery-hole', 'roadside-oddities', 38.123751, -81.141022, 'Ansted', 'WV', 'Guided tours through a tilted building where a ball rolls uphill and standing straight feels wrong, run since 1973 beside Route 60 with a Volkswagen Beetle embedded in the wall. Fifteen or twenty minutes, seasonal hours, no cameras inside, and entirely committed to the bit.', 'limited', null, 'http://www.mysteryhole.com/', '2026-09-06T01:56:28.154232+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The New York Earth Room', 'the-new-york-earth-room', 'roadside-oddities', 40.72598, -73.99975, 'New York', 'NY', 'Walter De Maria filled a second-floor SoHo loft with roughly 250 cubic yards of earth in 1977, turning an ordinary interior into a permanent room of dark soil. Dia Art Foundation maintains the installation and allows visitors to see it for free during posted weekly hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.diaart.org/visit/visit-our-locations-sites/walter-de-maria-the-new-york-earth-room-new-york-united-states', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Only Swayzee in the World', 'the-only-swayzee-in-the-world', 'roadside-oddities', 40.5071, -85.8254, 'Swayzee', 'IN', 'Swayzee proudly advertises itself as the "Only Swayzee in the World," a slogan tied to a local story that a wartime postcard addressed only to "Swayzee" still reached its destination. The claim appears on town signage and has become the tiny community''s defining roadside identity.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.in.gov/towns/swayzee/about/', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('The Poky Dot', 'the-poky-dot', 'roadside-oddities', 39.47057, -80.155, 'Fairmont', 'WV', 'The Poky Dot was a famously colorful Fairmont diner known for enormous desserts, including a nine-pound banana split, and an interior that looked more like a carnival than a conventional restaurant. The business is now permanently closed, so this is a record of a vanished roadside institution; view the former location only from public ground and do not attempt to enter.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-poky-dot', '2026-09-08T03:30:19.766632+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Ruins at Holliday Park', 'the-ruins-at-holliday-park', 'roadside-oddities', 39.87082, -86.16339, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'Three massive stone figures from the demolished St. Paul Building in New York City were rescued and incorporated into a strange architectural installation in Holliday Park. The sculptures now rise from a deliberately ruined-looking structure that combines public art with pieces of a vanished skyscraper.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-ruins-indianapolis-indiana', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, 'https://www.hollidaypark.org/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('The Secret Chamber House of Oddities and Artwork', 'the-secret-chamber-house-of-oddities-and-artwork', 'roadside-oddities', 39.82179, -84.02197, 'Fairborn', 'OH', 'The Secret Chamber is an oddities shop and gallery packed with sideshow-style specimens, skeletons, unusual taxidermy, purported haunted objects and macabre artwork. It opened in 2017 and remains a public retail stop, making it an easy detour for travelers who want something stranger than a conventional museum.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-secret-chamber-house-of-oddities-and-artwork', '2026-09-08T01:52:19.873287+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Tepee', 'the-tepee', 'roadside-oddities', 42.80784, -74.68453, 'Cherry Valley', 'NY', 'This giant concrete-and-steel tepee has stood beside U.S. Route 20 since the 1950s as a surviving piece of classic American roadside architecture. It still operates as a gift shop and overlook, so visitors can stop rather than simply photograph it while driving past.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-tepee', '2026-09-08T02:40:05.196871+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('The Weeping Glass', 'the-weeping-glass', 'roadside-oddities', 40.42162, -79.994, 'Pittsburgh', 'PA', 'Pittsburgh''s long-running oddities shop sells and displays taxidermy, bones, funeral objects, anatomical pieces, strange artwork and other macabre curiosities. It operates as a normal storefront on East Warrington Avenue during posted weekly hours, so visitors can browse without an appointment.', 'open', null, 'https://www.visitpittsburgh.com/blog/occult-shops/', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Thorny Mountain Fire Tower', 'thorny-mountain-fire-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 38.31345, -79.94589, 'Dunmore', 'WV', 'The 65-foot Thorny Mountain Fire Tower rises above Seneca State Forest and has been converted into one of West Virginia''s strangest overnight accommodations. It can be reserved during the May–October season, with a climb to a small elevated cab and wraparound views of the forest.', 'limited', null, 'https://wvstateparks.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/07/WVSP_InspirationGuide.pdf', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Topiary Park', 'topiary-park', 'roadside-oddities', 39.96115, -82.98762, 'Columbus', 'OH', 'Topiary Park recreates Georges Seurat''s painting A Sunday Afternoon on the Island of La Grande Jatte using sculpted shrubs instead of paint. More than 50 human figures along with boats, animals and landscape forms fill the public park, which can be walked during normal park hours.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-topiary-park', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Touchdown Jesus — Word of Life Mural', 'touchdown-jesus-word-of-life-mural', 'roadside-oddities', 41.70211, -86.23448, 'Notre Dame', 'IN', 'Millard Sheets'' enormous 1964 "Word of Life" mosaic on the Hesburgh Library depicts Christ with raised arms directly beyond Notre Dame Stadium. Students quickly nicknamed it "Touchdown Jesus" because the pose resembles a referee signaling a touchdown and the mural is visible from inside the stadium.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-word-of-life-mural-at-the-university-of-notre-dame', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Tree on the Decatur County Courthouse Tower', 'tree-on-the-decatur-county-courthouse-tower', 'roadside-oddities', 39.33703, -85.48312, 'Greensburg', 'IN', 'Trees have mysteriously managed to grow from the courthouse tower high above Greensburg since the nineteenth century, with successive trees replacing earlier ones over time. The living courthouse-top tree became such a local symbol that Greensburg adopted the nickname "Tree City."', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/location/in/all', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Twisted House', 'twisted-house', 'roadside-oddities', 39.87778, -86.14379, 'Indianapolis', 'IN', 'Artist John McNaughton created this warped cedar sculpture to look like a small house twisting upward as though caught in a vortex. It stands on the grounds of the Indianapolis Art Center and can be viewed as part of the center''s outdoor sculpture environment.', 'open', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/twisted-house-sculpture', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Uniroyal Tire (World''s Largest Tire)', 'uniroyal-tire-world-s-largest-tire', 'roadside-oddities', 42.270523, -83.209012, 'Allen Park', 'MI', 'The Giant Uniroyal Tire began life as a 96-passenger Ferris wheel at the 1964–65 New York World’s Fair. It was moved to Allen Park in 1966 and converted into the stationary 80-foot tire landmark that still towers beside I-94; it is best viewed from public roads and nearby legal stopping points rather than approached directly.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.uniroyaltires.com/auto/news/giant-uniroyal-tire-reaches-60-year-milestone', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Detroit'),
  ('Uranus Fudge Factory & General Store', 'uranus-fudge-factory-general-store', 'roadside-oddities', 40.06145, -85.70098, 'Anderson', 'IN', 'Indiana''s first Uranus Fudge Factory opened in Anderson in 2022 and commits completely to its deliberately ridiculous name through signs, jokes, photo opportunities and a general store built around fudge. The active business also includes ice cream and seasonal mini golf, making it a modern roadside attraction rather than merely a novelty sign.', 'open', null, 'https://uranusindiana.com/anderson/', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, 'https://uranusindiana.com/', null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Vanadu Art House', 'vanadu-art-house', 'roadside-oddities', 38.96074, -76.95407, 'Hyattsville', 'MD', 'Artist and conservator Clarke Bedford transformed his home and vehicles into dense assemblages of metal, found objects, antlers, machine parts and architectural fragments. It is a private residence: admire it from the public street unless the owner is present and explicitly welcomes visitors onto the grounds.', 'private', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/vanadu-art-house', '2026-09-08T03:44:27.5898+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Vasehenge', 'vasehenge', 'roadside-oddities', 39.93945, -82.01552, 'Zanesville', 'OH', 'Vasehenge was a circle of enormous painted ceramic vases installed as a tribute to Zanesville''s pottery heritage. The installation has been removed and is no longer accessible, but the former location is worth recording as a closed OddWay stop rather than sending travelers there expecting the giant vases to remain.', 'closed', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/vasehenge', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Wild Geese: Flock Together', 'wild-geese-flock-together', 'roadside-oddities', 40.59749, -77.57718, 'Lewistown', 'PA', 'Five-foot fiberglass geese painted by local artists are scattered around the Juniata River Valley in honor of the region''s Goose Day tradition. This pin marks one of the public sculptures in Lewistown, and a separate tracker map can be used to hunt down the rest of the flock.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/geese-flock-together', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Williamson Coal House', 'williamson-coal-house', 'roadside-oddities', 37.67194, -82.27778, 'Williamson', 'WV', 'Built in 1933 from roughly 65 tons of local bituminous coal, this small downtown building is quite literally constructed from blocks of coal. It survived a damaging 2010 fire, was restored and now houses the Tug Valley Chamber of Commerce and visitor information center.', 'open', null, 'https://wvtourism.com/town-guide-williamson/', '2026-09-08T03:11:33.200322+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Wisteria Vine, Worlds Largest Blossoming Plant', 'wisteria-vine-worlds-largest-blossoming-plant', 'roadside-oddities', 34.170884, -118.05739, 'Sierra Madre', 'CA', 'Sierra Madre’s enormous Chinese wistaria vine began as a one-gallon plant purchased by Alice Brugman in April 1894 and eventually spread across neighboring residential properties. Because the vine grows on private homes, travelers normally see it only during the city’s annual Wistaria Festival/open-house period rather than as a daily walk-up attraction.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.sierramadreca.gov/life-wellness/library/sierra-madre-historical-archives/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Woodward Cave', 'woodward-cave', 'roadside-oddities', 40.88944, -77.38819, 'Haines Township', 'PA', 'Woodward Cave contains large limestone rooms, active cave formations and the roughly 14-foot Tower of Babel, described as Pennsylvania''s largest known free-standing stalagmite. Guided tours operate seasonally, and visitors cannot enter the cave outside the attraction''s tour schedule.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/woodward-cave', '2026-09-08T02:24:39.058393+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Worden''s Ledges', 'wordens-ledges', 'roadside-oddities', 41.20362, -81.71882, 'Hinckley Township', 'OH', 'Hidden among sandstone ledges in Hinckley Reservation are faces, animals, religious imagery and other figures carved into the rock by Noble Stuart in the mid-twentieth century. The carvings are reached on a short wooded trail, so this is a hike rather than a roadside pull-off.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/wordens-ledges', '2026-09-08T02:02:43.398883+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Biggest Frying Pan', 'world-s-biggest-frying-pan', 'roadside-oddities', 46.349034, -124.054282, 'Long Beach', 'WA', 'Long Beach’s giant frying pan was commissioned by the local chamber of commerce and forged in 1941 for the town’s Razor Clam Festival. It has since been surpassed by larger pans elsewhere, but the 14-foot-long landmark remains a free downtown roadside photo stop and one of the classic oddities of the Washington coast.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/2972', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Nome Giant Gold Pan', 'world-s-biggest-gold-pan', 'roadside-oddities', 64.500439, -165.408315, 'Nome', 'AK', 'Nome’s giant metal gold pan is roughly 20 feet across and stands with the Three Lucky Swedes statues as a tribute to the 1898 gold discovery that launched the Nome Gold Rush. The exact installation year is not well documented in current sources; today it is a free outdoor photo stop at Bering Street and Seppala Road, and Visit Nome describes it as the largest metal gold pan in the United States.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.visitnomealaska.com/summer', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Nome'),
  ('Casey Big Pencil', 'world-s-biggest-pencil', 'roadside-oddities', 39.299277, -87.993148, 'Casey', 'IL', 'Casey’s Big Pencil is a deliberately oversized teacher-style pencil created as part of the town’s Big Things Small Town project. The city explicitly says it is often mistaken for the world’s largest but is only a supersized replica, and visitors can see it free at 8 West Main Street along with Casey’s cluster of giant objects.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.bigthingssmalltown.com/yardstick-pencil', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Casey Big Yardstick', 'world-s-biggest-yard-stick', 'roadside-oddities', 39.299351, -87.992062, 'Casey', 'IL', 'Casey’s Big Yardstick is a 36-foot-long yardstick with every inch enlarged to a foot, built as part of Jim Bolin’s town-wide Big Things project. It is not presented by Casey as a current Guinness record holder, but it remains a free outdoor stop at 3 East Main Street within walking distance of the town’s other oversized objects.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.bigthingssmalltown.com/yardstick-pencil', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Amish Chair', 'world-s-largest-amish-chair', 'roadside-oddities', 34.843965, -83.935105, 'Blairsville', 'GA', 'This oversized Amish-style chair was built in March 2013 outside Owltown Market south of Blairsville. It remains a free roadside photo stop beside the market, although visitors are asked not to climb or sit on the chair.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/38152', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Apple', 'world-s-largest-apple', 'roadside-oddities', 39.186615, -78.166452, 'Winchester', 'VA', 'Winchester’s giant red apple began as a parade float for the Shenandoah Apple Blossom Festival before being permanently placed on the lawn of the historic Sheridan’s Headquarters property. The exact fabrication year is not clearly documented in current sources, but the apple has become a longstanding symbol of the region’s orchard industry and remains visible from the downtown street.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/4032', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Apple Basket', 'world-s-largest-apple-basket', 'roadside-oddities', 40.1355, -82.083138, 'Frazeysburg', 'OH', 'Longaberger built this huge apple-filled basket at its Homestead property in 1999 as another supersized expression of the company’s basket-making identity. The commercial village later closed and the property became restricted; the basket was repainted in 2022 and is still visible, but travelers should remain on public/access roads and respect barriers and no-trespassing signs.', 'private', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/2586', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Ball of Sisal Twine', 'world-s-largest-ball-of-sisal-twine', 'roadside-oddities', 39.509227, -98.433692, 'Cawker City', 'KS', 'This community-grown ball is in Cawker City, not Osborne. Farmer Frank Stoeber began rolling discarded sisal twine into a ball on Christmas Eve 1953, and the town later took over the tradition; visitors now find it beneath a roadside shelter and the community continues adding twine during special events.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.cawkercitykansas.com/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Ball of Twine Made By One Man', 'world-s-largest-ball-of-twine-made-by-one-man', 'roadside-oddities', 45.096339, -94.410164, 'Darwin', 'MN', 'This famous ball is in Darwin, not Dassel. Francis A. Johnson wound sisal twine continuously from 1950 until 1979, creating a 17,400-pound ball later protected inside a glass gazebo; travelers can see it from outside at any time and visit the adjacent museum when it is open.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.darwintwineball.com/twineball.html', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Basket', 'world-s-largest-basket', 'roadside-oddities', 40.12397, -82.012013, 'Dresden', 'OH', 'Dresden’s giant Longaberger Market Basket was built from hardwood maple and dedicated in 1980. Measuring 48 feet long, 11 feet wide and 23 feet high, it still stands at Fifth and Main streets as a free downtown photo stop tied to the town’s basket-making history.', 'roadside', null, 'https://destinationdresden.com/worlds-largest-basket/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Bowie Knife', 'world-s-largest-bowie-knife', 'roadside-oddities', 33.547184, -97.832162, 'Bowie', 'TX', 'Bowie’s enormous steel knife was created as a civic landmark and earned Guinness recognition in April 2016. The 20-foot sculpture remains at the south entrance to town as a free roadside photo stop celebrating both the city name and the famous Bowie knife.', 'roadside', null, 'https://cityofbowietx.com/384/Worlds-Largest-Bowie-Knife', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Buffalo', 'world-s-largest-buffalo', 'roadside-oddities', 46.889295, -98.698575, 'Jamestown', 'ND', 'Jamestown’s 26-foot, 60-ton concrete buffalo was created by sculptor Elmer Petersen in 1959 and received the name Dakota Thunder in a public contest in 2010. It still overlooks the Frontier Village and is open year-round as a free-will-donation public attraction.', 'roadside', null, 'https://discoverjamestownnd.com/fun-things-to-do-in-jamestown-nd/all-things-buffalo/worlds-largest-buffalo-monument/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Bullhead', 'world-s-largest-bullhead', 'roadside-oddities', 43.225496, -93.790098, 'Crystal Lake', 'IA', 'The giant bullhead is actually in Crystal Lake, Iowa, not Forest City. Carl Frick and Rush Gabrilson built the 12-foot fish in 1958, and it was restored in 2007; today it sits by Crystal Lake as a free lakeside photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/4339', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Catsup Bottle', 'world-s-largest-catsup-bottle', 'roadside-oddities', 38.662906, -89.982241, 'Collinsville', 'IL', 'Collinsville’s 170-foot Brooks catsup-bottle water tower was built in 1949 by Caldwell Tanks for the G.S. Suppiger catsup plant. Saved from demolition and restored by a community preservation campaign in 1995, it remains beside Route 159 as one of America’s best-known roadside landmarks and can be photographed from nearby public areas.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.catsupbottle.com/index.html', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Cherry Pie - Pan', 'world-s-largest-cherry-pie-pan', 'roadside-oddities', 44.736254, -85.625162, 'Traverse City', 'MI', 'Traverse City’s giant pie pan is the surviving hardware from the city’s July 25, 1987 attempt to bake the world’s largest cherry pie, which weighed more than 28,000 pounds. The pan remains outdoors as a roadside monument to the event, giving travelers a quick photo stop tied directly to northern Michigan’s cherry industry.', 'roadside', null, 'https://sanweb.lib.msu.edu/DMC/MFN/1987/1987-10.pdf', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Detroit'),
  ('World''s Largest Chest of Drawers', 'world-s-largest-chest-of-drawers', 'roadside-oddities', 35.96358, -80.008257, 'High Point', 'NC', 'High Point’s oversized furniture landmark began in 1926 as a giant “Bureau of Information” promoting the city’s furniture industry. It was completely redesigned in 1996 into the present 38-foot chest of drawers with giant socks hanging out, and travelers can still view and photograph the exterior from the surrounding streets.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/2148', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Chile Pepper', 'world-s-largest-chile-pepper', 'roadside-oddities', 32.311858, -106.807619, 'Las Cruces', 'NM', 'Las Cruces’ giant concrete chile pepper was built in 2010–2011 by the owners of the Big Chile Inn as a deliberately oversized symbol of southern New Mexico’s chile culture. The 47-foot sculpture remains outside the motel property and is an easy roadside photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://lascrucesdirectory.com/places/worlds-largest-chili-pepper', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('World''s Largest Christmas Pickle', 'world-s-largest-christmas-pickle', 'roadside-oddities', 35.312973, -94.332372, 'Barling', 'AR', 'This giant Christmas pickle began life as an oversized Chili’s pepper before artist Eric Brown repainted and repurposed it as a pickle wearing a Santa hat. The current artwork was in place by 2021 and stands outdoors along Wells Lake Road near Barling/Fort Smith as a quick roadside photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/78502', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Collection of the World''s Smallest Versions of the World''s Largest Things', 'world-s-largest-collection-of-the-world-s-smallest-versions-of-the-world-s-large', 'roadside-oddities', 39.057611, -98.537771, 'Lucas', 'KS', 'Artist Erika Nelson created this deliberately tongue-twisting collection of miniature replicas of famous giant roadside attractions, turning the idea of “world’s largest” inside out. The collection now has a home at the Roadside Sideshow Expo in Lucas, where travelers can self-tour during the April-through-October season and see tiny versions of oversized American landmarks.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.travelks.com/listing/worlds-largest-collection-of-the-worlds-smallest-versions-of-the-worlds-largest-things-roadside-attraction-%26-museum/1709/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Corn Cob', 'world-s-largest-corn-cob', 'roadside-oddities', 44.776084, -95.005925, 'Olivia', 'MN', 'Olivia’s 25-foot fiberglass corn cob stands in Memorial Park as a playful symbol of the community’s official “Corn Capital of the World” identity. The exact installation year is not clearly documented in current reliable sources, but the cob remains an easy public park photo stop along Highway 212.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/best-roadside-attractions-in-minnesota-part-2/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s largest covered wagon', 'world-s-largest-covered-wagon', 'roadside-oddities', 40.148572, -89.387311, 'Lincoln', 'IL', 'Lincoln’s Railsplitter Covered Wagon was built by David Bentley and donated to the city in January 2007. The 25-foot-tall, 40-foot-long wagon carries an oversized seated Abraham Lincoln and remains a free Route 66 photo stop; its canvas cover is removed during winter and returned in spring.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.lincolnil.gov/lincoln-route-66', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('The Giant Justins', 'world-s-largest-cowboy-boots', 'roadside-oddities', 29.519994, -98.493982, 'San Antonio', 'TX', 'These are Bob “Daddy-O” Wade’s “The Giant Justins,” created in 1979 for the Washington Project for the Arts. The 40-foot boots moved permanently to North Star Mall in San Antonio in 1980, where they remain an easy exterior photo stop and one of the city’s best-known pieces of oversized public art.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.northstarmall.com/en/events/39974/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Cuckoo Clock', 'world-s-largest-cuckoo-clock', 'roadside-oddities', 40.503106, -81.640582, 'Sugarcreek', 'OH', 'This giant animated clock was built in 1972 for the Alpine-Alpa restaurant near Wilmot and later donated to Sugarcreek. It was moved and restored downtown in 2012, where travelers can still watch its cuckoo bird, mechanical band and dancing figures perform on a regular schedule.', 'roadside', null, 'https://visitsugarcreek.com/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Czech Egg', 'world-s-largest-czech-egg', 'roadside-oddities', 38.824102, -98.472706, 'Wilson', 'KS', 'The giant Czech egg is in Wilson, Kansas, not Ellsworth. The project began around 2003, the fiberglass egg arrived in 2012, local artist Christine Slechta and community volunteers painted it over the following years, and it was formally dedicated July 29, 2016; travelers now find the 20-foot hand-painted egg in Shiroky Park.', 'roadside', null, 'https://wilsonkschamber.com/worlds-largest-czech-egg/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Drumsticks', 'world-s-largest-drumsticks', 'roadside-oddities', 41.235693, -80.818786, 'Warren', 'OH', 'Warren’s giant drumsticks were carved from two roughly 23-foot poplar logs by local artist Joel Eggert and installed as part of Dave Grohl Alley in 2013. They remain outdoors with murals and other Grohl-themed artwork celebrating the Foo Fighters frontman’s Warren birthplace.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/32170', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Easel', 'world-s-largest-easel', 'roadside-oddities', 39.338009, -101.7049, 'Goodland', 'KS', 'Goodland’s giant easel is part of artist Cameron Cross’s international Van Gogh Project and carries a 24-by-32-foot reproduction of Van Gogh’s “Three Sunflowers in a Vase.” It was installed in Pioneer Park on June 19, 2001 and remains a free roadside artwork visible from Business Highway 24.', 'roadside', null, 'https://goodlandks.gov/news/high-plains-museum-news/goodlands-treasures/2011/10/art-in-a-big-way-goodlands-big-easel/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('World''s Largest Egg', 'world-s-largest-egg', 'roadside-oddities', 46.493327, -122.937891, 'Winlock', 'WA', 'Winlock’s giant egg tradition began in 1923 when the first oversized egg was built for a parade celebrating the Pacific Highway bridge and the local poultry industry. Several replacements followed as earlier versions deteriorated, and today a later fiberglass incarnation stands in Vern Zander Memorial Park as the town’s signature roadside landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Winlock_Egg', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('World''s Largest Egg', 'world-s-largest-egg-mentone', 'roadside-oddities', 41.1734, -86.0349, 'Mentone', 'IN', 'Mentone''s approximately ten-to-twelve-foot concrete egg was built in 1946 to advertise the community''s egg industry and festival. It still stands downtown emblazoned with "The Egg Basket of the Midwest," preserving a wonderfully literal piece of small-town promotional history.', 'open', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/471', '2026-09-08T13:20:58.818667+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('World''s Largest Fork', 'world-s-largest-fork', 'roadside-oddities', 37.145369, -93.323274, 'Springfield', 'MO', 'The giant fork is in Springfield, not Battlefield. Noble & Associates created the 35-foot, roughly 11-ton stainless-steel fork in 1990 for a restaurant, and after the restaurant closed it was moved to its current office-property setting at 2215 W. Chesterfield Street; visitors can pull in for a quick photo.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.springfieldmo.org/blog/post/visit-these-fun-quirky-locations-around-springfield/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Crabbie, the World''s Largest Horseshoe Crab', 'world-s-largest-horseshoe-crab', 'roadside-oddities', 31.36, -87.06, 'Lenox', 'AL', 'A sixty-seven foot fibreglass horseshoe crab, hollow enough to stand inside, built in the 1990s for a maritime attraction in Baltimore''s Inner Harbor that closed before it opened. It has moved four times since: to a creationist museum in Kentucky, then a church car park in Blanchester, Ohio, then a private lawn near Hillsboro, and since roughly 2021 to a private attraction north of Lenox in Conecuh County, Alabama. Our coordinates are approximate — placed from directions rather than a survey — and the site is private, so check before turning up.', 'private', null, 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World%27s_Largest_Horseshoe_Crab', '2026-09-07T01:44:25.054929+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Kaatskill Kaleidoscope', 'world-s-largest-kaleidoscope', 'roadside-oddities', 42.049237, -74.286949, 'Mount Tremper', 'NY', 'The Kaatskill Kaleidoscope is a roughly 60-foot silo converted into an immersive walk-in kaleidoscope at the Emerson Resort in Mount Tremper, not Shokan proper. It opened in 1996, and visitors today buy admission to stand inside while projected imagery and sound transform the silo interior.', 'limited', null, 'https://emersonresort.com/worlds-largest-kaleidoscope/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Former World''s Largest Knitting Needles', 'world-s-largest-knitting-needles', 'roadside-oddities', 39.299502, -87.992594, 'Casey', 'IL', 'Casey’s giant knitting needles were created by Jim Bolin and officially held the world-record title from 2013 to 2017. They are 13.75 feet long and are now presented as the former world’s largest, displayed with the town’s giant crochet hook at 2 East Main Street.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.bigthingssmalltown.com/knitting-needles-and-crocket-hook', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Lobster Trap', 'world-s-largest-lobster-trap', 'roadside-oddities', 44.648972, -67.708151, 'Addison', 'ME', 'This enormous lobster trap is a roadside-scale tribute to Maine’s lobster industry in the Addison area. I could not find a reliable published construction year or maker for this specific installation, so the safest description is an oversized local photo stop rather than attaching an unsupported record history to it.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.openstreetmap.org/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Mineral Hot Spring', 'world-s-largest-mineral-hot-spring', 'roadside-oddities', 43.65636, -108.197973, 'Thermopolis', 'WY', 'The Big Spring at Hot Springs State Park is a natural geothermal feature rather than something built, with hot mineral water feeding the terraces and bathhouse system at Thermopolis. An 1897 agreement reserved part of the spring water for free public bathing, and travelers today can view the spring from boardwalks and use the park’s free bathhouse during posted hours.', 'roadside', null, 'https://npgallery.nps.gov/GetAsset/0c2763ad-9455-4707-9804-b3b07b7587c9', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Denver'),
  ('World''s Largest Mosquito', 'world-s-largest-mosquito', 'roadside-oddities', 63.341491, -143.078154, 'Tok', 'AK', 'This oversized metal mosquito is part of the deliberately odd collection around Mukluk Land outside Tok, a seasonal roadside attraction and museum filled with unusual exhibits and games. The exact construction year of the mosquito is not well documented, but the sculpture is still mapped beside Mukluk Land; visitors should expect the surrounding attraction itself to keep limited seasonal hours.', 'limited', null, 'https://muklukland.com/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Anchorage'),
  ('World''s Largest Olive', 'world-s-largest-olive', 'roadside-oddities', 36.204887, -119.105308, 'Lindsay', 'CA', 'Lindsay’s giant concrete black olive originally stood at the local olive-packing cooperative, reflecting the town’s history as a major olive-processing center. After the plant closed it was rescued and moved to the former Olive Tree Inn around 1999–2000, and today travelers find it in the parking lot of the property now operated as a Super 8.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/4022', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('World''s Largest Oyster', 'world-s-largest-oyster', 'roadside-oddities', 46.666338, -123.810894, 'South Bend', 'WA', 'South Bend’s giant oyster is a concrete shell monument celebrating the Willapa Bay oyster industry and sits in Robert Bush Memorial Park. The exact installation year is not well documented in reliable current sources, but travelers today can walk up to the oversized shell in the public riverfront park.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/the-world-s-largest-oyster', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('World''s Largest "Paper" Cup', 'world-s-largest-paper-cup', 'roadside-oddities', 34.006539, -117.339255, 'Riverside', 'CA', 'Riverside’s giant concrete cup was built as advertising for the paper-cup factory that operated here under Lily-Tulip and later Sweetheart Cup; the adjacent plant produced cups from 1958 to 1997. The exact construction year of the monument is poorly documented, but the cup still stands behind a fence at the former industrial site and is best treated as a roadside photo stop.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/203', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Durant Giant Peanut', 'world-s-largest-peanut', 'roadside-oddities', 33.992736, -96.378405, 'Durant', 'OK', 'Durant’s molded-aluminum peanut monument was dedicated on November 15, 1974 to Bryan County’s peanut growers and processors. Although larger peanut sculptures now exist elsewhere, the original local claim remains on the monument, which sits on the City Hall lawn and is viewable 24 hours a day.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.travelok.com/listings/view.profile/id.22732', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Peanut Monument', 'world-s-largest-peanut-monument', 'roadside-oddities', 31.706373, -83.635334, 'Ashburn', 'GA', 'Ashburn’s giant peanut monument was originally erected in 1975 to celebrate the local peanut-processing industry. Hurricane Michael destroyed the earlier peanut in 2018, and a new steel-supported monument was completed in 2023 after a community fundraising effort; travelers now see the rebuilt peanut as a roadside landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.worldrecordacademy.org/2023/9/worlds-largest-peanut-monument-world-record-in-ashburn-georgia-423347', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('Seguin Giant Pecan', 'world-s-largest-pecan', 'roadside-oddities', 29.628837, -97.969628, 'Seguin', 'TX', 'The giant pecan associated with this record is at the Texas Agricultural Education & Heritage Center in Seguin, not Geronimo. Seguin unveiled the 16-foot-long fiberglass pecan in 2011 to regain a “world’s largest” title, although a still larger Texas pecan surpassed it in 2025; travelers can see the monument on the Big Red Barn grounds during public access.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/33385', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Penny', 'world-s-largest-penny', 'roadside-oddities', 45.895118, -89.700177, 'Woodruff', 'WI', 'Woodruff’s giant concrete penny commemorates the 1953 “Million Penny Parade,” when local schoolchildren and supporters collected more than a million cents to help fund a hospital. The monument was dedicated May 29, 1954 and remains beside the road as a permanent tribute to the campaign.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/2255', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Pheasant', 'world-s-largest-pheasant', 'roadside-oddities', 44.370001, -98.200075, 'Huron', 'SD', 'Huron’s enormous pheasant was built in 1959 as a tribute to South Dakota’s celebrated pheasant-hunting culture. The roughly 28-foot-tall bird still stands beside U.S. Highway 14 on the east side of town, where travelers can pull off for photos.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/3320', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Kriz Farm Horseshoe Pile', 'world-s-largest-pile-of-horseshoes', 'roadside-oddities', 41.399241, -73.042863, 'Bethany', 'CT', 'The Kriz family’s enormous horseshoe pile is the accumulation of generations of farrier work, with the current pile begun after a 1955 flood washed away an earlier collection. It was moved to the Kriz Farm in Bethany in 1978 and continues to grow, but it is on a working private farm rather than a public roadside attraction, so visitors should not enter without permission.', 'private', null, 'https://www.farmshow.com/a_article.php?aid=22639', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Popcorn Ball', 'world-s-largest-popcorn-ball', 'roadside-oddities', 42.422549, -94.99997, 'Sac City', 'IA', 'Sac City’s current popcorn ball was built by community volunteers in 2016 and weighs 9,370 pounds, replacing earlier record attempts by the town. It is protected inside its own transparent display building near the Sac City Museum Village, allowing travelers to see the giant snack even when the museum itself is closed.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.traveliowa.com/places/sac-city-museum-village-and-world-s-largest-popcorn-ball/51/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Potato Masher', 'world-s-largest-potato-masher', 'roadside-oddities', 44.444892, -89.521939, 'Plover', 'WI', 'Plover installed its nearly 39-foot, roughly three-ton potato masher on May 19, 2023 outside the Food + Farm Exploration Center. The giant utensil was designed specifically as a selfie landmark celebrating central Wisconsin agriculture, and travelers can photograph the exterior sculpture even if they are not touring the center.', 'roadside', null, 'https://spmetrowire.com/potd-the-worlds-largest-potato-masher/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Route 66 Red Rocker', 'world-s-largest-rocker', 'roadside-oddities', 38.037444, -91.469595, 'Cuba', 'MO', 'This 42-foot steel chair was erected at Fanning on April 1, 2008 and once held the Guinness title for the world’s largest rocking chair. Casey, Illinois later surpassed it, and it was repainted red and renamed the Route 66 Rocker; travelers still find it beside old Route 66 west of Cuba as a free roadside landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.visitmo.com/things-to-do/route-66-red-rocker', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Rocking Chair', 'world-s-largest-rocking-chair-franklin', 'roadside-oddities', 39.41789, -85.99979, 'Franklin', 'IN', 'A gigantic wooden rocking chair survives outside a furniture business along US 31. An equally oversized chest of drawers once accompanied it but was destroyed in a fire, leaving the giant chair as the property''s solitary oversized landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://fotospot.com/attractions/indiana/worlds-largest-rocking-chair', '2026-09-08T13:34:34.826362+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('World''s Largest Round Barn', 'world-s-largest-round-barn', 'roadside-oddities', 44.652396, -90.174269, 'Marshfield', 'WI', 'Marshfield’s enormous round barn was built in 1916 to house purebred livestock and measures about 150 feet across and 70 feet high. It still serves its original agricultural purpose during the Central Wisconsin State Fair, while interior tours outside events require advance arrangement with the fair office.', 'limited', null, 'https://visitmarshfield.com/business/worlds-largest-round-barn/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Sandhill Crane', 'world-s-largest-sandhill-crane', 'roadside-oddities', 46.861697, -99.913138, 'Steele', 'ND', '“Sandy,” Steele’s 40-foot metal sandhill crane, was built in 1998–99 by self-taught ironworker James Miller. The bird stands in a landscaped area just off I-94 and remains an easy roadside stop celebrating the large crane migrations through central North Dakota.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/tip/1834', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Six-Pack', 'world-s-largest-six-pack', 'roadside-oddities', 43.802842, -91.253231, 'La Crosse', 'WI', 'La Crosse’s “six-pack” is actually six 54-foot beer storage tanks built by G. Heileman Brewing Company in 1969 and painted as giant Old Style cans in 1970. The working brewery tanks have changed branding several times and returned to Old Style imagery in 2023; travelers view them from the surrounding public streets rather than touring the industrial tanks themselves.', 'roadside', null, 'https://wi101.wisc.edu/object-history-worlds-largest-six-pack/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('Quinault Big Sitka Spruce', 'world-s-largest-spruce', 'roadside-oddities', 47.477977, -123.829595, 'Quinault', 'WA', 'This is the Quinault Big Sitka Spruce near Lake Quinault, not in Hoquiam itself. The natural tree is roughly 191 feet tall with a circumference approaching 59 feet and is estimated to be around a thousand years old; travelers reach it on a short trail managed from the Rain Forest Resort Village area.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.nps.gov/places/000/quinault-big-sitka-spruce-tree.htm', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('World''s Largest Spur', 'world-s-largest-spur', 'roadside-oddities', 31.051275, -98.182169, 'Lampasas', 'TX', 'Lampasas’ giant spur was forged by ironsmith Waylon Dobbs for local businesswoman Leah Caruthers and installed on March 14, 2016. The roughly 35-foot steel, copper and iron sculpture earned Guinness recognition and remains visible from U.S. 281 with parking available for photos.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.lampasas.org/m/newsflash/home/detail/432', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Strawberry', 'world-s-largest-strawberry', 'roadside-oddities', 42.682731, -91.534686, 'Strawberry Point', 'IA', 'Strawberry Point’s 15-foot fiberglass strawberry was dedicated in the late 1960s and has stood outside City Hall for more than half a century. Restored again in 2025, it remains an easy public photo stop and one of the town’s defining landmarks.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/4035', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s largest surfboard', 'world-s-largest-surfboard', 'roadside-oddities', 33.65928, -118.000959, 'Huntington Beach', 'CA', 'Huntington Beach’s enormous surfboard was built for the Epic Big Board Ride on June 20, 2015, when 66 people successfully rode it and Guinness certified it as the world’s largest surfboard. The 42-foot board was subsequently placed on display at the International Surfing Museum, so visitors see it as part of the museum rather than as a freestanding roadside object.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.guinnessworldrecords.com/news/2015/6/worlds-largest-surfboard-66-catch-a-wave-and-ride-their-way-to-a-record-video-386094', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('World''s Largest Sweet Tea', 'world-s-largest-sweet-tea', 'roadside-oddities', 33.01869, -80.176746, 'Summerville', 'SC', 'Summerville created a giant batch of sweet tea on June 10, 2016, filling a custom oversized Mason jar with more than 2,500 gallons to set a Guinness record. The permanent jar remains near Town Hall as a roadside monument to the record attempt and the town’s claim as the birthplace of sweet tea.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.visitsummerville.com/sweet-tea/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Teapot', 'world-s-largest-teapot', 'roadside-oddities', 40.616118, -80.557208, 'Chester', 'WV', 'Chester’s giant teapot began as an oversized Hires Root Beer keg before William “Babe” Devon bought it in 1938, added a handle, spout and lid, and turned it into a teapot-shaped concession stand promoting the region’s pottery industry. Restored and relocated over the years, it now stands on a landscaped roadside site as one of West Virginia’s classic oversized attractions.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/11259', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Largest Teeter-Totter', 'world-s-largest-teeter-totter', 'roadside-oddities', 39.299713, -87.990597, 'Casey', 'IL', 'Casey’s enormous teeter-totter is another piece of the Big Things Small Town project, built as a functioning oversized playground object and certified as a world-record attraction. It is visible outdoors for free beside Casey’s other giants, while opportunities to actually ride it are restricted to scheduled dates during the tourism season.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.bigthingssmalltown.com/list', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Tiger Muskie', 'world-s-largest-tiger-muskie', 'roadside-oddities', 46.964471, -94.842047, 'Nevis', 'MN', 'The giant tiger muskie is actually in Nevis, just east of Park Rapids. The community erected the fish in 1949 as a tourism symbol for its lake country, and today the oversized muskie remains a public landmark near the center of town and the Heartland Trail.', 'roadside', null, 'https://cityofnevismn.gov/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Turkey', 'world-s-largest-turkey', 'roadside-oddities', 46.72275, -95.710257, 'Frazee', 'MN', 'Frazee’s current giant turkey, Big Tom II, was installed on September 19, 1998 after the original statue accidentally burned while workers were removing it. The fiberglass bird stands more than 20 feet tall in Lions Park and remains a free roadside photo stop overlooking the entrance to town.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.roadsideamerica.com/story/2130', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Largest Windchime', 'world-s-largest-windchime', 'roadside-oddities', 39.299581, -87.991057, 'Casey', 'IL', 'Casey’s first major world-record project was the giant wind chime, whose steel framework went up November 17, 2011 and whose chimes were installed on December 15 that year. The 54-foot structure still stands downtown and visitors can pull the rope to make the huge chimes sound.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.bigthingssmalltown.com/wind-chime', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Smallest City Block', 'world-s-smallest-city-block', 'roadside-oddities', 31.225372, -85.38923, 'Dothan', 'AL', 'Dothan’s tiny triangular block sits at the meeting of North Appletree, North College and East Troy streets. The Camellia Garden Club marked it on May 1, 1964 after Ripley’s recognition, and travelers today find a tiny traffic island with street signs and a granite marker that can be viewed from the surrounding public streets.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.atlasobscura.com/places/worlds-smallest-city-block', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago'),
  ('World''s Tallest Filing Cabinet', 'world-s-tallest-filing-cabinet', 'roadside-oddities', 44.455837, -73.217221, 'Burlington', 'VT', 'Burlington artist Bren Alvarez created “File Under So. Co., Waiting for…” in 2002 from stacked filing cabinets as a joke about decades of paperwork surrounding the long-delayed Southern Connector highway. The sculpture was moved and revised in 2020 and now stands at an art park outside 208 Flynn Avenue, where visitors can view it freely from the public-facing site.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.burlingtoncityarts.org/so-co-file-under', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/New_York'),
  ('World''s Tallest Free Standing Redwood Chainsaw Carving', 'world-s-tallest-free-standing-redwood-chainsaw-carving', 'roadside-oddities', 39.919097, -123.764318, 'Piercy', 'CA', 'This approximately 44-foot carving was cut upright from a dead redwood at Confusion Hill, making it a freestanding chainsaw carving rather than a totem carved horizontally and raised later. Confusion Hill says the carving itself took about three months to make; its exact year is not well documented, and travelers now find it in the attraction’s parking area at Piercy.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.confusionhill.com/faqs', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Jackson Creek Giant Sugar Pine', 'world-s-tallest-sugarpine', 'roadside-oddities', 42.961233, -122.703101, 'Shady Cove', 'OR', 'This is a natural giant sugar pine in the southern Oregon forest rather than a man-made attraction, so there is no construction date; the famous tree is several centuries old. The Jackson Creek-area specimen long carried a “world’s tallest” reputation but newer measurements have identified taller living sugar pines elsewhere, and reaching this one requires forest roads and a woodland approach rather than a simple highway pull-off.', 'limited', null, 'https://conifers.org/pi/Pinus_lambertiana.php', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('World''s Tallest Thermometer', 'world-s-tallest-thermometer', 'roadside-oddities', 35.266485, -116.072778, 'Baker', 'CA', 'Baker’s 134-foot electric thermometer was created by businessman Willis Herron to commemorate the 134°F temperature recorded in nearby Death Valley. The first version was built in 1991 but toppled in high winds before opening, and the rebuilt structure was illuminated in October 1992; it remains a prominent I-15 roadside landmark.', 'roadside', null, 'https://www.pbssocal.org/history-society/return-of-the-desert-wayfinder-worlds-tallest-thermometer-in-baker-ca', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Los_Angeles'),
  ('Worlds Largest Ball Of Paint', 'worlds-largest-ball-of-paint', 'roadside-oddities', 40.258859, -85.709091, 'Alexandria', 'IN', 'Mike Carmichael began the Ball of Paint on January 1, 1977 by repeatedly coating a baseball, eventually turning it into a multiton object with tens of thousands of paint layers. The Alexandria attraction is still an active family project, and visitors who arrange a visit can add their own coat of paint and receive a certificate.', 'limited', null, 'https://www.worldslargestballofpaint.com/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Indiana/Indianapolis'),
  ('Giant Joe Tinker Baseball', 'worlds-largest-baseball', 'roadside-oddities', 39.551224, -95.521726, 'Muscotah', 'KS', 'The giant baseball is in Muscotah, not Horton, and was created from a large former water tank as a tribute to Hall of Fame shortstop and Muscotah native Joe Tinker. The local baseball-themed project developed in the 2010s; today the oversized stitched ball sits as a public roadside monument, although the “world’s largest” claim is local rather than a well-documented current record.', 'roadside', null, 'https://ksbaseballhof.com/tinker-joe/', '2026-09-06T21:21:44.179039+00:00', null, null, null, null, null, 'America/Chicago')
